helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Positioning Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147828				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>objects;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>positioning;objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>anchors;options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>centering;images on HTML pages\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147828	45			0	lt	\<variable id=\"anchor_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/anchor_object.xhp\" name=\"Positioning Objects\"\>Positioning Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3147251	46			0	lt	You can use anchors to position an object, graphic, or frame in a document. An anchored item remains in place, or moves when you modify the document. The following anchoring options are available:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145599	47			0	lt	Anchoring				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145622	48			0	lt	Effect				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145650	49			0	lt	As character				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151181	50			0	lt	Anchors the selected item as a character in the current text. If the height of the selected item is greater than the current font size, the height of the line containing the item is increased.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	lt	To center an image on an HTML page, insert the image, anchor it "as character", then center the paragraph.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212	51			0	lt	To character				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151235	52			0	lt	Anchors the selected item to a character.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155071	53			0	lt	To paragraph				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155094	54			0	lt	Anchors the selected item to the current paragraph.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155122	55			0	lt	To page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155144	56			0	lt	Anchors the selected item to the current page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674	57			0	lt	To frame				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145697	58			0	lt	Anchors the selected item to the surrounding frame.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145715	59			0	lt	When you insert an object, graphic, or frame, an anchor icon appears where the item is anchored. You can position an anchored item by dragging the item to another location. To change the anchoring options of an item, right-click the item, and then choose an option from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Anchor\</item\>         \<emph/\>submenu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Rearranging a Document by Using the Navigator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149973				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>headings;rearranging\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rearranging headings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>moving;headings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>demoting heading levels\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>promoting heading levels\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Navigator;heading levels and chapters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>arranging;headings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>outlines;arranging chapters\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149973	58			0	lt	\<variable id=\"arrange_chapters\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/arrange_chapters.xhp\" name=\"Rearranging a Document by Using the Navigator\"\>Arranging Chapters in the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147795	59			0	lt	You can move headings and subordinate text up and down in a document text by using the Navigator. You can also promote and demote heading levels. To use this feature, format the headings in your document with one of the predefined heading paragraph styles. To use a custom paragraph style for a heading, choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>, select the style in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style \</emph\>box, and then double-click a number in the \<emph\>Levels \</emph\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145652	62			0	lt	To quickly move the text cursor to a heading in the document, double-click the heading in the \<emph\>Navigator \</emph\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155461	60			0	lt	To dock the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>, drag the title bar to the edge of the workspace. To undock the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>, double-click its frame.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151184	70			0	lt	To Move a Heading Up or Down in the Document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id0915200809400790				0	lt	Ensure that all heading levels are shown in the Navigator. By default all levels are shown. See steps below how to change the heading levels that are shown.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151206	71			0	lt	On the \<emph\>Standard Bar\</emph\>, click the\<emph\> Navigator\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id5211883\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_navigator.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5211883\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151238	72			0	lt	On the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Content View \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id3156338\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20244.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156338\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155089	74			0	lt	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	63			0	lt	Drag a heading to a new location in the \<emph\>Navigator \</emph\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155139	75			0	lt	Click a heading in the \<emph\>Navigator \</emph\>list, and then click the \<emph\>Promote Chapter\</emph\>\<image id=\"img_id4217546\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20174.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4217546\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or \<emph\>Demote Chapter \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id6505788\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20171.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6505788\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145758	64			0	lt	To move the heading without the subordinate text, hold down Ctrl while you drag or click the \<emph\>Promote Chapter \</emph\>or \<emph\>Demote Chapter \</emph\>icons.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155402	76			0	lt	To Promote or Demote the Level of a Heading				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155424	77			0	lt	Select the heading in the \<emph\>Navigator \</emph\>list. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081C				0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Promote Level \</emph\>\<image id=\"img_id5564488\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20172.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5564488\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or \<emph\>Demote Level \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id3159363\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20173.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159363\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155525	78			0	lt	To Change the Number of Heading Levels That Are Displayed				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151352	79			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Heading Levels Shown \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id3151310\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20236.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151310\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>, and then select a number from the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147407				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; lists, while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;creating while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;automatic numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers;lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic bullets/numbers; AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullets; using automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; automatic numbering\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147407	26			0	lt	\<variable id=\"auto_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type\"\>Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155525	16			0	lt	$[officename] can automatically apply numbering or bullets as you type.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154243	28			0	lt	To Enable Automatic Numbering and Bulleting				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152830	29			0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab, and then select “Apply numbering – symbol”.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152867	30			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect\</emph\>, and ensure that \<emph\>While Typing\</emph\> is selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id2357860				0	lt	The automatic numbering option is only applied to paragraphs that are formatted with the "Default", "Text body", or "Text body indent" paragraph style.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152897	21			0	lt	To Create a Numbered or Bulleted List While You Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773	22			0	lt	Type 1., i., or I. to start a numbered list. Type * or - to start a bulleted list. You can also type a right parenthesis after the number instead of a period , for example, 1) or i).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147794	23			0	lt	Enter a space, type your text, and then press Enter. The new paragraph automatically receives the next number or bullet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147814	31			0	lt	Press Enter again to finish the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287	25			0	lt	You can start a numbered list with any number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3154083	27			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Numbering/Bullets\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Turning Off AutoCorrect 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154250				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>turning off automatic correction\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text;turning off automatic correction\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>uppercase;changing to lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;changing to small letters after periods\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>quotation marks;changing automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>words;automatic replacement on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines;automatic drawing on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>underlining;quick\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders; automatic drawing on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic changes on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changes;automatic\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;turning off\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147812	16			0	lt	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Turning Off AutoFormat and AutoCorrect\"\>Turning Off AutoCorrect\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147833	2			0	lt	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081B				0	lt	To quickly undo an automatic correction or completion, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_idN10846				0	lt	To turn off most AutoCorrect features, remove the check mark from the menu \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect - While Typing\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147251	12			0	lt	To Remove a Word from the AutoCorrect List				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147274	14			0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596	23			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145620	15			0	lt	In the \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\> list, select the word pair that you want to remove.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145645	24			0	lt	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145668	4			0	lt	To Stop Replacing Quotation Marks				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3151196	6			0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3151220	7			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Localized Options\</emph\> tab				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245	25			0	lt	Clear the "Replace" check box(es).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155076	8			0	lt	To Stop Capitalizing the First Letter of a Sentence				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155099	10			0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools – AutoCorrect Options\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155123	11			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155148	26			0	lt	Clear the "Capitalize first letter of every sentence" check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155401	17			0	lt	To Stop Drawing a Line When You Type Three Identical Characters				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155415	22			0	lt	$[officename] automatically draws a line when you type three of the following characters and press Enter: - _ = * ~ #				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155439	19			0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155463	20			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155488	27			0	lt	Clear the "Apply border" check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Automatically Check Spelling				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154265				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck;AutoSpellcheck on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>checking spelling;while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>words;disabling spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154265	31			0	lt	\<variable id=\"auto_spellcheck\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_spellcheck.xhp\" name=\"Automatically Check Spelling\"\>Automatically Check Spelling\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3154664	5			0	lt	You can have $[officename] automatically check spelling while you type and underline possible misspelt words with a red wavy line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154678	41			0	lt	To Check Spelling Automatically While You Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531	42			0	lt	Activate the \<emph\>AutoSpellcheck \</emph\>icon on the Standard bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3155569	33			0	lt	Right-click a word with a red wavy underline, and then choose a suggested replacement word from the list, or from the \<emph\>AutoCorrect \</emph\>submenu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759	6			0	lt	If you choose a word from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>AutoCorrect\</item\> submenu, the underlined word and the replacement word are automatically added to the AutoCorrect list for the current language. To view the AutoCorrect list, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools – AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace\</item\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147819	7			0	lt	You can also add the underlined word to your custom dictionary by choosing \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147220	32			0	lt	To Exclude Words From the Spellcheck				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147263	35			0	lt	Select the words that you want to exclude.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147282	36			0	lt	Click the Language control on the Status bar to open a menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3145602	38			0	lt	Choose “None (Do not check spelling)”.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3145648	40			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Creating a new dictionary.\"\>Creating a new dictionary.\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
