helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152887				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; adding exceptions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exceptions; AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>abbreviations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;avoiding after specific abbreviations\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152887	10			0	lt	\<variable id=\"autocorr_except\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autocorr_except.xhp\" name=\"Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List\"\>Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3154254	11			0	lt	You can prevent AutoCorrect from correcting specific abbreviations or words that have mixed capital letters and lowercase letters. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3155576	13			0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Exceptions\</item\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147762	18			0	lt	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147786	19			0	lt	Type the abbreviation followed by a period in the \<emph\>Abbreviations (no subsequent capital) \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812	20			0	lt	Type the word in the \<emph\>Words with TWo INitial CApitals \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3144875	17			0	lt	To quickly undo an AutoCorrect replacement, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. This also adds the word or abbreviation that you typed to the AutoCorrect exceptions list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Using AutoText				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155521				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>AutoText\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>networks and AutoText directories\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;AutoText shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;AutoText shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text blocks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text blocks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>blocks of text\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155521	26			0	lt	\<variable id=\"autotext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autotext.xhp\" name=\"Using AutoText\"\>Using AutoText\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534	27			0	lt	In $[officename] Writer, you can store text - also containing graphics, tables, and fields - as AutoText, so that you can quickly insert the text later on. If you want, you can also store formatted text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155539	48			0	lt	To To Create an AutoText Entry				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155560	47			0	lt	Select the text, text with graphics, table, or field that you want to save as an AutoText entry. A graphic can only be stored if it is anchored as a character and is preceded and followed by at least one text character.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155581	57			0	lt	Choose\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - AutoText\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147761	58			0	lt	Select the category where you want to store the AutoText.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147779	59			0	lt	Type a name that is longer than four characters. This allows you to use the \<emph\>Display remainder of name as suggestion while typing\</emph\> AutoText option. If you want, you can modify the proposed shortcut.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147807	60			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>AutoText\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_idN10732				0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147282	39			0	lt	To Insert an AutoText Entry				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145597	61			0	lt	Click in your document where you want to insert an AutoText entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615	28			0	lt	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - AutoText\"\>\<emph\>Edit - AutoText\</emph\>\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145644	38			0	lt	Select the AutoText that you want to insert, and then click\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145668	30			0	lt	You can also type the shortcut for an AutoText entry, and then press F3, or click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>AutoText\</item\>         \<emph/\>icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> bar, and then choose an AutoText entry. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155090	43			0	lt	To quickly enter a %PRODUCTNAME Math formula, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>fn\</item\>, and then press F3. If you insert more than one formula, the formulae are sequentially numbered. To insert dummy text, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>dt\</item\>, and then press F3. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155115	45			0	lt	To Print a List of AutoText Entries				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136	44			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155160	62			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> list, double-click "%PRODUCTNAME Macros - Gimmicks".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277	63			0	lt	Select "AutoText" and then click \<emph\>Run\</emph\>. A list of the current AutoText entries is generated in a separate text document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151304	64			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151327	49			0	lt	Using AutoText in Network Installations				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151355	50			0	lt	You can store AutoText entries in different directories on a network.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370	51			0	lt	For example, you can store "read-only" AutoText entries for your company on a central server, and user-defined AutoText entries in a local directory.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390	52			0	lt	The paths for the AutoText directories can be edited in the configuration.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154960	53			0	lt	Two directories are listed here. The first entry is on the server installation and the second entry is in the user directory. If there are two AutoText entries with the same name in both directories, the entry from the user directory is used.				20130618 17:22:18
