helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2316660				0	lt	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5908688				0	lt	Examples				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5118564				0	lt	Select a single cell in a Writer table, then choose \<emph\>Table - Table properties - Borders\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id244758				0	lt	Select a thick line style.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7741325				0	lt	To set a lower border, click the lower edge repeatedly until you see a thick line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id542313				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id4273506\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4273506\"\>setting thick lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2210760				0	lt	All cells in a Writer table have at least a left and a lower line by default. Most cells on the table perimeter have more lines applied by default. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5400860				0	lt	All lines that are shown in white in the preview will be removed from the cell.				20130618 17:22:18
