helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409	2			0	lt	An input field is a variable that you can click in a document to open a dialog where you can edit the variable.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145776	3			0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>               \<emph/\>and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620	5			0	lt	Click “Input field”\<emph/\>in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154257	6			0	lt	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>               \<emph/\>and type the text for the variable.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155888	7			0	lt	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150708	4			0	lt	To quickly open all input fields in a document for editing, press Ctrl+Shift+F9.				20130618 17:22:18
