helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3153167	101			0	lt	If you want, you can use a condition to hide specific text in your document from a specific user.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190	102			0	lt	Select the text in the document that you want to hide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273	103			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3145297	104			0	lt	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533	105			0	lt	In the \<emph\>With Condition\</emph\> box, type \<emph\>user_lastname == "Doe"\</emph\>, where "Doe" is the last name of the user that you want to hide the text from. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3155573	107			0	lt	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then save the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3147760	108			0	lt	The name of the hidden section can still be seen in the Navigator.				20130618 17:22:18
