helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Finding and Replacing in Writer				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id1163670				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>finding; text/text formats/styles/objects\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>replacing; text and text formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>styles;finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>text formats; finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>formats; finding and replacing\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching; formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>objects;finding by Navigator\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Asian languages;search options\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8568681				0	lt	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Writer\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id611285				0	lt	In text documents you can find words, formatting, styles, and more. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all results at once, then apply another format or replace the words by other text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id6226081				0	lt	The Find & Replace dialog				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6702780				0	lt	To find text within the whole document, open the Find & Replace dialog without any active text selection. If you want to search only a part of your document, first select that part of text, then open the Find & Replace dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158970				0	lt	To Find Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6957304				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2164677				0	lt	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5684072				0	lt	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4377269				0	lt	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Writer will show you the next text that is equal to your entry. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found text. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1371807				0	lt	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (Ctrl+Shift+F) to find the next text without opening the dialog. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id924100				0	lt	Alternatively, you can use the icons at the lower right of the document to navigate to the next text or to any other object in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9359416				0	lt	When you click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find All\</item\>, Writer selects all text that is equal to your entry. Now you can for example set all found text to bold, or apply a character style to all at once.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id5891598				0	lt	To Replace Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1780755				0	lt	Unlike searching text, replacing text cannot be restricted to the current selection only.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2467421				0	lt	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4286935				0	lt	Enter the text to search in the \<emph\>Search for \</emph\>text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9959410				0	lt	Enter the text to replace the found text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id24109				0	lt	Either click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> or \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id703451				0	lt	When you click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>, Writer will search the whole document for the text in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, starting at the current cursor position. When text is found, Writer highlights the text and waits for your response. Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> to replace the highlighted text in the document with the text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box. Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> to advance to the next found text without replacing the current selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7540818				0	lt	When you click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>, Writer replaces all text that matches your entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id9908444				0	lt	To Find Styles				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8413953				0	lt	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain Paragraph Style is assigned, for example the "Heading 2" style.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2696920				0	lt	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id896938				0	lt	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9147007				0	lt	Check \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for Styles\</item\>.\<br/\>The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> text box now is a list box, where you can select any of the Paragraph Styles that are applied in the current document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id679342				0	lt	Select the style to search for, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3231299				0	lt	To Find Formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8087405				0	lt	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain direct character formatting is assigned. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3406170				0	lt	Finding formats only finds direct character attributes, it does not find attributes applied as part of a style.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2448805				0	lt	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4542985				0	lt	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4679403				0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7783745				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5597094				0	lt	More options				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9919431				0	lt	The similarity search can find text that is almost the same as your search text. You can set the number of characters that are allowed to differ.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8533280				0	lt	Check the \<emph\>Similarity search\</emph\> option and optionally click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to change the settings. (Setting all three numbers to 1 works fine for English text.)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4646748				0	lt	When you have enabled Asian language support under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>, the Find & Replace dialog offers options to search Asian text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2489394				0	lt	The Navigator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9934385				0	lt	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects. You can also use the Navigator to move and arrange chapters, providing an outline view to your document. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4159062				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7421796				0	lt	Use the Navigator for inserting objects, links and references within the same document or from other open documents. See the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/navigator.xhp\"\>Navigator\</link\> guide for more information.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6417432				0	lt	Click the icon with the blue circle at the bottom right part of your document to open the small \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4639728				0	lt	Use the small Navigation window to quickly jump to the next object or find the next text in your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Inserting Page Numbers of Continuation Pages				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145819				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>pages; continuation pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>next page number in footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>continuation pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page numbers; continuation pages\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145819	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"footer_nextpage\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footer_nextpage.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Page Numbers of Continuation Pages\"\>Inserting Page Numbers of Continuation Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154242	12			0	lt	You can easily insert the page number of the next page in a footer by using a field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256	4			0	lt	The page number is only displayed if the following page exists.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886	5			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\> and select the page style that you want to add the footer to.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147109	6			0	lt	Place the cursor in the footer and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147134	7			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>Document\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150955	8			0	lt	Click 'Page' in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list and 'Next page' in the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517	9			0	lt	Click a numbering style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
