helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F6				0	lt	\<variable id=\"print_brochure\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/print_brochure.xhp\"\>Printing a Brochure\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	lt	You can print a Writer document as a brochure or a booklet. That is, Writer prints two pages on each side of the paper, so that when you fold the paper, you can read the document as a book.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DE				0	lt	When you create a document that you want to print as a brochure, use portrait orientation for the pages. Writer applies the brochure layout when you print the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	lt	To Print a Brochure				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10621				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B6				0	lt	In the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070E				0	lt	In the properties dialog for your printer, set the paper orientation to landscape.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_id8947416				0	lt	If your printer prints duplex, and because brochures always print in landscape mode, you should use the "duplex - short edge" setting in your printer setup dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10628				0	lt	Return to \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog, and click the \<emph\>Page Layout\</emph\> tab page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1062C				0	lt	Select \<emph\>Brochure\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10740				0	lt	For a printer that automatically prints on both sides of a page, specify to include "All pages".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10630				0	lt	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EA				0	lt	If %PRODUCTNAME prints the pages in the wrong order, open the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, select \<emph\>Print in reverse page order\</emph\>, and then print the document again.				20130618 17:22:18
