helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10652				0	lt	\<variable id=\"registertrue\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/registertrue.xhp\"\>Printing Register-true\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065E				0	lt	To Set a Document to Register-True Printing				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10665				0	lt	Select the whole document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10669				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page - Page\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	lt	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Register-true\</item\> checkbox and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10678				0	lt	All the paragraphs in the document will be printed register-true, unless otherwise specified.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	lt	To Exempt Paragraphs From Register-True Printing				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	lt	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10685				0	lt	Select all the paragraphs you want to exempt, then choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068C				0	lt	Open the Styles and Formatting window, click the Paragraph Style you want to exempt, right-click that style, choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Indents & Spacing\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10698				0	lt	Clear the \<emph\>Register-true\</emph\> checkbox.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030100.xhp\"\>Register-true\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Removing Line Breaks				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149687				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>hard returns in pasted text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>line breaks;removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting; line breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copies;removing line breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph marks;removing\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"removing_line_breaks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/removing_line_breaks.xhp\"\>Removing Line Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858	2			0	lt	Use the AutoCorrect feature to remove line breaks that occur within sentences. Unwanted line breaks can occur when you copy text from another source and paste it into a text document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153413	3			0	lt	This AutoCorrect feature only works on text that is formatted with the "Default" paragraph style. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138	5			0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>               \<emph\>.\</emph\>            				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645	6			0	lt	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, ensure that \<emph\>Combine single line paragraphs if length greater than 50%\</emph\> is selected. To change the minimum percentage for the line length, double-click the option in the list, and then enter a new percentage.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145093	12			0	lt	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118	7			0	lt	Select the text containing the line breaks that you want to remove.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156253	8			0	lt	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Apply Style\</item\> box on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar, choose “Default”.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153388	9			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect - Apply\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Resetting Font Attributes				20130618 17:22:18
