helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695	16			0	lt	\<variable id=\"section_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/section_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Sections\"\>Inserting Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917	26			0	lt	You can insert new sections, or links to sections in other documents into the current document. If you insert a section as a link, the content of the link changes when you modify the source document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863	27			0	lt	To Insert a New Section				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843	23			0	lt	Click in your document where you want to insert a new section, or select the text that you want to convert to a section.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156103	28			0	lt	If you select a text that occurs within a paragraph, the text is automatically converted into a new paragraph.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281	24			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404	29			0	lt	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Section\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, type a name for the section.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127	25			0	lt	Set the options for the section, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149635	30			0	lt	To Insert a Section as a Link				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149648	31			0	lt	Before you can insert a section as link, you must first create sections in the source document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611	18			0	lt	When you open a document that contains linked sections, $[officename] prompts you to update the contents of the sections. To manually update a link, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Links\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149860	22			0	lt	You can also insert linked sections in HTML documents. When you view the page in a web browser, the content of the sections corresponds to the content of the sections at the time the HTML document was last saved.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145104	32			0	lt	Click in your document where you want to insert the linked section.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241	33			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363	34			0	lt	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Section\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, type a name for the section.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387	35			0	lt	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\>               \<emph/\>check box. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>Under Windows, you can also select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>DDE\</item\> check box to automatically update the contents of the section when the section in the source document is changed. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154852	36			0	lt	Click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File name\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155882	37			0	lt	Locate the document containing the section that you want to link to, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149978	38			0	lt	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Section\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the section that you want to insert.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150003	39			0	lt	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Using Sections				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149832				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>multi-column text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; multi-column\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; on text pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections; columns in/use of\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832	40			0	lt	\<variable id=\"sections\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/sections.xhp\" name=\"Using Sections\"\>Using Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128	2			0	lt	Sections are named blocks of text, including graphics or objects, that you can use in a number of ways:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149284	5			0	lt	To prevent text from being edited.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149630	4			0	lt	To show or hide text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149647	20			0	lt	To reuse text and graphics from other $[officename] documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612	38			0	lt	To insert sections of text that uses a different column layout than the current page style.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149855	7			0	lt	A section contains at least one paragraph. When you select a text and create a section, a paragraph break is automatically inserted at the end of the text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872	8			0	lt	You can insert sections from a text document, or an entire text document as a section into another text document. You can also insert sections from a text document as links in another text document, or in the same document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153367	39			0	lt	To insert a new paragraph immediately before or after a section, click in front or behind the section, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242	44			0	lt	Sections and Columns				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255	41			0	lt	You can insert sections into an existing section. For example, you can insert a section containing two columns into a section that contains one column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154845	42			0	lt	A section layout, for example on the number of columns, has priority over the page layout defined in a page style.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3155883				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Saving Text Documents in HTML Format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>text documents; publishing in HTML\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; creating from text documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>homepage creation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>saving;in HTML format\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"send2html\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/send2html.xhp\" name=\"Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\"\>Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149825	2			0	lt	You can save a $[officename] Writer document in HTML format, so that you can view it in a web browser. If you want, you can associate a page break with a specific heading paragraph style to generate a separate HTML page each time the style appears in the document. $[officename] Writer automatically creates a page containing hyperlinks to each of these pages.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922	3			0	lt	When you save a text document in HTML format, any graphics in the document are saved in JPEG format. The name of the HTML document is added as a prefix to the name of the graphic file. The JPEG images are saved in the same folder as the HTML document and are referenced with <IMG> tags in the HTML code.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155868	5			0	lt	Apply one of the default $[officename] heading paragraph styles, for example, "Heading 1", to the paragraphs where you want to generate a new HTML page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3156100	6			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create HTML Document\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281	7			0	lt	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the paragraph style that you want to use to generate a new HTML page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3153407	9			0	lt	Enter a path and a name for the HTML document, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Applying Text Formatting While You Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149689				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>text; formatting bold while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; bold, while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keyboard;bold formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bold;formatting while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys;bold formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
