helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153396	15			0	lt	\<variable id=\"templates_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/templates_styles.xhp\" name=\"Templates and Styles\"\>Templates and Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635	2			0	lt	A template is a document that contains specific formatting styles, graphics, tables, objects, and other information. A template is used as the basis for creating other documents. For example, you can define paragraph and character styles in a document, save the document as a template, and then use the template to create a new document with the same styles.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149957	18			0	lt	Unless you specify otherwise, every new $[officename] text document is based on the default template.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149974	3			0	lt	$[officename] has a number of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"predefined templates\"\>predefined templates\</link\> that you can use to create different types or text documents, such as business letters.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149613	4			0	lt	Viewing and Organizing Styles in Templates				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	lt	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Template Management\"\>Template Management\</link\> dialog to copy styles from one document to another.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153377	7			0	lt	To copy a style, drag it to another template or document.				20130618 17:22:18
