helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916	2			0	lt	You can change the case of text, format text with small capitals, or capitalize the first letter of each word in a selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	lt	When you apply a formatting to your text by \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, the text stays the same, it is only displayed in another way. On the other hand, when you choose \<emph\>Format - Change Case\</emph\>, the text is permanently changed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155861	8			0	lt	To Capitalize Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3147420	9			0	lt	Select the text that you want to capitalize.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841	10			0	lt	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485778				0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Uppercase\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485775				0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select the type of capitalization in the Effects box. "Capitals" capitalizes all letters. "Title" capitalizes the first letter of each word. "Small capitals" capitalizes all letters, but in a reduced font size.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149644	11			0	lt	To Change Text to Lowercase				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149964	12			0	lt	Select the text that you want to change to lowercase.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149606	13			0	lt	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id112020091049000				0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Lowercase\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910490034				0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select "Lowercase" in the Effects box.				20130618 17:22:18
