helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487	3			0	lt	\<variable id=\"text_frame\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_frame.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\"\>Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842	65			0	lt	A text frame is a container for text and graphics that you can place anywhere on a page. You can also use a frame to apply a column layout to text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156104	64			0	lt	To Insert a Text Frame				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961	5			0	lt	Select the text that you want to include in the frame.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149602	9			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>, and click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145115	66			0	lt	To Edit a Text Frame				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	16			0	lt	To edit the contents of a text frame, click in the frame, and make the changes that you want.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156239	14			0	lt	To edit a frame, select the frame, right-click, and then choose a formatting option. You can also right-click the selected frame, and choose \<emph\>Frame\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261	63			0	lt	To resize a text frame, click an edge of the frame, and drag one of the edges or corners of the frame. Hold down Shift while you drag to maintain the proportion of the frame.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153386	98			0	lt	To Hide Text From Printing				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262	99			0	lt	Any Writer text frame can be set to a mode which allows viewing the text on screen, but hides the text from printing.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154858	100			0	lt	Select the text frame (you see the eight handles).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155875	101			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Frame/Object - Options\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155899	102			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, unmark the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
