helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695	20			0	lt	\<variable id=\"using_hyphen\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_hyphen.xhp\" name=\"Hyphenation\"\>Hyphenation\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918	31			0	lt	By default, $[officename] moves words that do not fit on a line to the next line. If you want, you can use automatic or manual hyphenation to avoid this behavior: 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155864	30			0	lt	Automatic Hyphenation				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147414	22			0	lt	Automatic hyphenation inserts hyphens where they are needed in a paragraph. This option is only available for paragraph styles and individual paragraphs.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832	51			0	lt	To Automatically Hyphenate Text in a Paragraph				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148850	32			0	lt	Right-click in a paragraph, and choose \<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156104	34			0	lt	Click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>\<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3150101	35			0	lt	In the Hyphenation area, select the Automatically check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153121	52			0	lt	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
