helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help					0	lt	To Manually Hyphenate Single Words				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363	24			0	lt	To quickly insert a hyphen, click in the word where you want to add the hyphen, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Hyphen(-).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154244	37			0	lt	If you insert a manual hyphen in a word, the word is only hyphenated at the manual hyphen. No additional automatic hyphenation is applied for this word. A word with a manual hyphen will be hyphenated without regard to the settings on the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab page.				20130618 17:22:18
