helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150017	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090001.xhp\" name=\"Document\"\>Document\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147167	2			0	lt	Fields are used to insert information about the current document, for example, file name, template, statistics, user data, date, and time.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154470	3			0	lt	For the HTML export and import of date and time fields, \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090007.xhp#datumuhrzeit\" name=\"special $[officename] formats\"\>special $[officename] formats\</link\> are used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151312	4			0	lt	Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153672	5			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKTYPE\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the \<emph\>Select \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> The following fields are available:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182	6			0	lt	Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3143272	7			0	lt	Meaning				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248	10			0	lt	Author				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148975	11			0	lt	Inserts the name of the current user. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145759	18			0	lt	Chapter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149172	19			0	lt	Inserts the chapter number and/or the chapter name.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145771	14			0	lt	Date				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370	15			0	lt	Inserts the current date. You can insert the date as a fixed field - \<item type=\"literal\"\>Date (fixed)\</item\> - that does not change, or as a dynamic field - \<item type=\"literal\"\>Date\</item\> - that it is updated automatically. To manually update the \<item type=\"literal\"\>Date\</item\> field, press F9.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150699	12			0	lt	File name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150122	13			0	lt	Inserts the filename and/or the directory path of the current document, as well as the filename without extension.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147495	20			0	lt	Page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145264	21			0	lt	Inserts the page number of the current, previous, or next page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150561	8			0	lt	Sender				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146341	9			0	lt	Inserts fields containing user data. You can change the user-data that is displayed by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010100.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - User Data\"\>$[officename] - User Data\</link\>\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148863	22			0	lt	Statistics				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151091	23			0	lt	Inserts document statistics, such as page and word counts, as a field. To view the statistics of a document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Statistics\</emph\> tab.               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153302	16			0	lt	Templates				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156123	17			0	lt	Inserts the filename, the path, or the filename without the file extension of the current template. You can also insert the names of the "Category" and the "Style" formats used in the current template. To view the names of the template categories and the styles used in the templates, choose \<emph\>File - Templates -\</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Organize\"\>\<emph\>Organize\</emph\>\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146939	24			0	lt	Time				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154340	25			0	lt	Inserts the current time. You can insert the time as a fixed field - \<item type=\"literal\"\>Time (fixed)\</item\> - that does not change, or as a dynamic field - \<item type=\"literal\"\>Time\</item\> - that it is updated automatically. To manually update the \<item type=\"literal\"\>Time\</item\> field, press F9.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154631	26			0	lt	The following fields can only be inserted if the corresponding field type is selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150660	27			0	lt	Select				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150678	28			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKSELECTION\"\>Lists the available fields for the field type selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list. To insert a field, click the field, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155537	53			0	lt	To quickly insert a field from the list, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and double-click the field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155359	30			0	lt	Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154220	31			0	lt	Function				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145107	32			0	lt	Previous page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149595	33			0	lt	Inserts the page number of the previous page in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146896	34			0	lt	Next page 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148923	35			0	lt	Inserts the page number of the next page in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	36			0	lt	Page Number 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159212	37			0	lt	Inserts the current page number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159229	38			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, click the numbering format that you want to use.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145188	39			0	lt	If you want, you can enter an \<emph\>Offset \</emph\>for the displayed page number. With an \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> value of 1, the field will display a number that is 1 more than the current page number, but only if a page with that number exists. On the last page of the document, this same field will be empty.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150891	45			0	lt	Offset				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155312	46			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DOK:ED_DOKVALUE\"\>Enter the offset value that you want to apply to a page number field, for example "+1".\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154948	54			0	lt	If you want to change the actual page number and not the displayed number, do not use the \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> value. To change page numbers, read the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>\<emph\>Page Numbers\</emph\>\</link\> guide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145595	41			0	lt	Format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145613	42			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKFORMAT\"\>Click the format that you want to apply to the selected field, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150138	49			0	lt	\<variable id=\"datumuhrzeitformat\"\>When you click "Additional formats", the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Number Format\"\>\<emph\>Number Format\</emph\>\</link\> dialog opens, where you can define a custom format. \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154867	50			0	lt	If you choose "Chapter number without separator" for a chapter field, the separators that are specified for chapter number in \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06060000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Outline numbering\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Outline numbering\</emph\>\</link\> are not displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156079	63			0	lt	If you choose "chapter number" as the \<emph\>format\</emph\> for reference fields, only the number of the chapter heading containing the referenced object is displayed in the field. If the paragraph style for the chapter heading is not numbered, the field is left blank.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148682	56			0	lt	The following number range formats are for paragraphs formatted with numbered or bulleted lists:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150006	57			0	lt	Category and number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155386	58			0	lt	The format contains everything between the beginning of the paragraph and directly after the number-range field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146919	59			0	lt	Caption text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155929	60			0	lt	The format contains the text following the number-range field up to the end of the paragraph				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148733	61			0	lt	Number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148755	62			0	lt	The format only contains the reference number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id0902200804313432				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts the field as static content, that is, the field cannot be updated.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153026	43			0	lt	Layer				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154580	44			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:TP_FLD_DOK:ED_DOKLEVEL\"\>Select the chapter heading level that you want to include in the selected field.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154598	51			0	lt	Offset in days/minutes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154899	52			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:TP_FLD_DOK:ED_DOKDATEOFF\"\>Enter the offset that you want to apply to a date or time field.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154922	47			0	lt	Value				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049	48			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:TP_FLD_DOK:ED_DOKDATEOFF\"\>Enter the contents that you want to add to a user-defined field.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Cross-references				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153641	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"Cross-references\"\>Cross-references\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"reftext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>This is where you insert the references or referenced fields into the current document. References are referenced fields within the same document or within sub-documents of a master document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159197	19			0	lt	The advantage of entering a cross-reference as a field is that you do not have to adjust the references manually every time you change the document. Just update the fields with F9 and the references in the document are updated too.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id4333628				0	lt	Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id4516129				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the Selection list, and then click Insert.\</ahelp\> The following fields are available:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3151380	3			0	lt	Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700	4			0	lt	Meaning				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862	5			0	lt	Set Reference				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147422	6			0	lt	Set target for a referenced field. Under \<emph\>Name\</emph\>, enter a name for the reference. When inserting the reference, the name will then appear as an identification in the list box \<emph\>Selection\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149556	7			0	lt	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For the target in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04040000.xhp\" name=\"insert a bookmark\"\>insert a bookmark\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150548	8			0	lt	Insert Reference				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147746	9			0	lt	Inserting a reference to another position in the document. The corresponding text position has to be defined with "Set Reference" first. Otherwise, inserting a reference by choosing a field name under \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not possible.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146344	16			0	lt	In master documents, you can also reference from one sub-document to another. Note that the reference name will not appear in the selection field and has to be entered "by hand".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149847	10			0	lt	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For referenced fields in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020400.xhp\" name=\"insert a hyperlink\"\>insert a hyperlink\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id2408825				0	lt	Headings				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id9988402				0	lt	The Selection box shows a list of all headings in the order of their appearance in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6401257				0	lt	Numbered Paragraphs				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5841242				0	lt	The Selection box shows a list of all numbered headings and numbered paragraphs in the order of their appearance in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id306711				0	lt	Bookmarks				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150907	11			0	lt	After inserting a bookmark in the document with \<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>, the bookmarks entry on the \<emph\>References\</emph\> tab becomes usable. Bookmarks are used to mark certain text passages in a document. In a text document, you can use the bookmarks, for example, to jump from one passage in the document to another.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155080	12			0	lt	In an HTML document, these bookmarks become anchors <A name>, which determine the target of hyperlinks for example.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0818200811011072				0	lt	Footnotes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0818200811011049				0	lt	If your documents contains a footnote, you can select the Footnotes entry. A reference to a footnote returns the footnote number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6794030				0	lt	(Inserted objects with captions)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7096774				0	lt	You can set references to objects that have captions applied. For example, insert a picture, right-click the picture, choose Caption. Now the object shows up as a numbered "Illustration" in the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154772	18			0	lt	References are fields. To remove a reference, delete the field. If you set a longer text as a reference and you do not want to reenter it after deleting the reference, select the text and copy it to the clipboard. You can then reinsert it as "unformatted text" at the same position using the command \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>. The text remains intact while the reference is deleted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id5824152				0	lt	Selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7374187				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKSELECTION\"\>Lists the available fields for the field type selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list. To insert a field, click the field, select a format in the "Insert reference to" list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7729728				0	lt	To quickly insert a field from the list, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and double-click the field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id2171086				0	lt	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, click the format that you want to use.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154333	21			0	lt	Insert reference to				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148786	22			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_REF:LB_REFFORMAT\"\>Select the format that you want to use for the selected reference field.\</ahelp\> The following formats are available:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7576525				0	lt	Format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id641193				0	lt	Meaning				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150039	23			0	lt	Page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153134	24			0	lt	Inserts the number of the page containing the reference target.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150681	27			0	lt	Reference				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154040	28			0	lt	Inserts the complete reference target text. For footnotes the footnote number is inserted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972	29			0	lt	Above/Below				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149619	30			0	lt	Inserts "above" or "below", depending on the location of the reference target relative to the position of the reference field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148705	31			0	lt	As Page Style				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728	32			0	lt	Inserts the number of the page containing the reference target using the format specified in the page style.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5699942				0	lt	Number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6420484				0	lt	Inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph, including superior levels depending on the context. See note below this table for more information.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6986602				0	lt	Number (no context)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id616779				0	lt	Inserts only the number of the heading or numbered paragraph.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id791039				0	lt	Number (full context)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id1953489				0	lt	Inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph, including all superior levels.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154635	25			0	lt	Chapter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149646	26			0	lt	Inserts the number of the chapter containing the reference target.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155553	33			0	lt	Category and Number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155356	34			0	lt	Inserts the category (caption type) and the number of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224	35			0	lt	Caption Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3145105	36			0	lt	Inserts the caption label of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149587	37			0	lt	Numbering				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146883	38			0	lt	Inserts the caption number of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id757469				0	lt	The "Number" format inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph. The superior levels are included depending on the context, as necessary. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5189062				0	lt	For example, when you are in a chapter 1, subchapter 2, subpart 5, this may be numbered as 1.2.5. When you insert here a reference to text in the previous subpart "1.2.4" and you apply the "Number" format, then the reference will be shown as "4". If in this example the numbering is set to show more sublevels, the same reference will be shown as "2.4" or "1.2.4", depending on the setting. If you use the "Number (full context)" format, you will always see "1.2.4", no matter how the numbered paragraph is formatted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156242	13			0	lt	Name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156259	14			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_REF:ED_REFNAME\"\>Type the name of the user-defined field that you want to create.\</ahelp\> To set a target, click "Set Reference" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, type a name in this box, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. To reference the new target, click the target name in the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	17			0	lt	In a master document, targets that are in different sub-documents are not displayed in the\<emph\> Selection\</emph\> list. If you want to insert a reference to the target, you must type the path and the name in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802250745				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the contents that you want to add to a user-defined fields.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159216	15			0	lt	If you select text in the document, and then insert a reference, the selected text becomes the contents of the field that you insert.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6501968				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Edit the value.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Functions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149123	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090003.xhp\" name=\"Functions\"\>Functions\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150343	45			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_FUNCVALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets additional function parameters for fields. The type of parameter depends on the field type that you select.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242	2			0	lt	Depending on the field type that you select, you can assign conditions to certain functions. For example, you can define a field that executes a macro when you click the field in the document, or a condition that, when met, hides a field. You can also define placeholder fields that insert graphics, tables, frames and other objects into your document when needed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id0902200804352037				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the \<emph\>Select \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537	3			0	lt	Type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155623	4			0	lt	Meaning				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152999	5			0	lt	Conditional text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149881	6			0	lt	Inserts text if a certain \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\> is met. For example, enter "sun eq 1" in the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> box, and then the text that you want to insert when the variable "sun" equals "1" in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box. If you want, you can also enter the text that you want to display when this condition is not met in the \<emph\>Else\</emph\> box. To define the variable "sun", click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090005.xhp\" name=\"Variables\"\>\<emph\>Variables\</emph\>\</link\> tab, select "Set variable", type "sun" in the\<emph\> Name\</emph\> box, and its value in the\<emph\> Value\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153719	47			0	lt	Input list				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147564	48			0	lt	Inserts a text field that displays one item from a list. You can add, edit, and remove items, and change their order in the list. Click an \<emph\>Input list\</emph\> field in your document or press Ctrl+Shift+F9 to display the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090003.xhp\" name=\"Choose Item\"\>\<emph\>Choose Item\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153146	7			0	lt	Input field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287	8			0	lt	Inserts a text field that you can open by \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090100.xhp\" name=\"clicking\"\>clicking\</link\> it in the document. You can then change the text that is displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154691	9			0	lt	Execute macro				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147515	10			0	lt	Inserts a text field that runs a macro when you click the field in the document. To assign a macro to the field, click the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> button. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152946	11			0	lt	Placeholder				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	12			0	lt	Inserts a placeholder field in the document, for example, for graphics. When you click a placeholder field in the document, you are prompted to insert the item that is missing.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150973	13			0	lt	Hidden text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147524	14			0	lt	Inserts a text field that is hidden when the condition that you specify is met. To use this function, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Fields: Hidden text\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480	15			0	lt	Hidden Paragraph				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153677	16			0	lt	Hides a paragraph when the condition that you specify is met. To use this function, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Fields: Hidden paragraph\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154192	39			0	lt	Combine characters 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3159199	42			0	lt	Combines up to 6 characters, so that they behave as a single character. This feature is only available when Asian fonts are supported.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id0902200804352213				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click the format that you want to apply to the selected field, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151329	17			0	lt	For function fields, the format field is only used for fields of the type placeholder. Here, the format determines the object for which the placeholder stands.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149494	18			0	lt	Condition				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3143281	19			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DB:ED_DBCONDITION\"\>For fields linked to a \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\>, enter the criteria here.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151248	20			0	lt	Then, Else				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154830	21			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_FUNCCOND2\"\>Enter the text to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box, and the text to display when the condition is not met in the \<emph\>Else \</emph\>box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865	22			0	lt	You can also insert database fields in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>and \<emph\>Else \</emph\>boxes using the format "databasename.tablename.fieldname".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147583	24			0	lt	If the table or the field name does not exist in a database, nothing is inserted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152585	23			0	lt	If you include the quotes in "databasename.tablename.fieldname", the expression is inserted as text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155136	26			0	lt	Reference				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155149	27			0	lt	Type the text that you want to display in the field. If you are inserting a placeholder field, type the text that you want to display as a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field. 				20130618 17:22:18
