helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145241	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/08010000.xhp\" name=\"Page Number\"\>Page Number\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151184	2			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:StatePageNumber\"\>The current page number is displayed in this field of the status bar. A double-click opens the Navigator, with which you can navigate in the document. A right-click shows all bookmarks in the document. Click a bookmark to position the text cursor at the bookmark location.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078	6			0	lt	The displayed page (x) and the total number of pages (y) are shown in the form \<emph\>Page x/y\</emph\> When you scroll through a document with the mouse, the page number is displayed when you release the mouse button. When you scroll using the right scrollbar, the page numbers are displayed as a Help tip. The page numbering format of the status bar and scrollbar is identical.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145417	3			0	lt	You can turn the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> display on or off by double-clicking the\<emph\> Page Number \</emph\>field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149806	4			0	lt	To go to a specific page, enter the page number in the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> spin button in the Navigator and then press Enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095	5			0	lt	By pressing the shortcut keys Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F5, you switch to entering a page number. When you press Enter, the cursor moves to the selected page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Combined Display				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151186	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/08080000.xhp\" name=\"Combined Display\"\>Combined Display\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172	2			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:StatusBarFunc\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Displays current information about the active document.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156375	3			0	lt	When the cursor is in a named section, the section name appears. When the cursor is in a table, the name of the table cell appears. The size of the object is shown when you edit frames or drawing objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145416	4			0	lt	When the cursor is positioned within text, you can double-click this field to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>\<emph\>Fields\</emph\>\</link\> dialog. In this dialog, you can define a field to be inserted in your document at the current cursor position. When the cursor is positioned in a table, a double-click in this field will call the \<emph\>Table Format\</emph\> dialog. Depending on the object selected, you can call up a dialog to edit a section, a graphic object, a floating frame, an OLE object, direct numbering or the position and size of a drawing object.				20130618 17:22:18
