helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148870	25			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_4\"\>Lists the names for the symbols in the current symbol set. Select a name from the list or type a name for a newly added symbol.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150215	28			0	lt	Adding a New Symbol				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3143233	6			0	lt	To add a symbol to a symbol set, select a font in the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> box, and then click a symbol in symbols pane. In the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> box, type a name for the symbol. In the \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box, select a symbol set, or type a new name to create a new symbol set. The right preview pane displays the symbol that you selected. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and then \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151389	29			0	lt	Modifying the Name of a Symbol				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147296	21			0	lt	To change the name of a symbol, select the old name in the \<emph\>Old symbol\</emph\> list box. Then enter the new name in the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> box. Check whether the desired character is in the preview window before you click the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> button. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157870	24			0	lt	Symbol Set				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145825	26			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_5\"\>The \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box contains the names of all existing symbol sets. You can modify a symbol set or create a new one.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154554	30			0	lt	Creating a New Symbol Set				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145594	22			0	lt	To create a new symbol set, type a name for it in the \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box and add at least one symbol. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog. The new symbol set is now available under the new name.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153736	10			0	lt	Font				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147374	11			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_LISTBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_1\"\>Displays the name of the current font and enables you to select a different font.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150564	32			0	lt	Subset				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145295	33			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_LISTBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_LB_FONTS_SUBSET\"\>If you selected a non-symbol font in the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> list box, you can select a Unicode subset in which to place your new or edited symbol. When a subset has been selected, all symbols belonging to this subset of the current symbol set are displayed in the symbols list above.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148386	19			0	lt	Typeface				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366	20			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_3\"\>The current typeface is displayed. You can change the typeface by selecting one from the list box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156262	12			0	lt	Add				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153922	13			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_1\"\>Click this button to add the symbol shown in the right preview window to the current symbol set.\</ahelp\> It will be saved under the name displayed in the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> list box. You must specify a name under \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> or \<emph\>Symbol Set\</emph\> to be able to use this button. Names cannot be used more than once.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150756	14			0	lt	Modify				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147570	15			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_2\"\>Click this button to replace the name of the symbol shown in the left preview window (the old name is displayed in the \<emph\>Old symbol\</emph\> list box) with the new name you have entered in the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> list box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154640	31			0	lt	Moving a Symbol to Another Symbol Set				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151174	27			0	lt	As an example, to transfer the large ALPHA from the "Greek" set to the "Special" set, select the old set (Greek) and then the ALPHA symbol using the two top list boxes. The symbol appears in the left preview window. In the \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box, select the "Special" set. Click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> and then \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The ALPHA symbol is now only in the "Special" symbol set.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145414	16			0	lt	Delete				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258	17			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_3\"\>Click to remove the symbol shown in the left preview window from the current symbol set.\</ahelp\> There will be no security query. Deleting the last remaining symbol of a symbol set also deletes the symbol set.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	18			0	lt	You can also click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> at any time to close the dialog without saving any of the changes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Import formula				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154659				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>importing; %PRODUCTNAME Math formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154659	1			0	lt	Import formula				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150251	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"formelimportierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ImportFormula\" visibility=\"visible\"\>This command opens a dialog for importing a formula.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153916	3			0	lt	The \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> dialog is set up like the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\> dialog under \<emph\>File\</emph\>. Use the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> dialog to load, edit and display a formula saved as a file in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\02\03010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Formula Cursor				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\02\03010000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149500				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>formula cursor in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cursor; in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\02\03010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149500	1			0	lt	Formula Cursor				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\02\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153916	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"cursor\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FORMULACURSOR\"\>Use this icon on the Tools bar to turn the Formula Cursor on or off.\</ahelp\> The part of the formula where the cursor is positioned in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window is marked with a thin border when the formula cursor is active.\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\02\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150048	14			0	lt	You can also click a position in the document to move the cursor to its corresponding position in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\02\03010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146966	15			0	lt	Double-clicking a character or symbol in the document moves the focus of the cursor to the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window and highlights its respective position. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Formula Shortcut Keys				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154702				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys; in formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154702	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"math_keys\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/04/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Formula Shortcut Keys\"\>Formula Shortcut Keys\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345	2			0	lt	A list of the shortcut keys specific to creating formulas is contained in this section.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150203	20			0	lt	The general \<link href=\"text/shared/04/01010000.xhp\" name=\"shortcut keys in $[officename]\"\>shortcut keys in $[officename]\</link\> also apply.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148870	3			0	lt	Shortcut Keys for Formula Functions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153246	19			0	lt	The following shortcut keys correspond to commands in the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> and \<emph\>View \</emph\>menus.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146324	11			0	lt	F3				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537	12			0	lt	Next Error				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155620	13			0	lt	Shift+F3				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355	14			0	lt	Previous Error				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153808	7			0	lt	F4				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149871	8			0	lt	Next Marker (Placeholder)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150396	9			0	lt	Shift+F4				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390	10			0	lt	Previous Marker (Placeholder)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154554	17			0	lt	F9				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153003	18			0	lt	Update				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153732	21			0	lt	Navigation in the Elements Window				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155927	23			0	lt	Left or right arrow				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145249	24			0	lt	Move left or right to the next category or function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150928	25			0	lt	Enter key				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148390	26			0	lt	Selects a category (within the category section) or inserts a function in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window (within the function section).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155988	27			0	lt	Tab				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153723	28			0	lt	Jump from the first category item to the first function of the category.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083451	29			0	lt	Shift+Tab				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\04\01020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151181	30			0	lt	Jump from the last category item to the last function of the category.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Arranging, Aligning and Distributing Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149656	73			0	lt	\<variable id=\"align_arrange\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/align_arrange.xhp\" name=\"Arranging and Aligning Objects\"\>Arranging, Aligning and Distributing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	bm_id3125863				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>arranging; objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;aligning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distributing draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aligning;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863	17			0	lt	Arranging Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3153727	18			0	lt	Each object that you place in your document is successively stacked on the preceding object. To re-arrange the stacking order of a selected object, proceed as follows.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	lt	Click the object whose position you want to change.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327	78			0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to bring up the context menu and choose one of the arrange options:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E6				0	lt	\<emph\>Bring to Front\</emph\> places the object on top of all other objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107EC				0	lt	\<emph\>Bring Forward\</emph\> places the object one place forward in the stack of objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F2				0	lt	\<emph\>Send Backward\</emph\> places the object one place back in the stack of objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	lt	\<emph\>Send to Back\</emph\> places the object behind all other objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FE				0	lt	\<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\> places the object behind another object that you select				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766	79			0	lt	Arranging an Object Behind Another Object				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN10811				0	lt	Click the object whose position you want to change.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253	80			0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\>. The mouse pointer changes to a hand.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126	81			0	lt	Click the object behind which you want to place the selected object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145789	20			0	lt	Reversing The Stacking Order of Two Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022	83			0	lt	Shift-click both objects to select them.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	84			0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reverse\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166425	21			0	lt	Aligning Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994	22			0	lt	The \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> function enables you to align objects relative to each other or relative to the page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	lt	Select an object to align it to the page or select multiple objects to align them relative to each other.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A7				0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Alignment\</item\> and select one of the alignment options.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	lt	Distributing Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390	71			0	lt	If you select three or more objects in Draw, you can also use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05360000.xhp\" name=\"Distribution\"\>\<emph\>Distribution\</emph\>\</link\> command to distribute the vertical and horizontal spacing evenly between the objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CE				0	lt	Select three or more objects to be distributed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D2				0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Distribution\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DA				0	lt	Select the horizontal and vertical distribution option and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535	72			0	lt	Selected objects are distributed evenly along the horizontal or vertical axis. The two outermost objects are used as reference points and do not move when the \<emph\>Distribution\</emph\> command is applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Defining Custom Colors				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149263				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>colors; defining and saving\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>user-defined colors\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>custom colors\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149263	7			0	lt	\<variable id=\"color_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/color_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Custom Colors\"\>Defining Custom Colors\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154511	8			0	lt	If you want, you can mix a custom color and add it to a color table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600	9			0	lt	To define a custom color				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327	25			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Colors\</emph\> tab. A table of the predefined colors is displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657	13			0	lt	Changes made to the standard color table are permanent and are saved automatically.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425	14			0	lt	Click a color in the table that is similar to the one you want to mix. The color appears in the upper preview box to the right of the table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992	15			0	lt	Select the RGB or CMYK color model in the box below the preview boxes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id4979705				0	lt	%PRODUCTNAME uses only the RGB color model for printing in color. The CMYK controls are provided only to ease the input of color values using CMYK notation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152987	16			0	lt	The RGB color model mixes red, green and blue light to create colors on a computer screen. In the RGB model, the three color components are additive and can have values ranging from 0 (black) to 255 (white). The CMYK color model combines Cyan (C), Magenta (M), Yellow (Y), and blacK (K, also used for "Key") to create colors for printing. The four colors of the CMYK models are subtractive and are defined as percentages. Black corresponds to 100 % and white to 0 %.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145386	17			0	lt	Enter a numeric value in the boxes next to the color components. The new color appears in the preview box directly above the color model box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152871	18			0	lt	You can also create a color using a color spectrum. Click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> button to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010501.xhp\" name=\"Color\"\>\<emph\>Color\</emph\>\</link\> dialog. Click a color. Use the Hue, Saturation, and Brightness boxes to adjust your color selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011	19			0	lt	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3147244	26			0	lt	If you want to replace the color in the standard color table that your custom color is based on, click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116	20			0	lt	If you want to add your custom color to the standard color table, enter a name in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> text box and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
