helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974	30			0	lt	\<variable id=\"draw_sector\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/draw_sector.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Sectors and Segments\"\>Drawing Sectors and Segments\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396	31			0	lt	The \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> toolbar contains tools for drawing ellipses and circles. You can also draw segments and sectors of circles and ellipses.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075	32			0	lt	To draw a sector of a circle or an ellipse:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	33			0	lt	Open the \<emph\>Ellipses\</emph\> toolbar and click one of the \<emph\>Circle Pie\</emph\> or \<emph\>Ellipse Pie\</emph\> icons \<image id=\"img_id3155768\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlepie_unfilled.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155768\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The mouse pointer changes to a cross hair with a small icon of a sector.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199	34			0	lt	Position the pointer at the edge of the circle you want to draw and drag to create the circle.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868	35			0	lt	To create a circle by dragging from the center, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3145361	36			0	lt	Release the mouse button when the circle has reached the size you want. A line corresponding to the circle radius appears in the circle.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872	37			0	lt	Position the pointer where you want to place the first boundary of the sector and click.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871	51			0	lt	As the radius line that follows the pointer is constrained to the circle boundaries, you can click anywhere in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3146874	38			0	lt	Position the pointer where you want to place the second boundary of the sector and click. The completed sector is displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148581	41			0	lt	To draw a segment of a circle or ellipse, follow the steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3153084	42			0	lt	To draw an arc based on an ellipse, choose one of the arc icons and follow the same steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20130618 17:22:18
