helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Grouping Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150793				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; grouping\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793	26			0	lt	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/groups.xhp\" name=\"Grouping Objects\"\>Grouping Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728	27			0	lt	You can combine several objects into a group so that they act as a single object. You can move and transform all objects in a group as a single unit. You can also change the properties (for example, line size, fill color) of all objects in a group as a whole or for individual objects in a group. Groups can be temporary or assigned:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434	64			0	lt	Temporary - group only lasts as long as all of the combined objects are selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	65			0	lt	Assigned - group lasts until it is ungrouped through a menu command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252	66			0	lt	Groups can also be grouped in other groups. Actions applied to a group do not affect the relative position of the individual objects to each other in the group.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150716	28			0	lt	To group objects:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3145643\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatgroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145643\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346	29			0	lt	Select the objects you want to group and choose \<emph\>Modify - Group\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485	30			0	lt	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147002	31			0	lt	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205	55			0	lt	Selecting Objects in a Group				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3155376\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_entergroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155376\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450	56			0	lt	You can select single objects in a group by entering the group. Double-click a group to enter it and click on the object to select it. You can also add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. The objects that are not part of the group are grayed out.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3151239				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3155264\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_leavegroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155264\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213	58			0	lt	To exit a group, double-click anywhere outside it.				20130618 17:22:18
