helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251	30			0	lt	3D objects that each form a 3D scene can be combined into a single 3D scene.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042	41			0	lt	To combine 3D objects:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702	31			0	lt	Insert a 3D object from the \<emph\>3D Objects\</emph\> toolbar (for example, a cube).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	32			0	lt	Insert a second slightly larger 3D object (for example, a sphere).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488	33			0	lt	Select the second 3D object (sphere) and choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211	34			0	lt	Double-click the first object (cube) to enter its group.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154652	35			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>. Both objects are now part of the same group. If you want, you can edit the individual objects or change their position within the group.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155376	36			0	lt	Double-click outside the group to exit the group.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606	38			0	lt	You cannot intersect or subtract 3D objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154537	39			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10090000.xhp\" name=\"Objects in 3D\"\>Objects in 3D\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
