helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	9			0	lt	Use EOF to avoid errors when you attempt to get input past the end of a file. When you use the Input or Get statement to read from a file, the file pointer is advanced by the number of bytes read. When the end of a file is reached, EOF returns the value "True" (-1).				20130618 17:22:18
