helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153380	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020405.xhp\" name=\"FileAttr-Function [Runtime]\"\>FileAttr Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366	2			0	lt	Returns the access mode or the file access number of a file that was opened with the Open statement. The file access number is dependent on the operating system (OSH = Operating System Handle).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3153364	3			0	lt	If you use a 32-Bit operating system, you cannot use the FileAttr-Function to determine the file access number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3163713	4			0	lt	See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020103.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151116	5			0	lt	Syntax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012	6			0	lt	FileAttr (FileNumber As Integer, Attribute As Integer)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147349	7			0	lt	Return value:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	8			0	lt	Integer				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153728	9			0	lt	Parameters:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3151074	10			0	lt	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> The number of the file that was opened with the Open statement.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3144766	11			0	lt	\<emph\>Attribute:\</emph\> Integer expression that indicates the type of file information that you want to return. The following values are possible:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396	12			0	lt	1: The FileAttr-Function indicates the access mode of the file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959	13			0	lt	2: The FileAttr-Function returns the file access number of the operating system.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018	14			0	lt	If you specify a parameter attribute with a value of 1, the following return values apply:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3149124	15			0	lt	1 - INPUT (file open for input)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275	16			0	lt	2 - OUTPUT (file open for output)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066	17			0	lt	4 - RANDOM (file open for random access)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3148406	18			0	lt	8 - APPEND (file open for appending)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757	19			0	lt	32 - BINARY (file open in binary mode).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147339	20			0	lt	Example:				20130618 17:22:18
