helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Date and Time Functions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150502	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030000.xhp\" name=\"Date and Time Functions\"\>Date and Time Functions\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153255	2			0	lt	Use the statements and functions described here to perform date and time calculations.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363	3			0	lt	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Basic lets you calculate time or date differences by converting the time and date values to continuous numeric values. After the difference is calculated, special functions are used to reconvert the values to the standard time or date formats.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054	4			0	lt	You can combine date and time values into a single floating-decimal number. Dates are converted to integers, and times to decimal values. \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Basic also supports the variable type Date, which can contain a time specification consisting of both a date and time.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Converting Date Values				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030100.xhp\" name=\"Converting Date Values\"\>Converting Date Values\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760	2			0	lt	The following functions convert date values to calculable numbers and back.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	DateSerial Function [Runtime]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157896				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>DateSerial function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157896	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030101.xhp\" name=\"DateSerial Function [Runtime]\"\>DateSerial Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267	2			0	lt	Returns a \<emph\>Date\</emph\> value for a specified year, month, or day.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147264	3			0	lt	Syntax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670	4			0	lt	DateSerial (year, month, day)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	5			0	lt	Return value:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398	6			0	lt	Date				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154141	7			0	lt	Parameters:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147229	8			0	lt	\<emph\>Year:\</emph\> Integer expression that indicates a year. All values between 0 and 99 are interpreted as the years 1900-1999. For years that fall outside this range, you must enter all four digits.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280	9			0	lt	\<emph\>Month:\</emph\> Integer expression that indicates the month of the specified year. The accepted range is from 1-12.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151043	10			0	lt	\<emph\>Day:\</emph\> Integer expression that indicates the day of the specified month. The accepted range is from 1-31. No error is returned when you enter a non-existing day for a month shorter than 31 days. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3161832	11			0	lt	The \<emph\>DateSerial function\</emph\> returns the number of days between December 30,1899 and the given date. You can use this function to calculate the difference between two dates.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155306	12			0	lt	The \<emph\>DateSerial function\</emph\> returns the data type Variant with VarType 7 (Date). Internally, this value is stored as a Double value, so that when the given date is 1.1.1900, the returned value is 2. Negative values correspond to dates before December 30, 1899 (not inclusive).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576	13			0	lt	If a date is defined that lies outside of the accepted range, $[officename] Basic returns an error message.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481	14			0	lt	Whereas you define the \<emph\>DateValue function\</emph\> as a string that contains the date, the \<emph\>DateSerial function\</emph\> evaluates each of the parameters (year, month, day) as separate numeric expressions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411	15			0	lt	Example:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646	16			0	lt	Sub ExampleDateSerial				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441	17			0	lt	Dim lDate as Long				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154791	18			0	lt	Dim sDate as String				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155415	19			0	lt	lDate = DateSerial(1964, 4, 9)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125	20			0	lt	sDate = DateSerial(1964, 4, 9)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942	21			0	lt	msgbox lDate REM returns 23476				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151074	22			0	lt	msgbox sDate REM returns 04/09/1964				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878	23			0	lt	end sub				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	DateValue Function [Runtime]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156344				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>DateValue function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156344	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030102.xhp\" name=\"DateValue Function [Runtime]\"\>DateValue Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150542	2			0	lt	Returns a date value from a date string. The date string is a complete date in a single numeric value. You can also use this serial number to determine the difference between two dates.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148799	3			0	lt	Syntax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910	4			0	lt	DateValue [(date)]				20130618 17:22:18
