helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03080101.xhp\" name=\"Atn Function [Runtime]\"\>Atn Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	2			0	lt	Trigonometric function that returns the arctangent of a numeric expression. The return value is in the range -Pi/2 to +Pi/2.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271	3			0	lt	The arctangent is the inverse of the tangent function. The Atn Function returns the angle "Alpha", expressed in radians, using the tangent of this angle. The function can also return the angle "Alpha" by comparing the ratio of the length of the side that is opposite of the angle to the length of the side that is adjacent to the angle in a right-angled triangle.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	4			0	lt	Atn(side opposite the angle/side adjacent to angle)= Alpha				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149669	5			0	lt	Syntax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148947	6			0	lt	Atn (Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148664	7			0	lt	Return value:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150359	8			0	lt	Double				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148798	9			0	lt	Parameters:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156212	10			0	lt	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Any numerical expression that represents the ratio of two sides of a right triangle. The Atn function returns the corresponding angle in radians (arctangent).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192	11			0	lt	To convert radians to degrees, multiply radians by 180/pi.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147230	12			0	lt	degree=(radian*180)/pi				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	13			0	lt	radian=(degree*pi)/180				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159252	14			0	lt	Pi is here the fixed circle constant with the rounded value 3.14159.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153142	15			0	lt	Example:				20130618 17:22:18
