helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869	9			0	lt	The natural logarithm is the logarithm to the base e. Base e is a constant with an approximate value of 2.718282...				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968	10			0	lt	You can calculate logarithms to any base (n) for any number (x) by dividing the natural logarithm of x by the natural logarithm of n, as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
