helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Controlling Program Execution				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145136	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090000.xhp\" name=\"Controlling Program Execution\"\>Controlling Program Execution\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143268	2			0	lt	The following statements control the execution of a program.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156152	3			0	lt	A program generally executes from the first line of code to the last line of code. You can also execute certain procedures within the program according to specific conditions, or repeat a section of the program within a sub-procedure or function. You can use loops to repeat parts of a program as many times as necessary, or until a certain condition is met. These type of control statements are classified as Condition, Loop, or Jump statements.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Condition Statements				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154422	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090100.xhp\" name=\"Condition Statements\"\>Condition Statements\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750	2			0	lt	The following statements are based on conditions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154422				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>If statement\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154422	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090101.xhp\" name=\"If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]\"\>If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555	2			0	lt	Defines one or more statement blocks that you only want to execute if a given condition is True.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957	3			0	lt	Syntax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	4			0	lt	If condition=true Then Statement block [ElseIf condition=true Then] Statement block [Else] Statement block EndIf\<br/\>Instead of Else If you can write ElseIf, instead of End If you can write EndIf.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419	5			0	lt	Parameters:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062	6			0	lt	The \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> statement executes program blocks depending on given conditions. When $[officename] Basic encounters an \<emph\>If\</emph\> statement, the condition is tested. If the condition is True, all subsequent statements up to the next \<emph\>Else\</emph\> or \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statement are executed. If the condition is False, and an \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statement follows, $[officename] Basic tests the next condition and executes the following statements if the condition is True. If False, the program continues either with the next \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> or \<emph\>Else\</emph\> statement. Statements following \<emph\>Else\</emph\> are executed only if none of the previously tested conditions were True. After all conditions are evaluated, and the corresponding statements executed, the program continues with the statement following \<emph\>EndIf\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192	7			0	lt	You can nest multiple \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> statements.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684	8			0	lt	\<emph\>Else\</emph\> and \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statements are optional.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152939	9			0	lt	You can use \<emph\>GoTo\</emph\> and \<emph\>GoSub\</emph\> to jump out of an \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> block, but not to jump into an \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> structure.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951	10			0	lt	The following example enables you to enter the expiration date of a product, and determines if the expiration date has passed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152576	11			0	lt	Example:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011	12			0	lt	Sub ExampleIfThenDate				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645	13			0	lt	Dim sDate as String				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	14			0	lt	Dim sToday as String				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	16			0	lt	sDate = InputBox("Enter the expiration date (MM.DD.YYYY)")				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943	17			0	lt	sDate = Right$(sDate, 4) + Mid$(sDate, 4, 2) + Left$(sDate, 2)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098	18			0	lt	sToday = Date$				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765	19			0	lt	sToday = Right$(sToday, 4)+ Mid$(sToday, 4, 2) + Left$(sToday, 2)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154792	20			0	lt	If sDate < sToday Then				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155601	21			0	lt	MsgBox "The expiration date has passed"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972	22			0	lt	ElseIf sDate > sToday Then				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146912	23			0	lt	MsgBox "The expiration date has not yet passed"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153710	24			0	lt	Else				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754	25			0	lt	MsgBox "The expiration date is today"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361	26			0	lt	End If				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405	28			0	lt	End Sub				20130618 17:22:18
