helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344	16			0	lt	\<emph\>Condition:\</emph\> A comparison, numeric or string expression, that evaluates either True or False.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	17			0	lt	\<emph\>Statement block:\</emph\> Statements that you want to repeat while or until the condition is True.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150791	18			0	lt	The \<emph\>Do...Loop\</emph\> statement executes a loop as long as, or until, a certain condition is True. The condition for exiting the loop must be entered following either the \<emph\>Do\</emph\> or the \<emph\>Loop\</emph\> statement. The following examples are valid combinations:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154366	19			0	lt	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171	20			0	lt	Do While condition = True				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149203	21			0	lt	...statement block				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	22			0	lt	Loop				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124	24			0	lt	The statement block between the Do While and the Loop statements is repeated so long as the condition is true.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968	25			0	lt	Do Until condition = True				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909	26			0	lt	...statement block				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159151	27			0	lt	Loop				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440	29			0	lt	The statement block between the Do Until and the Loop statements is repeated if the condition so long as the condition is false.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153952	30			0	lt	Do				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147349	31			0	lt	...statement block				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153	32			0	lt	Loop While condition = True				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985	34			0	lt	The statement block between the Do and the Loop statements repeats so long as the condition is true.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488	35			0	lt	Do				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189	36			0	lt	...statement block				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	37			0	lt	Loop Until condition = True				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151117	39			0	lt	The statement block between the Do and the Loop statements repeats until the condition is true.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484	41			0	lt	Use the \<emph\>Exit Do\</emph\> statement to unconditionally end the loop. You can add this statement anywhere in a \<emph\>Do\</emph\>...\<emph\>Loop\</emph\> statement. You can also define an exit condition using the \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> structure as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
