helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149205				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>For statement\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>To statement\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Step statement\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Next statement\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149205	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090202.xhp\" name=\"For...Next Statement [Runtime]\"\>For...Next Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267	2			0	lt	Repeats the statements between the For...Next block a specified number of times.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156153	3			0	lt	Syntax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473	4			0	lt	For counter=start To end [Step step]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024	5			0	lt	statement block				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146796	6			0	lt	[Exit For]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3159414	7			0	lt	statement block				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153897	8			0	lt	Next [counter]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150400	9			0	lt	Variables:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358	10			0	lt	\<emph\>Counter:\</emph\> Loop counter initially assigned the value to the right of the equal sign (start). Only numeric variables are valid. The loop counter increases or decreases according to the variable Step until End is passed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152455	11			0	lt	\<emph\>Start:\</emph\> Numeric variable that defines the initial value at the beginning of the loop.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151043	12			0	lt	\<emph\>End:\</emph\> Numeric variable that defines the final value at the end of the loop.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281	13			0	lt	\<emph\>Step:\</emph\> Sets the value by which to increase or decrease the loop counter. If Step is not specified, the loop counter is incremented by 1. In this case, End must be greater than Start. If you want to decrease Counter, End must be less than Start, and Step must be assigned a negative value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684	14			0	lt	The \<emph\>For...Next\</emph\> loop repeats all of the statements in the loop for the number of times that is specified by the parameters.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287	15			0	lt	As the counter variable is decreased, $[officename] Basic checks if the end value has been reached. As soon as the counter passes the end value, the loop automatically ends.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154	16			0	lt	It is possible to nest \<emph\>For...Next\</emph\> statements. If you do not specify a variable following the \<emph\>Next\</emph\> statement, \<emph\>Next\</emph\> automatically refers to the most recent \<emph\>For\</emph\> statement.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3155306	17			0	lt	If you specify an increment of 0, the statements between \<emph\>For\</emph\> and \<emph\>Next\</emph\> are repeated continuously.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854	18			0	lt	When counting down the counter variable, $[officename] Basic checks for overflow or underflow. The loop ends when Counter exceeds End (positive Step value) or is less than End (negative Step value).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273	19			0	lt	Use the \<emph\>Exit For\</emph\> statement to exit the loop unconditionally. This statement must be within a \<emph\>For...Next\</emph\> loop. Use the \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> statement to test the exit condition as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190	20			0	lt	For...				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149482	21			0	lt	statements				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124	22			0	lt	If condition = True Then Exit For				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153159	23			0	lt	statements				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096	24			0	lt	Next				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286	25			0	lt	Note: In nested \<emph\>For...Next\</emph\> loops, if you exit a loop unconditionally with \<emph\>Exit For\</emph\>, only one loop is exited.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148457	26			0	lt	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151074	27			0	lt	The following example uses two nested loops to sort a string array with 10 elements ( sEntry() ), that are first filled with various contents:				20130618 17:22:18
