helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150199	33			0	lt	            \<variable id=\"background\"\>                \<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/background.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Slide Background Fill\"\>Changing the Slide Background Fill\</link\>            \</variable\>        				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155067	34			0	lt	You can change the background color or the background fill of the current slide or all of the slides in your document. For a background fill, you can use hatching, a gradient, or a bitmap image.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148701	36			0	lt	If you want to change the background fill for all of the slides, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>. To change the background fill of a single slide, choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id624713				0	lt	            \<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click Set Background Picture for Slide in the context menu of a slide in Normal view to select a bitmap file. This file is used as a background picture.\</ahelp\>        				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150534	49			0	lt	To use a color, gradient, or hatching pattern for the slide background				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149942	50			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148725	51			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Fill \</emph\>area, do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153040	52			0	lt	Select \<emph\>Color\</emph\>, and then click a color in the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150866	53			0	lt	Select \<emph\>Gradient\</emph\>, and then click a gradient style in the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150338	54			0	lt	Select \<emph\>Hatching\</emph\>, and then click a hatching style in the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150021	55			0	lt	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145244	56			0	lt	To use an image for the slide background				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148394	57			0	lt	You can display an entire image as a slide background, or you can tile the image to produce a patterned background.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156064	58			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3145356	59			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Fill \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap\</emph\>, and then click an image in the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150757	60			0	lt	If you want to use a custom image for the slide background, close the \<emph\>Page Setup \</emph\>dialog, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Bitmaps \</emph\>tab, and then click \<emph\>Import\</emph\>. Locate the image you want to import and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When you return to the \<emph\>Background \</emph\>tab, the image you imported will be in the \<emph\>Bitmap \</emph\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153151	61			0	lt	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150263	62			0	lt	To display the entire image as the background, clear the \<emph\>Tile \</emph\>check box in the \<emph\>Position \</emph\>area, and then select \<emph\>AutoFit\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149756	63			0	lt	To tile the image on the background, select \<emph\>Tile\</emph\>, and set the \<emph\>Size\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> options for the image.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154934	64			0	lt	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3158403	47			0	lt	This modification is only valid for the current presentation document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10820				0	lt	To save a new slide master as a template				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10827				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\> to change to the slide master.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\> to change the slide background, or choose other formatting commands. Objects that you add here will be visible on all slides that are based on this slide master.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> to close the master view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083F				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> to save the document as a template.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10847				0	lt	Enter a name for the template. Do not change the category from "My Templates". Click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084A				0	lt	Now you can use the Presentation Wizard to open a new presentation based on your new template.				20130618 17:22:18
