helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146121				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>importing; presentations with HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; importing HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; importing into presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;inserting in slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; text in presentations\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"html_import\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/html_import.xhp\" name=\"Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations \"\>Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations \</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3150750	2			0	lt	You can import any text file, including text in HTML documents, into a slide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155443	11			0	lt	To insert text from a file into a slide:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	4			0	lt	In the slide where you want to insert the text, choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3150207	5			0	lt	Select "Text" or "HTML Document" as the \<emph\>File type\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3148610	12			0	lt	Locate the file containing the text that you want to add, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915	6			0	lt	If the text file contains more text than can be inserted into a single slide, you can divide the text over several slides.				20130618 17:22:18
