helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	3			0	lt	Layers are available in $[officename] Draw, not in $[officename] Impress. Layers allow you to assemble elements on a page that are related. Think of layers as individual workspaces that you can hide from view, hide from printing, or lock. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id7036957				0	lt	Layers do not determine the stacking order of objects on your page, except for the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer which is always in front of other layers. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id1614734				0	lt	The stacking order of objects on your page is determined by the sequence in which you add the objects. You can rearrange the stacking order by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\>. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id398876				0	lt	The areas on a layer that do not contain objects are transparent.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962	12			0	lt	$[officename] Draw provides three default layers:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073	13			0	lt	Layout				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053	14			0	lt	Controls				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391	15			0	lt	Dimension Lines				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156397	16			0	lt	You cannot delete or rename the default layers. You can add your own layers by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Layer\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534	17			0	lt	The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer is the default workspace. The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer determines the location of title, text, and object placeholders on your page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742	18			0	lt	The \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer can be used for buttons that have been assigned an action, but that should not be printed. Set the layer's properties to not printable. Objects on the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer are always in front of objects on other layers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085	19			0	lt	The \<emph\>Dimension Lines\</emph\> layer is where you draw, for example, the dimension lines. By switching the layer to show or hide, you can easily switch these lines on and off.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507	2			0	lt	You can lock a layer to protect its contents, or hide a layer and its contents from view or from printing. When you add a new layer to a page, the layer is added to all of the pages in your document. However, when you add an object to a layer, it is only added to the current page. If you want the object to appear on all of the pages, add the object to the master page (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Master\</item\>).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Loading Line and Arrow Styles				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>line styles;loading\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines;about line ends\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>arrows;loading arrow styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;arrow and line styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>loading;arrow and line styles\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253	48			0	lt	\<variable id=\"line_arrow_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_arrow_styles.xhp\" name=\"Loading Line and Arrow Styles\"\>Loading Line and Arrow Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017	49			0	lt	You can use styles to organize similar line and arrow types. $[officename] provides a few standard style files that you can load and use in your document. If you want, you can add or delete elements from a style file, or even create a custom style file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154485	50			0	lt	To load a line styles file:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	58			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Line Styles\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705	51			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Load Line Styles\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145588	52			0	lt	Locate the file containing the line styles that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The file has the format [filename].sod.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240	53			0	lt	To save a line styles file, click the \<emph\>Save Line Styles\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154765	54			0	lt	To load an arrow styles file:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153070	59			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Arrow Styles\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149054	55			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Load Arrow Styles\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391	56			0	lt	Locate the file containing the arrow styles that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The file has the format [filename].soe.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465	57			0	lt	To save an arrow styles file, click the \<emph\>Save Arrow Styles\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145822				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05200000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Line\"\>Format - Line\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Drawing Curves				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149377				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>lines; drawing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves; drawing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>control points definition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>corner points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing;lines\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377	3			0	lt	\<variable id=\"line_draw\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_draw.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Curves\"\>Drawing Curves\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868	4			0	lt	The \<emph\>Curve\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3150205\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150205\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar opens a toolbar to draw Bézier curves. Bézier curves are defined by a start point and an end point, which are called "anchors". The curvature of the Bézier curve is defined by control points ("handles"). Moving a control point changes the shape of the Bézier curve.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id8532364				0	lt	Control points are only visible in "Edit Points" mode. Control points are represented by circles, anchor points are represented by squares. The start point is a little bit larger than the other anchor points.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210	39			0	lt	Bézier curve segments and straight line segments can be joined to form more complex Bézier curves. Three different transitions can be applied to join adjacent segments:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766	25			0	lt	A \<emph\>symmetrical\</emph\> anchor point has the same line curvature on either side, and two control lines that move together as a straight line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874	26			0	lt	A \<emph\>smooth\</emph\> anchor point may have different line curvatures on either side.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150435	27			0	lt	A \<emph\>corner\</emph\> anchor point has one or two independent control lines. Changing one side has no effect on the other side.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id46388				0	lt	How to use the Curve tool				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155262	5			0	lt	On the Drawing toolbar, open the \<emph\>Curves\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"img_id3145829\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145829\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and select the \<emph\>Curve\</emph\>\<image id=\"Graphic1\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezier_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> tool.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155928	6			0	lt	Click where you want the curve to start, and drag in the direction where you want the curve to go. The control line will indicate the direction. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id8174687				0	lt	Hold down \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift\</item\> while you drag to restrict the direction to a 45 degree grid.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3148390	41			0	lt	Release the mouse where the first control point should be.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154865	22			0	lt	Move the pointer to where you want the curve segment to end. The curve follows the pointer. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id1556443				0	lt	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172	9			0	lt	Double-click on the position of the end point to finish drawing the line. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id5377056				0	lt	To create a closed shape, double-click the starting point of the line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919	23			0	lt	Click and release the mouse button to add an anchor point. Move the mouse to draw the next segment.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149451	43			0	lt	Click and drag in any direction to add a smooth anchor point.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id2071596				0	lt	How to use the Freeform Line tool				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id4907681				0	lt	On the Drawing toolbar, open the \<emph\>Curves\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"Graphic2\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and select the \<emph\>Freeform Line\</emph\>\<image id=\"Graphic3\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_freeline_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> tool.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id1122165				0	lt	Click where you want the curve to start, and keep holding the mouse button down.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id5792107				0	lt	Draw the freeform line as you would do with a pencil.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id7734916				0	lt	Release the mouse button to finish the line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Editing Curves				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>curves; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>splitting;curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>closing;shapes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>points;adding/converting/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441	10			0	lt	\<variable id=\"line_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Curves\"\>Editing Curves\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342	11			0	lt	A curved line segment consists of two data points (endpoints) and two control points (handles). A control line connects a control point to a data point. You can change the shape of a curve by converting a data point to a different type, or by dragging the control points to a different location.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252	16			0	lt	You can also modify the properties of the line by selecting the line and choosing \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3149018\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectbeziermode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149018\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959	54			0	lt	To view the data points and control points of a curved line, select the line, and then click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the Drawing bar. The data points are represented by squares and the control points by circles. A control point might overlay a data point.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145587	55			0	lt	To adjust a curved line segment:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241	51			0	lt	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213	56			0	lt	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810	12			0	lt	Drag a data point to resize the line. If a control point overlies the data point, drag the control point until you can see the data point, and then drag the data point.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872	13			0	lt	Drag a control point. The curve pulls in the direction that you drag the control point.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150431	57			0	lt	To split a curved line:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395	58			0	lt	You can only split a curved line that has three or more data points.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151392	59			0	lt	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149941	60			0	lt	Select a data point, and then click the \<emph\>Split Curve \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150655	61			0	lt	To create a closed shape:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150743	62			0	lt	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153080	63			0	lt	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Close Bézier\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145162	15			0	lt	To convert a data point on a curved line:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336	64			0	lt	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155925	14			0	lt	Click the data point you want to convert, and do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241	65			0	lt	To convert the data point to a smooth point, click the \<emph\>Smooth Transition\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299	66			0	lt	To convert the data point to a symmetrical point, click the \<emph\>Symmetric Transition\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145348	67			0	lt	To convert the data point to a corner point, click the \<emph\>Corner Point\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150471	68			0	lt	To add a data point:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155373	69			0	lt	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156256	70			0	lt	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Insert Points\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3083280	71			0	lt	Click the line where you want to add the point, and drag a short distance.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154643	72			0	lt	If a data point does not have a control point, select the data point, and then click the \<emph\>Convert to Curve\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151186	73			0	lt	To delete a data point:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153624	74			0	lt	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150261	75			0	lt	Click the point you want to delete.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3143230	76			0	lt	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Delete Points\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151174	52			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0227.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points bar\"\>Edit Points bar\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
