helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id5703909				0	lt	You see four areas on this dialog with check boxes for Header, Date and time, Footer, and Page number. These four areas correspond to the four areas in the corners of the handout master view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id4984282				0	lt	Enter text for header, footer, and date. Check the \<emph\>Page number\</emph\> box, if you want to number the handout pages. Ensure the \<emph\>Header\</emph\> check box is enabled if you want your header text to be printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id816064				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Apply to All\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id863063				0	lt	The fields in the handout master view on screen are not updated, but the text that you entered will be printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id5036164				0	lt	Printing handouts or notes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id2901394				0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Print\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id5674611				0	lt	Click the Document listbox and select the type of contents to print.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id1308023				0	lt	Select \<emph\>Handouts\</emph\> or \<emph\>Notes\</emph\> and select the number of slides to print on each page of paper.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id6821192				0	lt	If you want another layout of the slides on the printed paper pages, use the mouse to move the slides around on the Handout view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151389	11			0	lt	Printing a range of slides				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3146318	12			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465	13			0	lt	Hold down Shift, and click the range of slides that you want to print.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875	14			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3150746	16			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Range and copies\</emph\> area, click \<emph\>Slides\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3154561	17			0	lt	Enter the slide numbers you want to print, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>presentations;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>timings; rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide changes;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording;display times for slides\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253	17			0	lt	\<variable id=\"rehearse_timings\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\" name=\"Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\"\>Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	1			0	lt	$[officename] assists you in defining the right rehearse timings for automatic slide changes. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963	16			0	lt	Prepare the slides, start the show using a special icon, tell your imaginary audience what you want to tell for the first slide, then advance to the next slide and so on. $[officename] records the display time for each slide, so the next time you play the show with automatic slide changes, the timing will be as recorded.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317	2			0	lt	To record a show with rehearse timings				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874	4			0	lt	Open a presentation, and switch to \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\> View.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150651	6			0	lt	Start the show with the \<emph\>Rehearse Timings\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156396\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_rehearsetimings.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156396\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the Slide View bar. You see the first slide, and a timer in the bottom corner.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145590	8			0	lt	When it's time to advance to the next slide, click the timer. To keep the default setting for this slide, click the slide, but not the timer. Continue for all slides in your presentation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150333	10			0	lt	$[officename] has recorded the display time for each slide. Save your presentation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145248	12			0	lt	If you want the whole presentation to auto-repeat, open the menu \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935	13			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Slide Show Settings\"\>Slide Show Settings\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Selecting Underlying Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154492				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>objects; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting; hidden objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>covered objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>underlying objects\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154492	7			0	lt	\<variable id=\"select_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/select_object.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Underlying Objects\"\>Selecting Underlying Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238	9			0	lt	To select an object that is covered by other objects, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click through the objects until you reach the underlying object. To cycle through the objects in reverse order, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift when you click.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213	10			0	lt	To select an object that is covered by another object using the keyboard, press Tab to cycle through the objects on the slide. To cycle through the objects in reverse order, press Shift+Tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Showing a Slide Show				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	bm_id5592516				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>running slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide shows; starting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; starting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting; slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide transitions;automatic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide transition\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id4901272				0	lt	\<variable id=\"show\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/show.xhp\" name=\"Showing a Slide Show\"\>Showing a Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9636829				0	lt	Different ways exist to start a slide show. Once a slide show is running, you can take control pressing keys or clicking the mouse buttons.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id7076937				0	lt	By default, a slide show always starts with the first slide. You advance manually through slides up to the last slide. You can change these settings.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id9954527				0	lt	Running a Slide Show				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6860255				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show\</emph\> to run the show.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4199957				0	lt	If you want all shows to start from the current slide instead of the first slide, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3209936				0	lt	Click to advance to the next effect or to the next slide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8702658				0	lt	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> to abort the show before the end.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3741264				0	lt	Many more keys are available to \<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\"\>control a slide show\</link\>. You can also right-click to open a context menu with useful commands.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id5694143				0	lt	Showing an automatic slide show (kiosk mode)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id5829645				0	lt	For an automatic change to the next slide, you must assign a slide transition to each slide. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id2361522				0	lt	On the Task Pane, click \<emph\>Slide Transition\</emph\> to open that tab page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9168980				0	lt	In the \<emph\>Advance slide\</emph\> area, click \<emph\>Automatically after\</emph\>, and select a time duration.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9766533				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Apply to All Slides\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6081728				0	lt	You can assign a different time for every slide to advance to the next slide. The \<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\"\>rehearse timings\</link\> feature can assist you to get the timing right.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9219641				0	lt	To advance to the first slide, after all slides have been shown, you must set the slide show to repeat automatically.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3174230				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1336405				0	lt	In the Type area, click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and select a pause time between shows.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4959257				0	lt	When you create a new slide show using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01050000.xhp\"\>Presentation Wizard\</link\>, you can select the duration of slides and of the pause, on the third wizard page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id1906491				0	lt	Running a slide show from a file				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4799340				0	lt	You can start %PRODUCTNAME from a command prompt, followed by the parameter \<item type=\"literal\"\>-show\</item\> and an Impress filename. For example, to start the file \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> from the command prompt, enter the following command:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1502121				0	lt	\<item type=\"literal\"\>soffice -show filename.odp\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	lt	This assumes that soffice is in the program path of your system, and that \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> is located in the current directory.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Including Spreadsheets in Slides				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154022				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;in presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations;inserting spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>including spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"table_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/table_insert.xhp\" name=\"Including Spreadsheets in Slides\"\>Including Spreadsheets in Slides\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id4231086				0	lt	You can apply different methods to insert spreadsheet cells into your Impress slides or Draw pages:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id9209875				0	lt	Insert a native table - you enter the data into the cells and apply fancy formatting using the Table Design section on the Tasks pane.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3044526				0	lt	Insert a new table as an OLE object or insert an existing file as an OLE object - you can specify the link to a file to be a live link to the latest data saved in a spreadsheet file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id137333				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the number of columns for the new table.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id8626667				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the number of rows for the new table.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551581				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Define the vertical alignment of selected or all cell contents. Split or merge cells.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551553				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All selected cells are merged into one cell.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551535				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The selected cell is split into several cells. You see the Split Cells dialog box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551651				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are align at the top of the cells.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551697				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are aligned vertically centered in the cells.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551632				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are aligned at the bottom of the cells.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10626				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Selects the current table.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551734				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose commands for the selected or all rows.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080035				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distributes the height of the selected or all rows to the same size. The height of the table is not changed.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080063				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, all rows will be selected. If currently cells are selected, all rows containing the selected cells will be selected.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id091620080408008				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, a new row will be inserted at the bottom of the table. If currently cells are selected, as many new rows as the selection has will be inserted below the selection.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080050				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All rows of the current selection will be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163012				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose commands for the selected or all columns.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163092				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distributes the width of the selected or all columns to the same size. The width of the table is not changed.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163046				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, all columns will be selected. If currently cells are selected, all columns containing the selected cells will be selected.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163128				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, a new column will be inserted at the right border of the table. If currently cells are selected, as many new columns as the selection has will be inserted right of the selection.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163127				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All columns of the current selection will be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163151				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Align the table within the page or slide.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id8594317				0	lt	Inserting a native table				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7184972				0	lt	Go to the Impress slide or Draw page where you want to insert the table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id248115				0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Table\</item\> or use the Table icon on the Standard toolbar to insert a table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2748496				0	lt	Double-click the table and enter or paste the data into the cells. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id8270210				0	lt	Select some cell contents and right-click to open the context menu. Choose commands to change the cell's contents, like font size and line spacing.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6820276				0	lt	Right-click the table border to open the table's context menu. Use the table's context menu to enter a name and description for the table, or to distribute the rows or columns equally, among other commands.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551725				0	lt	Select some cells and right-click to open a context menu, where you can insert or delete rows and columns, among other commands. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id091620080355171				0	lt	To select a rectangular area of cells, point to a cell in one corner of the rectangle, hold down the mouse button, and drag the mouse to the opposite corner of the rectangle, then release the mouse button. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551880				0	lt	To select one cell, point to that cell, hold down the mouse button, and drag the mouse to the next cell and back, then release the mouse button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075	2			0	lt	Inserting a new spreadsheet as an OLE object				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715	7			0	lt	You can add a blank $[officename] Calc spreadsheet to a slide as an OLE object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749	3			0	lt	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	18			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Insert - OLE- Object\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Create new\</emph\> and select the %PRODUCTNAME Spreadsheet. Click OK. Click in the spreadsheet to enter your data. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2466505				0	lt	Click outside the spreadsheet to view the slide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148870	9			0	lt	To resize the spreadsheet without resizing the cells, double-click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle. To resize the cells of the spreadsheet, click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150215	11			0	lt	Inserting a spreadsheet from a file				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154765	19			0	lt	When you insert an existing spreadsheet into your slide, changes that are made to the original spreadsheet file are not updated on your slide. You can, however, make changes to the spreadsheet in your slide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145112	12			0	lt	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153075	13			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - OLE Object\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391	14			0	lt	Select \<emph\>Create from file\</emph\>, and click \<emph\>Search\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537	20			0	lt	Locate the file you want to insert, and then click\<emph\> OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id1616565				0	lt	Enable the \<emph\>Link to file\</emph\> checkbox to insert the file as a live link.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155256	21			0	lt	The entire spreadsheet is inserted into your slide. If you want to change the sheet that is displayed, double-click the spreadsheet, and then select a different sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
