helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150767				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; sorting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sorting; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>data;sorting in databases\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767	44			0	lt	\<variable id=\"database_sort\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_sort.xhp\" name=\"Sorting Database Ranges\"\>Sorting Data\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3145751	45			0	lt	Click in a database range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id121020081121549				0	lt	If you select a range of cells, only these cells will get sorted. If you just click one cell without selecting, then the whole database range will get sorted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10635				0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Sort\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id121020081121547				0	lt	The range of cells that will get sorted is shown in inverted colors.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	lt	Select the sort options that you want.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063D				0	lt	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1846980				0	lt	\<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Defining_a_Data_Range\"\>Wiki page about defining a data range\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Pivot Table				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150448				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; introduction\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot, see pivot table function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150448	7			0	lt	\<variable id=\"datapilot\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot.xhp\" name=\"Pivot Table\"\>Pivot Table\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024	2			0	lt	The \<emph\>pivot table\</emph\> (formerly known as \<emph\>DataPilot\</emph\>) allows you to combine, compare, and analyze large amounts of data. You can view different summaries of the source data, you can display the details of areas of interest, and you can create reports.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069	9			0	lt	A table that has been created as a \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090000.xhp\" name=\"pivot table\"\>pivot table\</link\> is an interactive table. Data can be arranged, rearranged or summarized according to different points of view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Creating Pivot Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148491				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; calling up and applying\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148491	7			0	lt	\<variable id=\"datapilot_createtable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_createtable.xhp\" name=\"Creating Pivot Tables\"\>Creating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023	8			0	lt	Position the cursor within a range of cells containing values, row and column headings.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264	9			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Create\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Select Source\</emph\> dialog appears. Choose \<emph\>Current selection\</emph\> and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The table headings are shown as buttons in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog. Drag these buttons as required and drop them into the layout areas "Page Fields", "Column Fields", "Row Fields" and "Data Fields".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868	10			0	lt	Drag the desired buttons into one of the four areas.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id7599414				0	lt	Drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the generated pivot table. The listbox can be used to filter the pivot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the generated pivot table to use another page field as a filter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011	11			0	lt	If the button is dropped in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area it will be given a caption that also shows the formula that will be used to calculate the data.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	16			0	lt	By double-clicking on one of the fields in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area you can call up the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286	17			0	lt	Use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Field\</item\> dialog to select the calculations to be used for the data. To make a multiple selection, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key while clicking the desired calculation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329	13			0	lt	The order of the buttons can be changed at any time by moving them to a different position in the area with the mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	14			0	lt	Remove a button by dragging it back to the area of the other buttons at the right of the dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338	15			0	lt	To open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, double-click one of the buttons in the \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> area. Use the dialog to select if and to what extent \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> calculates display subtotals.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020	18			0	lt	Exit the Pivot Table dialog by pressing OK. A \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button will now be inserted, or a page button for every data field that you dropped in the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area. The pivot table is inserted further down.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Deleting Pivot Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; deleting tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726	31			0	lt	\<variable id=\"datapilot_deletetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_deletetable.xhp\" name=\"Deleting Pivot Tables\"\>Deleting Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014	32			0	lt	In order to delete a pivot table, click any cell in the pivot table, then choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> in the context menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Editing Pivot Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; editing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663	25			0	lt	\<variable id=\"datapilot_edittable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_edittable.xhp\" name=\"Editing Pivot Tables\"\>Editing Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868	26			0	lt	Click one of the buttons in the pivot table and hold the mouse button down. A special symbol will appear next to the mouse pointer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786	27			0	lt	By dragging the button to a different position in the same row you can alter the order of the columns. If you drag a button to the left edge of the table into the row headings area, you can change a column into a row.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id1648915				0	lt	In the Pivot Table dialog, you can drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the pivot table. The listbox can be used to filter the pivot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the pivot table to use another page field as a filter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434	29			0	lt	To remove a button from the table, just drag it out of the pivot table. Release the mouse button when the mouse pointer positioned within the sheet has become a 'not allowed' icon. The button is deleted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442	40			0	lt	To edit the pivot table, click a cell inside the pivot table and open the context menu. In the context menu you find the command \<emph\>Edit Layout\</emph\>, which displays the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog for the current pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id2666096				0	lt	In the pivot table, you can use drag-and-drop or cut/paste commands to rearrange the order of data fields.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id266609688				0	lt	You can assign custom display names to fields, field members, subtotals (with some restrictions), and grand totals inside pivot tables. A custom display name is assigned to an item by overwriting the original name with another name.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Filtering Pivot Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; filtering tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	lt	\<variable id=\"datapilot_filtertable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_filtertable.xhp\" name=\"Filtering Pivot Tables\"\>Filtering Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	lt	You can use filters to remove unwanted data from a pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150441				0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button in the sheet to call up the dialog for the filter conditions. Alternatively, call up the context menu of the pivot table and select the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> command. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090103.xhp\" name=\"Filter\"\>\<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears. Here you can filter the pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id315044199				0	lt	You can also click the arrow on a button in the pivot table to show a pop-up window. In this pop-up window, you can edit the visibility settings of the associated field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344485				0	lt	The pop-up window displays a list of field members associated with that field. A check box is placed to the left of each field member name. When a field has an alternative display name that differs from its original name, that name is displayed in the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344449				0	lt	Enable or disable a checkbox to show or hide the associated field member in the pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344493				0	lt	Enable or disable the \<emph\>All\</emph\> checkbox to show all or none of the field members.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344431				0	lt	Select a field member in the pop-up window and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Show only the current item\</item\> button to show only the selected field member. All other field members are hidden in the pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344484				0	lt	Select a field member in the pop-up window and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide only the current item\</item\> button to hide only the selected field member. All other field members are shown in the pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344578				0	lt	Commands enable you to sort the field members in ascending order, descending order, or using a custom sort list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344584				0	lt	To edit the custom sort lists, open \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344811				0	lt	The arrow to open the pop-up window is normally black. When the field contains one or more hidden field members, the arrow is blue and displays a tiny square at its lower-right corner.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344884				0	lt	You can also open the pop-up window by positioning the cell cursor at the button and pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+D.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Grouping Pivot Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	bm_id4195684				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function;grouping table entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping entries in pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	lt	\<variable id=\"datapilot_grouping\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_grouping.xhp\"\>Grouping Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10661				0	lt	The resulting pivot table can contain many different entries. By grouping the entries, you can improve the visible result.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	lt	Select a cell or range of cells in the pivot table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Group\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	lt	Depending on the format of the selected cells, either a new group field is added to the pivot table, or you see one of the two \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090400.xhp\"\>Grouping\</link\> dialogs, either for numeric values, or for date values.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_id3328653				0	lt	The pivot table must be organized in a way that grouping can be applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	lt	To remove a grouping, click inside the group, then choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Ungroup\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; preventing data overwriting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>output ranges of pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663	19			0	lt	\<variable id=\"datapilot_tipps\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_tipps.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\"\>Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123	20			0	lt	Click the button \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog. The dialog will be extended.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771	21			0	lt	You can select a named range in which the pivot table is to be created, from the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. If the results range does not have a name, enter the coordinates of the upper left cell of the range into the field to the right of the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. You can also click on the appropriate cell to have the coordinates entered accordingly.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	23			0	lt	If you mark the \<emph\>Ignore empty rows\</emph\> check box, they will not be taken into account when the pivot table is created.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273	24			0	lt	If the \<emph\>Identify categories\</emph\> check box is marked, the categories will be identified by their headings and assigned accordingly when the pivot table is created.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Updating Pivot Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; refreshing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recalculating;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	33			0	lt	\<variable id=\"datapilot_updatetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_updatetable.xhp\" name=\"Updating Pivot Tables\"\>Updating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684	34			0	lt	If the data of the source sheet has been changed, $[officename] recalculates the pivot table. To recalculate the table, choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Refresh\</emph\>. Do the same after you have imported an Excel pivot table into $[officename] Calc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Importing and Exporting dBASE Files 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id1226844				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;spreadsheets to dBASE\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dBASE import/export\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; importing from/exporting to dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;importing dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10738				0	lt	\<variable id=\"dbase_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/dbase_files.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting dBASE Files\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	lt	You can open and save data in the dBASE file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, a dBASE database is a folder that contains files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulas and formatting are lost when you open and save a dBASE file from %PRODUCTNAME.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10759				0	lt	To Import a dBASE File Into a Spreadsheet				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071F				0	lt	Locate the *.dbf file that you want to import. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	lt	The \<emph\>Import dBASE files\</emph\> dialog opens.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	lt	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	lt	The dBASE file opens as a new Calc spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074E				0	lt	If you want to save the spreadsheet as a dBASE file, do not alter or delete the first row in the imported file. This row contains information that is required by a dBASE database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	lt	To Import a dBASE File Into a Database Table				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	lt	A %PRODUCTNAME Base database table is actually a link to an existing database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10796				0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - New - Database\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	lt	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialog, enter a name for the database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10792				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079A				0	lt	In the \<emph\>Database type \</emph\>box of the \<emph\>Database Properties\</emph\> dialog, select "dBASE".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A6				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AE				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B6				0	lt	Locate the directory that contains the dBASE file, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F1				0	lt	To Save a Spreadsheet as a dBASE File				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10800				0	lt	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> box, select "dBASE file".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	lt	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, type a name for the dBASE file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10801				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10808				0	lt	Only the data on the current sheet is exported.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Selecting Themes for Sheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>theme selection for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>layout;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791	6			0	lt	\<variable id=\"design\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/design.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Themes for Sheets\"\>Selecting Themes for Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786	13			0	lt	$[officename] Calc comes with a predefined set of formatting themes that you can apply to your spreadsheets.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	16			0	lt	It is not possible to add themes to Calc, and they cannot be modified. However, you can modify their styles after you apply them to a spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757	17			0	lt	Before you format a sheet with a theme, you have to apply at least one custom cell style to the cells on the sheet. You can then change the cell formatting by selecting and applying a theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	18			0	lt	To apply a custom cell style to a cell, you can open the Styles and Formatting window and, in its lower list box, set the Custom Styles view. A list of the existing custom defined cell styles will be displayed. Double click a name from the Styles and Formatting window to apply this style to the selected cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963	19			0	lt	To apply a theme to a spreadsheet:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	15			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Choose Themes\</emph\> icon in the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> bar. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488	20			0	lt	The \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog appears. This dialog lists the available themes for the whole spreadsheet and the Styles and Formatting window lists the custom styles for specific cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	9			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Theme Selection \</emph\>dialog, select the theme that you want to apply to the spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090	21			0	lt	Click OK				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150201	22			0	lt	As soon as you select another theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog, some of the properties of the custom style will be applied to the current spreadsheet. The modifications will be immediately visible in your spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146979	12			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/02/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Theme selection\"\>Theme selection\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Copying to Multiple Sheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>copying;values, to multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;values in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;inserting in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>sheets; simultaneous multiple filling\</bookmark_value\> 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	3			0	lt	\<variable id=\"edit_multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/edit_multitables.xhp\" name=\"Copying to Multiple Sheets\"\>Copying to Multiple Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868	6			0	lt	In $[officename] Calc, you can insert values, text or formulas that are simultaneously copied to other selected sheets of your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768	8			0	lt	Select all desired sheets by holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key and clicking the corresponding register tabs that are still gray at the bottom margin of the workspace. All selected register tabs are now white.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	lt	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435	7			0	lt	Now when you insert values, text or formulas into the active sheet, they will also appear in the identical positions in the other selected sheets. For example, data entered in cell A1 of the active sheet is automatically entered into cell A1 of any other seleted sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Applying Filters				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153896				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>filters; applying/removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows;removing/redisplaying with filters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;filters\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896	70			0	lt	\<variable id=\"filters\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/filters.xhp\" name=\"Applying Filters\"\>Applying Filters\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869	2			0	lt	Filters and advanced filters allow you to work on certain filtered rows (records) of a data range. In the spreadsheets in $[officename] there are various possibilities for applying filters.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131	3			0	lt	One use for the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function is to quickly restrict the display to records with identical entries in a data field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119	4			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialog, you can also define ranges which contain the values in particular data fields. You can use the standard filter to connect the conditions with either a logical AND or a logical OR operator.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010	5			0	lt	The \<emph\>Advanced filter\</emph\> allows up to a total of eight filter conditions. With advanced filters you enter the conditions directly into the sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id9384746				0	lt	To remove a filter, so that you see all cells again, click inside the area where the filter was applied, then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	lt	When you select multiple rows from an area where a filter was applied, then this selection can include rows that are visible and rows that are hidden by the filter. If you then apply formatting, or delete the selected rows, this action then applies only to the visible rows. The hidden rows are not affected. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id218817				0	lt	This is the opposite to rows that you have hidden manually by the \<emph\>Format - Rows - Hide Rows\</emph\> command. Manually hidden rows are deleted when you delete a selection that contains them.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Finding and Replacing in Calc				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id3769341				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding;formulas/values/text/objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing; cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;multiple cell texts\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149204				0	lt	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Calc\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9363689				0	lt	In spreadsheet documents you can find words, formulas, and styles. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all matching cells at once, then apply another format or replace the cell content by other content.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3610644				0	lt	The Find & Replace dialog				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	lt	Cells can contain text or numbers that were entered directly as in a text document. But cells can also contain text or numbers as the result of a calculation. For example, if a cell contains the formula =1+2 it displays the result 3. You must decide whether to search for the 1 respective 2, or to search the 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2423780				0	lt	To find formulas or values				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	lt	You can specify in the Find & Replace dialog either to find the parts of a formula or the results of a calculation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	lt	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	lt	Select "Formulas" or "Values" in the \<emph\>Search in\</emph\> list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	lt	With "Formulas" you will find all parts of the formulas. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	lt	With "Values" you will find the results of the calculations. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	lt	Cell contents can be formatted in different ways. For example, a number can be formatted as a currency, to be displayed with a currency symbol. You see the currency symbol in the cell, but you cannot search for it.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id7359233				0	lt	Finding text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	lt	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	lt	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	lt	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Calc will select the next cell that contains your text. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found cell. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	lt	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F) to find the next cell without opening the dialog. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	lt	By default, Calc searches the current sheet. Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\>, then enable \<emph\>Search in all sheets\</emph\> to search through all sheets of the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	lt	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Calc selects all cells that contain your entry. Now you can for example set all found cells to bold, or apply a Cell Style to all at once.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8531449				0	lt	The Navigator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>View - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	lt	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	lt	Use the Navigator for inserting objects and links within the same document or from other open documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Formatting Spreadsheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154125				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; formatting options for selected cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies;formats\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154125	6			0	lt	\<variable id=\"format_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\" name=\"Designing Spreadsheets\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153912	13			0	lt	Formatting Text in a Spreadsheet 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3144772	14			0	lt	Select the text you want to format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155268	15			0	lt	Choose the desired text attributes from the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. You can also choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog will appear in which you can choose various text attributes on the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149899	16			0	lt	Formatting Numbers in a Spreadsheet				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226	17			0	lt	Select the cells containing the numbers you want to format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046	18			0	lt	To format numbers in the default currency format or as percentages, use the icons on the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. For other formats, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. You can choose from the preset formats or define your own on the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153483	19			0	lt	Formatting Borders and Backgrounds for Cells and Pages				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733	20			0	lt	You can assign a format to any group of cells by first selecting the cells (for multiple selection, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key when clicking), and then activating the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cell\</item\>. In this dialog, you can select attributes such as shadows and backgrounds.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116	21			0	lt	To apply formatting attributes to an entire sheet, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>. You can define headers and footers, for example, to appear on each printed page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389	22			0	lt	An image that you have loaded with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Background\</item\> is only visible in print or in the page preview. To display a background image on screen as well, insert the graphic image by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Picture - From File\</item\> and arrange the image behind the cells by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Arrange - To Background\</item\>. Use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> to select the background image.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2837916				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\"\>Number Formatting Options\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2614215				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\"\>Backgrounds for Cells\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Formatting Numbers With Decimals				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145367				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;formatting decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers in tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults; number formats in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places;formatting numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers with decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;adding/deleting decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats; adding/deleting decimal places in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places; adding/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367	4			0	lt	\<variable id=\"format_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers With Decimals\"\>Formatting Numbers With Decimals\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576	5			0	lt	Enter a number into the sheet, for example, 1234.5678. This number will be displayed in the default number format, with two decimal places. You will see 1234.57 when you confirm the entry. Only the display in the document will be rounded off; internally, the number retains all four decimal places after the decimal point.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012	12			0	lt	To format numbers with decimals:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394	6			0	lt	Set the cursor at the number and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> to start the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157	9			0	lt	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab you will see a selection of predefined number formats. In the bottom right in the dialog you will see a preview of how your current number would look if you were to give it a particular format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3149021\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_numberformatincdecimals.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149021\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3149256	10			0	lt	If you only want to modify the number of the decimal places displayed, the easiest method is to use the \<emph\>Number Format: Add Decimal Place\</emph\> or \<emph\>Number Format: Delete Decimal Place\</emph\> icons on the Formatting Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	User-defined Number Formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143268				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;user-defined formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; user-defined numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats; millions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>format codes; user-defined number formats\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143268	26			0	lt	\<variable id=\"format_value_userdef\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value_userdef.xhp\" name=\"User-defined Number Formats\"\>User-defined Number Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400	1			0	lt	You can define your own number formats to display numbers in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767	2			0	lt	As an example, to display the number 10,200,000 as 10.2 Million:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868	3			0	lt	Select the cells to which you want to apply a new, user-defined format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	4			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	5			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Categories\</emph\> list box select "User-defined".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646	6			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> text box enter the following code:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596	7			0	lt	0.0,, "Million"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764	8			0	lt	Click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417	9			0	lt	The following table shows the effects of rounding, thousands delimiters (,), decimal delimiters (.) and the placeholders # and 0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971	10			0	lt	Number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757	11			0	lt	.#,, "Million"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338	12			0	lt	0.0,, "Million"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	13			0	lt	#,, "Million"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147344	14			0	lt	10200000				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147003	15			0	lt	10.2 Million				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426	16			0	lt	10.2 Million				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155113	17			0	lt	10 Million				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369	18			0	lt	500000				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3145585	19			0	lt	.5 Million				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486	20			0	lt	0.5 Million				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146114	21			0	lt	1 Million				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155810	22			0	lt	100000000				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818	23			0	lt	100. Million				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241	24			0	lt	100.0 Million				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3144771	25			0	lt	100 Million				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Copying Formulas				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151113				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151113	54			0	lt	\<variable id=\"formula_copy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_copy.xhp\" name=\"Copying Formulas\"\>Copying Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424	11			0	lt	There are various ways to copy a formula. One suggested method is:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439	30			0	lt	Select the cell containing the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319	31			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy it.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155	32			0	lt	Select the cell into which you want the formula to be copied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728	33			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V. The formula will be positioned in the new cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961	34			0	lt	If you want to copy a formula into multiple cells, there is a quick and easy way to copy into adjacent cell areas:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400	12			0	lt	Select the cell containing the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018	13			0	lt	Position the mouse on the bottom right of the highlighted border of the cell, and continue holding down the mouse button until the pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749	14			0	lt	With the mouse button pressed, drag it down or to the right over all the cells into which you want to copy the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	15			0	lt	When you release the mouse button, the formula will be copied into the cells and automatically adjusted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385	53			0	lt	If you do not want values and texts to be automatically adjusted, then hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key when dragging. Formulas, however, are always adjusted accordingly.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Entering Formulas 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>formula bar; input line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>input line in formula bar\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; inputting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868	9			0	lt	\<variable id=\"formula_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Formulas\"\>Entering Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6848353				0	lt	You can enter formulas in several ways: using the icons, or by typing on the keyboard, or by a mixture of both methods.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364	10			0	lt	Click the cell in which you want to enter the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012	11			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> icon on the Formula Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441	12			0	lt	You will now see an equals sign in the input line and you can begin to input the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	3			0	lt	After entering the required values, press Enter or click \<emph\>Accept\</emph\> to insert the result in the active cell. If you want to clear your entry in the input line, press Escape or click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394	8			0	lt	You can also enter the values and the formulas directly into the cells, even if you cannot see an input cursor. Formulas must always begin with an equals sign.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id4206976				0	lt	You can also press the + or - key on the numerical keyboard to start a formula. NumLock must be "on". For example, press the following keys in succession:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	lt	+ 5 0 - 8 Enter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8171330				0	lt	You see the result \<item type=\"literal\"\>42\</item\> in the cell. The cell contains the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=+50-8\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	6			0	lt	If you are editing a formula with references, the references and the associated cells will be highlighted with the same color. You can now resize the reference border using the mouse, and the reference in the formula displayed in the input line also changes. \<emph\>Show references in color\</emph\> can be deactivated under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060300.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210	7			0	lt	\<variable id=\"tip\"\>If you would like to view the calculation of individual elements of a formula, select the respective elements and press F9. For example, in the formula =SUM(A1:B12)*SUM(C1:D12) select the section SUM(C1:D12) and press F9 to view the subtotal for this area. \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304	5			0	lt	If an error occurs when creating the formula, an \<link href=\"text/scalc/05/02140000.xhp\" name=\"error message\"\>error message\</link\> appears in the active cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993	13			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Formula bar\"\>Formula bar\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Displaying Formulas or Values				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153195				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; displaying in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values; displaying in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; displaying formulas/values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>results display vs. formulas display\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying; formulas instead of results\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153195	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"formula_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_value.xhp\" name=\"Displaying Formulas or Values\"\>Displaying Formulas or Values\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010	2			0	lt	If you want to display the formulas in the cells, for example in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116	3			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120	4			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Display\</emph\> area mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> box. Click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396	5			0	lt	If you want to view the calculation results instead of the formula, do not mark the Formulas box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157	6			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Calculating With Formulas				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>formulas;calculating with\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; with formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;formula calculation\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411	20			0	lt	\<variable id=\"formulas\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formulas.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Formulas\"\>Calculating With Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281	21			0	lt	All formulas begin with an equals sign. The formulas can contain numbers, text, arithmetic operators, logic operators, or functions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272	39			0	lt	Remember that the basic arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /) can be used in formulas using the "Multiplication and Division before Addition and Subtraction" rule. Instead of writing =SUM(A1:B1) you can write =A1+B1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119	42			0	lt	Parentheses can also be used. The result of the formula =(1+2)*3 produces a different result than =1+2*3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156285	23			0	lt	Here are a few examples of $[officename] Calc formulas:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015	24			0	lt	=A1+10				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972	25			0	lt	Displays the contents of cell A1 plus 10.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643	45			0	lt	=A1*16%				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255	46			0	lt	Displays 16% of the contents of A1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146917	47			0	lt	=A1 * A2				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146315	48			0	lt	Displays the result of the multiplication of A1 and A2.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022	26			0	lt	=ROUND(A1;1)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363	27			0	lt	Displays the contents of cell A1 rounded to one decimal place.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150209	28			0	lt	=EFFECTIVE(5%;12)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883	29			0	lt	Calculates the effective interest for 5% annual nominal interest with 12 payments a year.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146114	33			0	lt	=B8-SUM(B10:B14)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486	34			0	lt	Calculates B8 minus the sum of the cells B10 to B14.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152890	35			0	lt	=SUM(B8;SUM(B10:B14))				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171	36			0	lt	Calculates the sum of cells B10 to B14 and adds the value to B8.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109	30			0	lt	It is also possible to nest functions in formulas, as shown in the example. You can also nest functions within functions. The Function Wizard assists you with nested functions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213	44			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060100.xhp\" name=\"Functions list\"\>Functions list\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869	43			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"AutoPilot: Functions\"\>Function Wizard\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Entering Fractions 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>fractions; entering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; entering fractions \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;fractions\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411	41			0	lt	\<variable id=\"fraction_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/fraction_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Fractions \"\>Entering Fractions \</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968	40			0	lt	You can enter a fractional number in a cell and use it for calculation:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133	42			0	lt	Enter "0 1/5" in a cell (without the quotation marks) and press the input key. In the input line above the spreadsheet you will see the value 0.2, which is used for the calculation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	43			0	lt	If you enter "0 1/2" AutoCorrect causes the three characters 1, / and 2 to be replaced by a single character. The same applies to 1/4 and 3/4. This replacement is defined in \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - Options\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367	44			0	lt	If you want to see multi-digit fractions such as "1/10", you must change the cell format to the multi-digit fraction view. Open the context menu of the cell, and choose \<emph\>Format cells. \</emph\>Select "Fraction" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, and then select "-1234 10/81". You can then enter fractions such as 12/31 or 12/32 - the fractions are, however, automatically reduced, so that in the last example you would see 3/8.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Applying Goal Seek				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>goal seeking;example\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>equations in goal seek\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;variables in equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables;calculating equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;goal seek\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068	22			0	lt	\<variable id=\"goalseek\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/goalseek.xhp\" name=\"Applying Goal Seek\"\>Applying Goal Seek\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171	2			0	lt	With the help of Goal Seek you can calculate a value that, as part of a formula, leads to the result you specify for the formula. You thus define the formula with several fixed values and one variable value and the result of the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153966	14			0	lt	Goal Seek Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150871	4			0	lt	To calculate annual interest (I), create a table with the values for the capital (C), number of years (n), and interest rate (i). The formula is:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596	5			0	lt	I = C * n* i				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	15			0	lt	Let us assume that the interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> of 7.5% and the number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\> (1) will remain constant. However, you want to know how much the investment capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would have to be modified in order to attain a particular return \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>. For this example, calculate how much capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would be required if you want an annual return of $15,000.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960	6			0	lt	Enter each of the values for Capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> (an arbitrary value like \<item type=\"literal\"\>$100,000\</item\>), number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n \</item\>(\<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>), and interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> (\<item type=\"literal\"\>7.5%\</item\>) in one cell each. Enter the formula to calculate the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\> in another cell. Instead of \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\"\>reference to the cell\</link\> with the corresponding value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001	16			0	lt	Place the cursor in the cell containing the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>, and choose \<emph\>Tools - Goal Seek\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Goal Seek\</emph\> dialog appears.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088	17			0	lt	The correct cell is already entered in the field \<emph\>Formula Cell\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426	18			0	lt	Place the cursor in the field \<emph\>Variable Cell\</emph\>. In the sheet, click in the cell that contains the value to be changed, in this example it is the cell with the capital value \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369	19			0	lt	Enter the expected result of the formula in the \<emph\>Target Value\</emph\> text box. In this example, the value is 15,000. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978	20			0	lt	A dialog appears informing you that the Goal Seek was successful. Click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> to enter the result in the cell with the variable value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409	23			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Goal Seek\"\>Goal Seek\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150542				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150542	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"html_doc\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/html_doc.xhp\" name=\"Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\"\>Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154124	2			0	lt	Saving Sheets in HTML				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785	3			0	lt	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc saves all the sheets of a Calc document together as an HTML document. At the beginning of the HTML document, a heading and a list of hyperlinks are automatically added which lead to the individual sheets within the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854	4			0	lt	Numbers are shown as written. In addition, in the <SDVAL> HTML tag, the exact internal number value is written so that after opening the HTML document with \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you know you have the exact values.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188	5			0	lt	To save the current Calc document as HTML, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645	6			0	lt	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> list box, in the area with the other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc filters, choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729	7			0	lt	Enter a \<emph\>File name\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149379	8			0	lt	Opening Sheets in HTML				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959	10			0	lt	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> offers various filters for opening HTML files, which you can select under \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Files of type\</emph\> list box:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	15			0	lt	Choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	16			0	lt	All \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc options are now available to you. However, not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc offers for editing can be saved in HTML format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370	17			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199	18			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"File - Save As\"\>File - Save As\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Entering a Number with Leading Zeros				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147560				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>zero values; entering leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>integers with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; changing text/number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; changing text/number\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; changing to numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text with leading zeros, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147560	67			0	lt	\<variable id=\"integer_leading_zero\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/integer_leading_zero.xhp\" name=\"Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\"\>Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194	55			0	lt	There are various ways to enter integers starting with a zero:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119	56			0	lt	Enter the number as text. The easiest way is to enter the number starting with an apostrophe (for example, \<item type=\"input\"\>'0987\</item\>). The apostrophe will not appear in the cell, and the number will be formatted as text. Because it is in text format, however, you cannot calculate with this number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013	57			0	lt	Format a cell with a number format such as \<item type=\"input\"\>\\0000\</item\>. This format can be assigned in the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> field under the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\> tab, and defines the cell display as "always put a zero first and then the integer, having at least three places, and filled with zeros at the left if less than three digits".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158	58			0	lt	If you want to apply a numerical format to a column of numbers in text format (for example, text "000123" becomes number "123"), do the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377	59			0	lt	Select the column in which the digits are found in text format. Set the cell format in that column as "Number".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	60			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	61			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>^[0-9]\</item\>               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	62			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>&\</item\>               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018	63			0	lt	Check \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	64			0	lt	Check \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	65			0	lt	Click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>               				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145120				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; %PRODUCTNAME Calc shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys;%PRODUCTNAME Calc accessibility\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145120	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)\"\>Shortcut Keys (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760	13			0	lt	Refer also to the lists of shortcut keys for \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> in general.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360	12			0	lt	Cell Selection Mode				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3150439\" src=\"formula/res/refinp1.png\" width=\"0.1327inch\" height=\"0.1327inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150439\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319	11			0	lt	In a text box that has a button to minimize the dialog, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> to enter the cell selection mode. Select any number of cells, then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> again to show the dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272	10			0	lt	In the cell selection mode, you can use the common navigation keys to select cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148646	14			0	lt	Controlling the Outline				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120	15			0	lt	You can use the keyboard in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Outline\"\>Outline\</link\>:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394	16			0	lt	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F6\</item\> until the vertical or horizontal outline window has the focus.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379	17			0	lt	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons from top to bottom or from left to right.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286	18			0	lt	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons in the opposite direction.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149403	19			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+1 to Command+8\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+8\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - show all levels up to the specified number; hide all higher levels.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329	20			0	lt	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>+\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>-\</item\> to show or hide the focused outline group.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	21			0	lt	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> to activate the focused button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253	22			0	lt	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\>, or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow to cycle through all buttons in the current level.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147343	8			0	lt	Selecting a Drawing Object or a Graphic				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AA				0	lt	Choose View - Toolbars - Drawing to open the Drawing toolbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333	7			0	lt	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> until the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar is selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345	4			0	lt	If the selection tool is active, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter. This selects the first drawing object or graphic in the sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159240	3			0	lt	With \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 you set the focus to the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379	2			0	lt	Now you can use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to select the next drawing object or graphic and \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> to select the previous one.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154684				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>tables; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>freezing rows or columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scrolling prevention in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows; splitting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; splitting windows\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"line_fix\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/line_fix.xhp\" name=\"Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\"\>Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576	2			0	lt	If you have long rows or columns of data that extend beyond the viewable area of the sheet, you can freeze some rows or columns, which allows you to see the frozen columns or rows as you scroll through the rest of the data.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441	3			0	lt	Select the row below, or the column to the right of the row or column that you want to be in the frozen region. All rows above, or all columns to the left of the selection are frozen.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158	13			0	lt	To freeze both horizontally and vertically, select the \<emph\>cell\</emph\> that is below the row and to the right of the column that you want to freeze.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286	4			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	5			0	lt	To deactivate, choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze \</emph\>again.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	7			0	lt	If the area defined is to be scrollable, apply the \<emph\>Window - Split\</emph\> command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345	8			0	lt	If you want to print a certain row on all pages of a document, choose \<emph\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004	9			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Freeze\"\>Window - Freeze\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088	10			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Split\"\>Window - Split\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304	11			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
