helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Selecting Multiple Cells				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>cells; selecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>marking cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple cells selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selection modes in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; selecting ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"mark_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/mark_cells.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Multiple Cells\"\>Selecting Multiple Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272	2			0	lt	Select a rectangular range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149261	3			0	lt	With the mouse button pressed, drag from one corner to the diagonally opposed corner of the range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119	4			0	lt	Mark a single cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	19			0	lt	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710	20			0	lt	Click, then Shift-click the cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959	5			0	lt	Pressing the mouse button, drag a range across two cells, do not release the mouse button, and then drag back to the first cell. Release the mouse button. You can now move the individual cell by drag and drop.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154942	6			0	lt	Select various dispersed cells				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072060				0	lt	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284	7			0	lt	Mark at least one cell. Then while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, click each of the additional cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072023				0	lt	Click the STD / EXT / ADD area in the status bar until it shows ADD. Now click all cells that you want to select.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971	8			0	lt	Switch marking mode				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064	9			0	lt	On the status bar, click the box with the legend STD / EXT / ADD to switch the marking mode:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264	10			0	lt	Field contents				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337	11			0	lt	Effect of clicking the mouse				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568	12			0	lt	STD				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3148486	13			0	lt	A mouse click selects the cell you have clicked on. Unmarks all marked cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090	14			0	lt	EXT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150305	15			0	lt	A mouse click marks a rectangular range from the current cell to the cell you clicked. Alternatively, Shift-click a cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587	16			0	lt	ADD				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368	17			0	lt	A mouse click in a cell adds it to the already marked cells. A mouse click in a marked cell unmarks it. Alternatively, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click the cells.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487	18			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0208.xhp\" name=\"Status bar\"\>Status bar\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Entering Matrix Formulas				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153969				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>matrices; entering matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153969	13			0	lt	\<variable id=\"matrixformula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/matrixformula.xhp\" name=\"Entering Matrix Formulas\"\>Entering Matrix Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144	14			0	lt	The following is an example of how you can enter a matrix formula, without going into the details of matrix functions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188	15			0	lt	Assume you have entered 10 numbers in Columns A and B (A1:A10 and B1:B10), and would like to calculate the sum of each row in Column C.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321	16			0	lt	Using the mouse, select the range C1:C10, in which the results are to be displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	17			0	lt	Press F2, or click in the input line of the Formula bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	18			0	lt	Enter an equal sign (=).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252	19			0	lt	Select the range A1:A10, which contains the first values for the sum formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767	20			0	lt	Press the (+) key from the numerical keypad.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018	21			0	lt	Select the numbers in the second column in cells B1:B10.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716	22			0	lt	End the input with the matrix key combination: Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640	23			0	lt	The matrix area is automatically protected against modifications, such as deleting rows or columns. It is, however, possible to edit any formatting, such as the cell background.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155686				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; moving cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; moving by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;moving by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;cells by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cells, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id986358				0	lt	\<variable id=\"move_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/move_dragdrop.xhp\"\>Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2760093				0	lt	When you drag-and-drop a selection of cells on a Calc sheet, the cells normally overwrite the existing cells in the area where you drop. This is the normal \<emph\>overwrite mode\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9527268				0	lt	When you hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while releasing the mouse button, you enter the \<emph\>insert mode\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id79653				0	lt	In insert mode, the existing cells where you drop will be shifted to the right or to the bottom, and the dropped cells are inserted into the now empty positions without overwriting. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8676717				0	lt	The surrounding box of the moved cells looks different in insert mode. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3968932				0	lt	In overwrite mode you see all four borders around the selected area. In insert mode you see only the left border when target cells will be shifted to the right. You see only the upper border when target cells will be shifted down. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id7399517				0	lt	Whether the target area will be shifted to the right or to the bottom depends on the distance between source and target cells, if you move within the same sheet. It depends on the number of horizontal or vertical cells in the moved area, if you move to a different sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8040406				0	lt	If you move cells in insert mode within the same row (only horizontally), then after insertion of the cells, all cells will be shifted to the left to fill the source area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2586748				0	lt	In both modes, you can hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key, or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys while you release the mouse button to insert a copy or a link, respectively.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5814081				0	lt	Keys pressed while releasing the mouse button				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6581316				0	lt	Result				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9906613				0	lt	No key				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2815637				0	lt	Cells are moved and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells are emptied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6161687				0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4278389				0	lt	Cells are copied and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2805566				0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5369121				0	lt	Links to the source cells are inserted and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9518723				0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	lt	Cells are moved and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells are emptied, except if you move within the same rows on the same sheet. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4021423				0	lt	If you move within the same rows on the same sheet, the cells in the target area shift to the right, and then the whole row shifts to fill the source area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2783898				0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>keys				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2785119				0	lt	Cells are copied and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id584124				0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5590990				0	lt	Links to the source cells are inserted and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Navigating Through Sheets Tabs				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; showing multiple\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769	4			0	lt	\<variable id=\"multi_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multi_tables.xhp\" name=\"Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\"\>Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771	3			0	lt	By default $[officename] displays three sheets "Sheet1" to "Sheet3", in each new spreadsheet. You can switch between sheets in a spreadsheet using the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	lt	 \<image id=\"img_id4829822\" src=\"res/helpimg/sheettabs.png\" width=\"3.3335inch\" height=\"0.7638inch\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4829822\"\>Sheet Tabs\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	lt	 \<image id=\"img_id3156441\" src=\"res/helpimg/calcnav.png\" width=\"0.6563inch\" height=\"0.1457inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156441\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396	5			0	lt	Use the navigation buttons to display all the sheets belonging to your document. Clicking the button on the far left or the far right displays, respectively, the first or last sheet tab. The middle buttons allow the user to scroll forward and backward through all sheet tabs. To display the sheet itself click on the sheet tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379	6			0	lt	If there is insufficient space to display all the sheet tabs, you can increase it by pointing to the separator between the scrollbar and the sheet tabs, pressing the mouse button and, keeping the mouse button pressed, dragging to the right. In doing so you will be sharing the available space between the sheet tabs and horizontal scrollbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Applying Multiple Operations				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147559				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>multiple operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>what if operations;two variables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-classified tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559	5			0	lt	\<variable id=\"multioperation\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multioperation.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Operations\"\>Applying Multiple Operations\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171	1			0	lt	Multiple Operations in Columns or Rows				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id4123966				0	lt	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Multiple Operations\</item\> command provides a planning tool for "what if" questions. In your spreadsheet, you enter a formula to calculate a result from values that are stored in other cells. Then, you set up a cell range where you enter some fixed values, and the Multiple Operations command will calculate the results depending on the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424	2			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the formula that applies to the data range. In the \<emph\>Column input cell/Row input cell\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the corresponding cell that is part of the formula. This can be explained best by examples:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153	7			0	lt	Examples				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189	8			0	lt	You produce toys which you sell for $10 each. Each toy costs $2 to make, in addition to which you have fixed costs of $10,000 per year. How much profit will you make in a year if you sell a particular number of toys?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id6478774				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id1621753\" src=\"res/helpimg/what-if.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1621753\"\>what-if sheet area\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145239	41			0	lt	Calculating With One Formula and One Variable				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146888	42			0	lt	To calculate the profit, first enter any number as the quantity (items sold) - in this example 2000. The profit is found from the formula Profit=Quantity * (Selling price - Direct costs) - Fixed costs. Enter this formula in B5.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875	43			0	lt	In column D enter given annual sales, one below the other; for example, 500 to 5000, in steps of 500.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3159115	44			0	lt	Select the range D2:E11, and thus the values in column D and the empty cells alongside in column E.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149723	45			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple operations\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149149	46			0	lt	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas \</emph\>field, click cell B5.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355	47			0	lt	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the variable in the formula, which is replaced by the selected column values.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149009	48			0	lt	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You see the profits for the different quantities in column E.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148725	49			0	lt	Calculating with Several Formulas Simultaneously				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880	50			0	lt	Delete column E.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154675	51			0	lt	Enter the following formula in C5: = B5 / B4. You are now calculating the annual profit per item sold.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148885	52			0	lt	Select the range D2:F11, thus three columns.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3147474	53			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154846	54			0	lt	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, select cells B5 thru C5.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931	55			0	lt	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B4.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3150862	56			0	lt	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will now see the profits in column E and the annual profit per item in column F.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139	3			0	lt	Multiple Operations Across Rows and Columns				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148584	4			0	lt	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> allows you to carry out joint multiple operations for columns and rows in so-called cross-tables. The formula cell has to refer to both the data range arranged in rows and the one arranged in columns. Select the range defined by both data ranges and call the multiple operation dialog. Enter the reference to the formula in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field. The \<emph\>Row input cell\</emph\> and the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> fields are used to enter the reference to the corresponding cells of the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149949	57			0	lt	Calculating with Two Variables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154808	58			0	lt	Consider columns A and B of the sample table above. You now want to vary not just the quantity produced annually, but also the selling price, and you are interested in the profit in each case.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149731	59			0	lt	Expand the table shown above. D2 thru D11 contain the numbers 500, 1000 and so on, up to 5000. In E1 through H1 enter the numbers 8, 10, 15 and 20.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3152810	95			0	lt	Select the range D1:H11.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153620	96			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149981	97			0	lt	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, click cell B5.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113	98			0	lt	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Row input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B1. This means that B1, the selling price, is the horizontally entered variable (with the values 8, 10, 15 and 20).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154049	99			0	lt	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click in B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the vertically entered variable.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149141	100			0	lt	Close the dialog with OK. You see the profits for the different selling prices in the range E2:H11.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155104	101			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12060000.xhp\" name=\"Multiple operations\"\>Multiple operations\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Applying Multiple Sheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154759				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; selecting multiple\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>appending sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154759	9			0	lt	\<variable id=\"multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multitables.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Sheets\"\>Applying Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148576	10			0	lt	Inserting a Sheet				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731	4			0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Sheet\</item\> to insert a new sheet or an existing sheet from another file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203598				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog box where you can assign macros to sheet events.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203523				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a window where you can assign a color to the sheet tab.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id050920091402035				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to select all sheets in the document.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914020391				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to deselect all sheets in the document, except the current sheet.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491	11			0	lt	Selecting Multiple Sheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251	6			0	lt	The sheet tab of the current sheet is always visible in white in front of the other sheet tabs. The other sheet tabs are gray when they are not selected. By clicking other sheet tabs while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>you can select multiple sheets.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	lt	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600	12			0	lt	Undoing a Selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	13			0	lt	To undo the selection of a sheet, click its sheet tab again while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key. The sheet that is currently visible cannot be removed from the selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382	15			0	lt	Calculating Across Multiple Sheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333	16			0	lt	You can refer to a range of sheets in a formula by specifying the first and last sheet of the range, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.A1) \</item\>sums up all A1 cells on Sheet1 through Sheet3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Inserting and Editing Comments				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153968				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>comments; on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>remarks on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>displaying; comments\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968	31			0	lt	\<variable id=\"note_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/note_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Comments\"\>Inserting and Editing Comments\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440	32			0	lt	You can assign a comment to each cell by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Comment\</emph\>\</link\>. The comment is indicated by a small red square, the comment indicator, in the cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	34			0	lt	The comment is visible whenever the mouse pointer is over the cell, provided you have activated \<emph\>Help - Tips\</emph\> or - \<emph\>Extended Tips\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575	33			0	lt	When you select the cell, you can choose \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> from the context menu of the cell. Doing so keeps the comment visible until you deactivate the \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> command from the same context menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958	35			0	lt	To edit a permanently visible comment, just click in it. If you delete the entire text of the comment, the comment itself is deleted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	lt	Move or resize each comment as you like.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	lt	Format each comment by specifying background color, transparency, border style, and text alignment. Choose the commands from the context menu of the comment.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764	38			0	lt	To show or hide the comment indicator, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and mark or unmark the \<emph\>Comment indicator\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715	39			0	lt	To display a help tip for a selected cell, use \<emph\>Data - Validity - Input Help\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	36			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>Insert - Comment\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Converting Text to Numbers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>formats; text as numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>time format conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200901265171				0	lt	\<variable id=\"numbers_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/numbers_text.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text to Numbers\"\>Converting Text to Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265127				0	lt	Calc converts text inside cells to the respective numeric values if an unambiguous conversion is possible. If no conversion is possible, Calc returns a #VALUE! error.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265196				0	lt	Only integer numbers including exponent are converted, and ISO 8601 dates and times in their extended formats with separators. Anything else, like fractional numbers with decimal separators or dates other than ISO 8601, is not converted, as the text string would be locale dependent. Leading and trailing blanks are ignored.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265220				0	lt	The following ISO 8601 formats are converted:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265288				0	lt	CCYY-MM-DD				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265267				0	lt	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265248				0	lt	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265374				0	lt	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss,s				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265327				0	lt	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.s				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265399				0	lt	hh:mm				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265347				0	lt	hh:mm:ss				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265349				0	lt	hh:mm:ss,s				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265342				0	lt	hh:mm:ss.s				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265491				0	lt	The century code CC may not be omitted. Instead of the T date and time separator, exactly one space character may be used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265467				0	lt	If a date is given, it must be a valid Gregorian calendar date. In this case the optional time must be in the range 00:00 to 23:59:59.99999...				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265420				0	lt	If only a time string is given, it may have an hours value of more than 24, while minutes and seconds can have a maximum value of 59.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265448				0	lt	The conversion is done for single arguments only, as in =A1+A2, or ="1E2"+1. Cell range arguments are not affected, so SUM(A1:A2) differs from A1+A2 if at least one of the two cells contain a convertible string.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id090820090126540				0	lt	Strings inside formulas are also converted, such as in ="1999-11-22"+42, which returns the date 42 days after November 22nd, 1999. Calculations involving localized dates as strings inside the formula return an error. For example, the localized date string "11/22/1999" or "22.11.1999" cannot be used for the automatic conversion.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id1005200903485368				0	lt	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485359				0	lt	In A1 enter the text \<item type=\"literal\"\>'1e2\</item\> (which is converted to the number 100 internally).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485341				0	lt	In A2 enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A1+1\</item\> (which correctly results in 101).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265544				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Printing Sheet Details				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>printing;sheet details\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing details\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids; printing sheet grids\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; printing, instead of results\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts;printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet grids; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; printing grids\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; printing cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>zero values; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>null values; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;printing\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"print_details\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_details.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheet Details\"\>Printing Sheet Details\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728	2			0	lt	When printing a sheet you can select which details are to be printed:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010	3			0	lt	Row and column headers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013	4			0	lt	Sheet grid				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273	5			0	lt	Comments				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801	6			0	lt	Objects and graphics				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491	7			0	lt	Charts				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731	8			0	lt	Drawing objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400	9			0	lt	Formulas				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752	10			0	lt	To choose the details proceed as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640	11			0	lt	Select the sheet you want to print.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042	12			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340	13			0	lt	The command is not visible if the sheet was opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> Bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	14			0	lt	Select the \<emph\>Sheet\</emph\> tab. In the \<emph\>Print \</emph\>area mark the details to be printed and click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145789	15			0	lt	Print the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345	16			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Defining Number of Pages for Printing				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153194				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page breaks; spreadsheet preview\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>previews;page breaks for printing\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153194	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"print_exact\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_exact.xhp\" name=\"Defining Number of Pages for Printing\"\>Defining Number of Pages for Printing\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771	2			0	lt	If a sheet is too large for a single printed page, $[officename] Calc will print the current sheet evenly divided over several pages. Since the automatic page break does not always take place in the optimal position, you can define the page distribution yourself.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155	3			0	lt	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012	4			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	5			0	lt	You will see the automatic distribution of the sheet across the print pages. The automatically created print ranges are indicated by dark blue lines, and the user-defined ones by light blue lines. The page breaks (line breaks and column breaks) are marked as black lines.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578	6			0	lt	You can move the blue lines with the mouse. You will find further options in the Context menu, including adding an additional print range, removing the scaling and inserting additional manual line and column breaks.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	7			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Printing Sheets in Landscape Format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing in landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing; landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>landscape printing\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"print_landscape\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_landscape.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\"\>Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257	2			0	lt	In order to print a sheet you have a number of interactive options available under \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>. Drag the delimiter lines to define the range of printed cells on each page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963	15			0	lt	To print in landscape format, proceed as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020	3			0	lt	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786	4			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089	5			0	lt	The command is not visible if the sheet has been opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430	6			0	lt	Select the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab. Select the \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\> paper format and click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150885	7			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288	8			0	lt	Depending on the printer driver and the operating system, it may be necessary to click the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button and to change your printer to landscape format there.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404	9			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Print \</emph\>dialog in the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page, select the contents to be printed:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305	10			0	lt	               \<emph\>All sheets\</emph\> - All sheets will be printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148871	12			0	lt	               \<emph\>Selected sheets\</emph\> - Only the selected sheets will be printed. All sheets whose names (at the bottom on the sheet tabs) are selected will be printed. By pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while clicking a sheet name you can change this selection.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3764763				0	lt	               \<emph\>Selected cells\</emph\> - All selected cells are printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id5538804				0	lt	From all the paper pages that result from the above selection, you can select the range of paper pages to be printed:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id14343				0	lt	               \<emph\>All pages\</emph\> - Print all resulting pages.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699	11			0	lt	               \<emph\>Pages\</emph\> - Enter the pages to be printed. The pages will also be numbered from the first sheet onwards. If you see in the Page Break Preview that Sheet1 will be printed on 4 pages and you want to print the first two pages of Sheet2, enter 5-6 here.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3145076	13			0	lt	If under \<emph\>Format - Print ranges\</emph\> you have defined one or more print ranges, only the contents of these print ranges will be printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019	14			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id8254646				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp\"\>Defining Print Ranges on a Sheet\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheets on multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing on multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; repeating when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; repeating when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>repeating;columns/rows on printed pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; printing on all sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; printing on sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers; printing on sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; rows/columns as table headings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headings;repeating rows/columns as\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153727	21			0	lt	\<variable id=\"print_title_row\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_title_row.xhp\" name=\"Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page\"\>Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014	2			0	lt	If you have a sheet that is so large that it will be printed multiple pages, you can set up rows or columns to repeat on each printed page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	7			0	lt	As an example, If you want to print the top two rows of the sheet as well as the first column (A)on all pages, do the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710	8			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Edit\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Edit Print Ranges\</emph\> dialog appears.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958	9			0	lt	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3145800	10			0	lt	The dialog shrinks so that you can see more of the sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602	11			0	lt	Select the first two rows and, for this example, click cell A1 and drag to A2.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018	12			0	lt	In the shrunk dialog you will see $1:$2. Rows 1 and 2 are now rows to repeat.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	13			0	lt	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area. The dialog is restored again.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443	14			0	lt	If you also want column A as a column to repeat, click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256	15			0	lt	Click column A (not in the column header).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704	16			0	lt	Click the icon again at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088	17			0	lt	Rows to repeat are rows from the sheet. You can define headers and footers to be printed on each print page independently of this in \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155380	18			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371	19			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146113	20			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05070000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\"\>Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Using Print Ranges on a Spreadsheet				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	bm_id14648				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PDF export of print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell ranges; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>clearing, see also deleting/removing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extending print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D7				0	lt	\<variable id=\"printranges\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp\"\>Defining Print Ranges on a Sheet\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108F5				0	lt	You can define which range of cells on a spreadsheet to print.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FB				0	lt	The cells on the sheet that are not part of the defined print range are not printed or exported. Sheets without a defined print range are not printed and not exported to a PDF file, unless the document uses the Excel file format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	lt	For files opened in Excel format, all sheets that do not contain a defined print range are printed. The same behavior occurs when you export the Excel formatted spreadsheet to a PDF file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FE				0	lt	To Define a Print Range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	lt	Select the cells that you want to print.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10909				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Define\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10910				0	lt	To Add Cells to a Print Range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10917				0	lt	Select the cells that you want to add to the existing print range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091B				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Add\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10922				0	lt	To Clear a Print Range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10929				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Remove\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10953				0	lt	Using the Page Break Preview to Edit Print Ranges				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093E				0	lt	In the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, print ranges as well as page break regions are outlined by a blue border and contain a centered page number in gray. Nonprinting areas have a gray background.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143	8			0	lt	To define a new page break region, drag the border to a new location. When you define a new page break region, an automatic page break is replaced by a manual page break.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10930				0	lt	To View and Edit Print Ranges				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10937				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082A				0	lt	To change the default zoom factor of the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, double click the percentage value on the \<emph\>Status\</emph\> bar, and select a new zoom factor.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10836				0	lt	Edit the print range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10944				0	lt	To change the size of a print range, drag a border of the range to a new location.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075	12			0	lt	To delete a manual page break that is contained in a print range, drag the border of the page break outside of the print range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10948				0	lt	To clear a print range, drag a border of the range onto the opposite border of the range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	lt	To exit the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CF				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\"\>Editing Print Ranges\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>addressing; relative and absolute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; absolute/relative\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute addresses in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative addresses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute references in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; to cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; references\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423	53			0	lt	\<variable id=\"relativ_absolut_ref\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\" name=\"Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative\"\>Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163712	3			0	lt	Relative Addressing				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119	4			0	lt	The cell in column A, row 1 is addressed as A1. You can address a range of adjacent cells by first entering the coordinates of the upper left cell of the area, then a colon followed by the coordinates of the lower right cell. For example, the square formed by the first four cells in the upper left corner is addressed as A1:B2.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730	5			0	lt	By addressing an area in this way, you are making a relative reference to A1:B2. Relative here means that the reference to this area will be adjusted automatically when you copy the formulas.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377	6			0	lt	Absolute Addressing				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943	7			0	lt	Absolute references are the opposite of relative addressing. A dollar sign is placed before each letter and number in an absolute reference, for example, $A$1:$B$2.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338	36			0	lt	$[officename] can convert the current reference, in which the cursor is positioned in the input line, from relative to absolute and vice versa by pressing Shift +F4. If you start with a relative address such as A1, the first time you press this key combination, both row and column are set to absolute references ($A$1). The second time, only the row (A$1), and the third time, only the column ($A1). If you press the key combination once more, both column and row references are switched back to relative (A1)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963	52			0	lt	$[officename] Calc shows the references to a formula. If, for example you click the formula =SUM(A1:C5;D15:D24) in a cell, the two referenced areas in the sheet will be highlighted in color. For example, the formula component "A1:C5" may be in blue and the cell range in question bordered in the same shade of blue. The next formula component "D15:D24" can be marked in red in the same way.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704	29			0	lt	When to Use Relative and Absolute References				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346	8			0	lt	What distinguishes a relative reference? Assume you want to calculate in cell E1 the sum of the cells in range A1:B2. The formula to enter into E1 would be: =SUM(A1:B2). If you later decide to insert a new column in front of column A, the elements you want to add would then be in B1:C2 and the formula would be in F1, not in E1. After inserting the new column, you would therefore have to check and correct all formulas in the sheet, and possibly in other sheets.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	9			0	lt	Fortunately, $[officename] does this work for you. After having inserted a new column A, the formula =SUM(A1:B2) will be automatically updated to =SUM(B1:C2). Row numbers will also be automatically adjusted when a new row 1 is inserted. Absolute and relative references are always adjusted in $[officename] Calc whenever the referenced area is moved. But be careful if you are copying a formula since in that case only the relative references will be adjusted, not the absolute references.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791	39			0	lt	Absolute references are used when a calculation refers to one specific cell in your sheet. If a formula that refers to exactly this cell is copied relatively to a cell below the original cell, the reference will also be moved down if you did not define the cell coordinates as absolute.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005	10			0	lt	Aside from when new rows and columns are inserted, references can also change when an existing formula referring to particular cells is copied to another area of the sheet. Assume you entered the formula =SUM(A1:A9) in row 10. If you want to calculate the sum for the adjacent column to the right, simply copy this formula to the cell to the right. The copy of the formula in column B will be automatically adjusted to =SUM(B1:B9).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Renaming Sheets				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150398				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>renaming;sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;renaming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;renaming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398	11			0	lt	\<variable id=\"rename_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\" name=\"Renaming Sheets\"\>Renaming Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131	12			0	lt	Click the name of the sheet that you want to change.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976	13			0	lt	Open the context menu and choose the \<emph\>Rename Sheet\</emph\> command. A dialog box appears where you can enter a new name.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	15			0	lt	Enter a new name for the sheet and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667	27			0	lt	Alternatively, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option key\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click on any sheet name and enter the new name directly.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502833				0	lt	Sheet names can contain almost any character. Some naming restrictions apply when you want to save the spreadsheet to Microsoft Excel format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050283				0	lt	When saving to Microsoft Excel format, the following characters are not allowed in sheet names:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050281				0	lt	colon :				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502897				0	lt	back slash \\				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050299				0	lt	forward slash /				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502913				0	lt	question mark ?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050298				0	lt	asterisk *				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502969				0	lt	left square bracket [				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502910				0	lt	right square bracket ]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502971				0	lt	single quote ' as the first or last character of the name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050307				0	lt	In cell references, a sheet name has to be enclosed in single quotes ' if the name contains other characters than alphanumeric or underscore. A single quote contained within a name has to be escaped by doubling it (two single quotes). For example, you want to reference the cell A1 on a sheet with the following name:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503071				0	lt	This year's sheet				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503054				0	lt	The reference must be enclosed in single quotes, and the one single quote inside the name must be doubled:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503069				0	lt	'This year''s sheet'.A1				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155444	16			0	lt	The name of a sheet is independent of the name of the spreadsheet. You enter the spreadsheet name when you save it for the first time as a file. The document can contain up to 256 individual sheets, which can have different names.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Using Rounded Off Numbers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; rounded off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounded off numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exact numbers in $[officename] Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;number of decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values;rounded in calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;rounded off values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>precision as shown\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding precision\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; values as shown\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156422	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"rounding_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rounding_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Using Rounded Off Numbers\"\>Using Rounded Off Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	3			0	lt	In $[officename] Calc, all decimal numbers are displayed rounded off to two decimal places.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596	4			0	lt	To change this for selected cells				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321	5			0	lt	Mark all the cells you want to modify.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428	6			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and go to the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876	7			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, select \<emph\>Number\</emph\>. Under \<emph\>Options\</emph\>, change the number of \<emph\>Decimal places\</emph\> and exit the dialog with OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155415	8			0	lt	To change this everywhere				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715	9			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	10			0	lt	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Modify the number of \<emph\>Decimal places\</emph\> and exit the dialog with OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154755	11			0	lt	To calculate with the rounded off numbers instead of the internal exact values				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150045	12			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	13			0	lt	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Mark the \<emph\>Precision as shown\</emph\> field and exit the dialog with OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790	14			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Numbers\"\>Numbers\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005	15			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\" name=\"Calculate\"\>Calculate\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Changing Row Height or Column Width				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145748				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>heights of cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell heights\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; heights and widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>widths of cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; heights\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;row heights/column widths\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"row_height\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/row_height.xhp\" name=\"Changing Row Height or Column Width\"\>Changing Row Height or Column Width\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017	2			0	lt	You can change the height of the rows with the mouse or through the dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702	3			0	lt	What is described here for rows and row height applies accordingly for columns and column width.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963	4			0	lt	Using the mouse to change the row height or column width				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020	5			0	lt	Click the area of the headers on the separator below the current row, keep the mouse button pressed and drag up or down in order to change the row height.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3159237	6			0	lt	Select the optimal row height by double-clicking the separator below the row.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154659	7			0	lt	Using the dialog to change the row height or column width				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3150367	8			0	lt	Click the row so that you achieve the focus.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3166432	9			0	lt	Start the context menu on the header at the left-hand side.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519	10			0	lt	You will see the commands \<emph\>Row Height\</emph\> and \<emph\>Optimal row height\</emph\>. Choosing either opens a dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487	11			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340100.xhp\" name=\"Row height\"\>Row height\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3149408	12			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Optimal row height\"\>Optimal row height\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305	13			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340200.xhp\" name=\"Column width\"\>Column width\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3153815	14			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05040200.xhp\" name=\"Optimal column width\"\>Optimal column width\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Using Scenarios				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149664				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>scenarios; creating/editing/deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;scenarios\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;scenarios in Navigator\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"scenario\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/scenario.xhp\" name=\"Using Scenarios\"\>Using Scenarios\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869	2			0	lt	A $[officename] Calc scenario is a set of cell values that can be used within your calculations. You assign a name to every scenario on your sheet. Define several scenarios on the same sheet, each with some different values in the cells. Then you can easily switch the sets of cell values by their name and immediately observe the results. Scenarios are a tool to test out "what-if" questions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149255	15			0	lt	Creating Your Own Scenarios				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704	16			0	lt	To create a scenario, select all the cells that provide the data for the scenario. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020	17			0	lt	Select the cells that contain the values that will change between scenarios. To select multiple cells, hold down the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</item\>key as you click each cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150364	18			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Scenarios\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Create Scenario\</emph\> dialog appears.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426	19			0	lt	Enter a name for the new scenario and leave the other fields unchanged with their default values. Close the dialog with OK. Your new scenario is automatically activated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664	3			0	lt	Using Scenarios				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415	11			0	lt	Scenarios can be selected in the Navigator:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752	12			0	lt	Open the Navigator with the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id1593676\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_navigator.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1593676\"\>Navigator icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the Standard bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	13			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Scenarios\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id7617114\" src=\"sc/res/imglst/navipi/na07.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7617114\"\>Scenarios icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the Navigator.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256	14			0	lt	In the Navigator, you see the defined scenarios with the comments that were entered when the scenarios were created.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id1243629				0	lt	Double-click a scenario name in the Navigator to apply that scenario to the current sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id9044770				0	lt	To delete a scenario, right-click the name in the Navigator and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3674123				0	lt	To edit a scenario, right-click the name in the Navigator and choose \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3424481				0	lt	To hide the border of a set of cells that are part of a scenario, open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog for each scenario that affects the cells and clear the Display border checkbox. Hiding the border also removes the listbox on the sheet where you can choose the scenarios.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368	22			0	lt	If you want to know which values in the scenario affect other values, choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Trace Dependents\</emph\>. You see arrows to the cells that are directly dependent on the current cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484	29			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Creating Scenarios\"\>Creating Scenarios\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Applying Sort Lists				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150870				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>filling;customized lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sort lists;applying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>geometric lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arithmetic lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>series;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists; user-defined\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customized lists\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150870	3			0	lt	\<variable id=\"sorted_list\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/sorted_list.xhp\" name=\"Applying Sort Lists\"\>Applying Sort Lists\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154	7			0	lt	Sort lists allow you to type one piece of information in a cell, then drag it to fill in a consecutive list of items.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645	4			0	lt	For example, enter the text "Jan" or "January" in an empty cell. Select the cell and click the mouse on the lower right corner of the cell border. Then drag the selected cell a few cells to the right or downwards. When you release the mouse button, the highlighted cells will be filled with the names of the months.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id2367931				0	lt	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577	5			0	lt	The predefined series can be found under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>. You can also create your own lists of text strings tailored to your needs, such as a list of your company's branch offices. When you use the information in these lists later (for example, as headings), just enter the first name in the list and expand the entry by dragging it with your mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434	6			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Sort lists\"\>Sort lists\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Filter: Applying Advanced Filters				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148798				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>filters;defining advanced filters \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining; advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148798	18			0	lt	\<variable id=\"specialfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/specialfilter.xhp\" name=\"Filter: Applying Advanced Filters\"\>Filter: Applying Advanced Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785	19			0	lt	Copy the column headers of the sheet ranges to be filtered into an empty area of the sheet, and then enter the criteria for the filter in a row beneath the headers. Horizontally arranged data in a row will always be logically connected with AND, and vertically arranged data in a column will always be logically connected with OR.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142	20			0	lt	Once you have created a filter matrix, select the sheet ranges to be filtered. Open the \<emph\>Advanced Filter\</emph\> dialog by choosing \<emph\>Data - Filter - Advanced Filter\</emph\>, and define the filter conditions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	21			0	lt	Then click OK, and you will see that only the rows from the original sheet whose contents have met the search criteria are still visible. All other rows are temporarily hidden and can be made to reappear with the \<emph\>Format - Row - Show \</emph\>command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	22			0	lt	 \<emph\>Example\</emph\> 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427	23			0	lt	Load a spreadsheet with a large number of records. We are using a fictional \<emph\>Turnover\</emph\> document, but you can just as easily use any other document. The document has the following layout:				20130618 17:22:18
