helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149992	138			0	lt	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148400	139			0	lt	TYPE(Value)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150830	140			0	lt	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is a specific value for which the data type is determined. Value 1 = number, value 2 = text, value 4 = Boolean value, value 8 = formula, value 16 = error value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154363	141			0	lt	Example (see example table above)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153357	142			0	lt	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TYPE(C2)\</item\> returns 2 as a result.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148980	143			0	lt	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TYPE(D9)\</item\> returns 1 as a result.				20130618 17:22:18
