helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156041	187			0	lt	Returns the contents of the referenced cell, without any formatting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151069	188			0	lt	TYPE				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155344	189			0	lt	Returns the type of cell contents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145217	190			0	lt	b = blank. empty cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155176	191			0	lt	l = label. Text, result of a formula as text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147280	192			0	lt	v = value. Value, result of a formula as a number				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156348	193			0	lt	WIDTH				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154920	194			0	lt	Returns the width of the referenced column. The unit is the number of zeros (0) that fit into the column in the default text and the default size.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3152355	195			0	lt	PREFIX				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230	196			0	lt	Returns the alignment of the referenced cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155946	197			0	lt	' = align left or left-justified				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147220	198			0	lt	" = align right				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149038	199			0	lt	^ = centered				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153129	200			0	lt	\\ = repeating (currently inactive)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154406	201			0	lt	PROTECT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145127	202			0	lt	Returns the status of the cell protection for the cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155794	203			0	lt	1 = cell is protected				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155072	204			0	lt	0 = cell is not protected				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156178	205			0	lt	FORMAT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150220	206			0	lt	Returns a character string that indicates the number format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824	207			0	lt	, = number with thousands separator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153837	208			0	lt	F = number without thousands separator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150318	209			0	lt	C = currency format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153168	210			0	lt	S = exponential representation, for example, 1.234+E56				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153515	211			0	lt	P = percentage				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154375	212			0	lt	In the above formats, the number of decimal places after the decimal separator is given as a number. Example: the number format #,##0.0 returns ,1 and the number format 00.000% returns P3				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150575	213			0	lt	D1 = MMM-D-YY, MM-D-YY and similar formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150589	214			0	lt	D2 = DD-MM				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151034	215			0	lt	D3 = MM-YY				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156371	216			0	lt	D4 = DD-MM-YYYY HH:MM:SS				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3157881	217			0	lt	D5 = MM-DD				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3157894	218			0	lt	D6 = HH:MM:SS AM/PM				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154068	219			0	lt	D7 = HH:MM AM/PM				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150286	220			0	lt	D8 = HH:MM:SS				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145756	221			0	lt	D9 = HH:MM				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145768	222			0	lt	G = All other formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153375	223			0	lt	- (Minus) at the end = negative numbers are formatted in color				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3155545	224			0	lt	() (brackets) at the end = there is an opening bracket in the format code				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154594	225			0	lt	COLOR				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3152922	226			0	lt	Returns 1, if negative values have been formatted in color, otherwise 0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145563	227			0	lt	PARENTHESES				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156072	228			0	lt	Returns 1 if the format code contains an opening bracket (, otherwise 0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156090	159			0	lt	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> (list of options) is the position of the cell to be examined. If \<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is a range, the cell moves to the top left of the range. If \<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is missing, $[officename] Calc uses the position of the cell in which this formula is located. Microsoft Excel uses the reference of the cell in which the cursor is positioned.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Logical Functions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153484				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>logical functions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; logical\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>functions; logical functions\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153484	1			0	lt	Logical Functions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149312	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"logischtext\"\>This category contains the \<emph\>Logical\</emph\> functions. \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147505				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>AND function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147505	29			0	lt	AND				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153959	65			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UND\"\>Returns TRUE if all arguments are TRUE.\</ahelp\> If one of the elements is FALSE, this function returns the FALSE value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3146100	66			0	lt	The arguments are either logical expressions themselves (TRUE, 1<5, 2+3=7, B8<10) that return logical values, or arrays (A1:C3) containing logical values.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538	67			0	lt	When a function expects a single value, but you entered a cell range, then the value from the cell range is taken that is in the same column or row as the formula.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149128	68			0	lt	If the entered range is outside of the current column or row of the formula, the function returns the error value #VALUE!				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150374	31			0	lt	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3159123	32			0	lt	AND(LogicalValue1; LogicalValue2 ...LogicalValue30)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150038	33			0	lt	            \<emph\>LogicalValue1; LogicalValue2 ...LogicalValue30\</emph\> are conditions to be checked. All conditions can be either TRUE or FALSE. If a range is entered as a parameter, the function uses the value from the range that is in the current column or row. The result is TRUE if the logical value in all cells within the cell range is TRUE.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149143	34			0	lt	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153123	35			0	lt	The logical values of entries 12<13; 14>12, and 7<6 are to be checked:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3145632	36			0	lt	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=AND(12<13;14>12;7<6)\</item\> returns FALSE.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946	60			0	lt	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=AND (FALSE;TRUE)\</item\> returns FALSE.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149015				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>FALSE function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
