helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157993	61			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCOSHYP\"\>Returns the inverse hyperbolic cosine of a number.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145295	62			0	lt	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017	63			0	lt	ACOSH(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149000	64			0	lt	 This function returns the inverse hyperbolic cosine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the number whose hyperbolic cosine is Number. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6393932				0	lt	 Number must be greater than or equal to 1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150566	65			0	lt	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145629	66			0	lt	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOSH(1)\</item\> returns 0.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id951567				0	lt	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOSH(COSH(4))\</item\> returns 4.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149027				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>ACOT function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149027	70			0	lt	ACOT				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155818	71			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCCOT\"\>Returns the inverse cotangent (the arccotangent) of the given number.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153225	72			0	lt	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158419	73			0	lt	ACOT(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154948	74			0	lt	 This function returns the inverse trigonometric cotangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the angle (in radians) whose cotangent is Number. The angle returned is between 0 and PI.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5834528				0	lt	To return the angle in degrees, use the DEGREES function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147538	75			0	lt	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155375	76			0	lt	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOT(1)\</item\> returns 0.785398163397448 (PI/4 radians).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8589434				0	lt	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DEGREES(ACOT(1))\</item\> returns 45. The tangent of 45 degrees is 1. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148426				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>ACOTH function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148426	80			0	lt	ACOTH				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147478	81			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ARCOTHYP\"\>Returns the inverse hyperbolic cotangent of the given number.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152585	82			0	lt	Syntax				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147172	83			0	lt	ACOTH(Number)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146155	84			0	lt	 This function returns the inverse hyperbolic cotangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the number whose hyperbolic cotangent is Number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5818659				0	lt	An error results if Number is between -1 and 1 inclusive.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083452	85			0	lt	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150608	86			0	lt	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ACOTH(1.1)\</item\> returns inverse hyperbolic cotangent of 1.1, approximately 1.52226.				20130618 17:22:18
