helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958	2			0	lt	\<emph\>Extended tips\</emph\> provide a brief description of the function of a particular icon, text box or menu command when you rest your cursor on that item.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155339	3			0	lt	To turn Extended Tips on and off:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	4			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>, and check \<emph\>Extended tips\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398	5			0	lt	A check mark indicates that the extended tips are activated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811	6			0	lt	To turn Extended Tips on temporarily:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541	7			0	lt	Press the shortcut keys Shift+F1 to activate extended tips once.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825	8			0	lt	A question mark appears beside the mouse pointer. You can move this \<emph\>Help Mouse Pointer\</emph\> over all controls, icons and menu commands to obtain a description of the command. The \<emph\>Help Mouse Pointer\</emph\> is disabled the next time you click the mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143267				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Internet; Internet Explorer for displaying $[officename] documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] documents;viewing and editing in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"activex\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/activex.xhp\" name=\"ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\"\>ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	2			0	lt	Under Windows only, you can view any $[officename] document in a window of the Microsoft Internet Explorer. Install the ActiveX control in the $[officename] Setup program.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156346	3			0	lt	Installing the ActiveX control				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821	4			0	lt	Close $[officename] and the Quickstarter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771	5			0	lt	Click the Start button on the Windows taskbar. Choose \<emph\>Control Panel\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	lt	In the Control Panel, click \<emph\>Add or Remove Programs\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155	6			0	lt	In the list, click %PRODUCTNAME, then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	lt	In the Installation Wizard, select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399	7			0	lt	Open the \<emph\>Optional Components\</emph\> entry and find the \<emph\>ActiveX Control\</emph\> entry. Open the sub menu of the icon and select to install the feature.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	8			0	lt	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> and \<emph\>Install\</emph\>. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384	9			0	lt	Viewing $[officename] documents				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	10			0	lt	In Internet Explorer, browse to a web page that contains a link to a $[officename] Writer document, for example.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550	11			0	lt	Click the link to view the document in the Internet Explorer window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154072	12			0	lt	You may still right-click the link to save the file on your harddisk.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361	13			0	lt	Editing $[officename] documents				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154367	14			0	lt	The $[officename] document inside the Internet Explorer shows a set of read-only toolbar icons.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451	15			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Edit file\</emph\> icon in the document's toolbar to open a copy of the document in a new $[officename] window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760	16			0	lt	Edit the copy of the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Assistive Tools in $[officename]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] assistive technology\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assistive technology in $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen readers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399	22			0	lt	\<variable id=\"assistive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"Assistive Tools in $[officename]\"\>Assistive Tools in $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267	25			0	lt	$[officename] supports some assistive technology tools like screen magnification software, screen readers, and on-screen keyboards. Most of these tools communicate with $[officename] by means of the Java(TM) Access Bridge software, that uses the Java Accessibility API, a part of the Java runtime environment.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id8847010				0	lt	A current list of supported assistive tools can be found on the Apache OpenOffice Wiki at \<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Accessibility\"\>http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Accessibility\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345	12			0	lt	Requirements to use assistive tools in $[officename]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209	13			0	lt	Java Runtime Environment (JRE) version 1.4.1_01 and higher, or version 1.4.0_02 with the locale set to "en_us".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797	26			0	lt	Most recent version of the software for your assistive tool				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	15			0	lt	On Windows systems, \<link href=\"http://www.sun.com/access/downloads/\" name=\"Java Access Bridge\"\>Java Access Bridge\</link\> software version 1.0.3 or higher 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762	16			0	lt	On UNIX(R) systems, the GNOME 2 desktop environment with the Java Access Bridge software for GNOME				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149795	23			0	lt	Supported Assistive Tools				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419	2			0	lt	On Windows systems, $[officename] directly supports most on-screen keyboard software. Additional support for assistive tools is provided by the Java Access Bridge software. The following is a list of some assistive tools that use the Java Access Bridge software to exchange data with $[officename]:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329	4			0	lt	ZoomText Screen Magnifier (version 7.11 or higher)(Windows)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628	5			0	lt	Gnopernicus Screen Reader and Magnifier, using GNOME Assistive Technology Service Provider Interface (at-spi) and Java Accessibility API software				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474	6			0	lt	GNOME On Screen Keyboard (GOK), using GNOME at-spi and Java Accessibility API software				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061	24			0	lt	Supported Input Devices				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024	7			0	lt	$[officename] provides the ability to use alternative input devices for access to all functions of $[officename].				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045	8			0	lt	Screen magnification software allow users with low vision to work in $[officename] with caret and focus tracking.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811	9			0	lt	On-screen keyboards enable users to perform almost all data input and commands with a mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379	10			0	lt	Screen readers allow visually impaired users to access $[officename] with text-to-speech and Braille displays.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149808	11			0	lt	When accessibility support in $[officename] is enabled, the Java Runtime Environment is loaded, and increases the startup time for $[officename].				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933	18			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010800.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - View\"\>$[officename] - View\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155430	19			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Appearance\"\>$[officename] - Appearance\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148617	20			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01013000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Accessibility\"\>$[officename] - Accessibility\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Turning off Automatic URL Recognition				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; URL recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>recognizing URLs automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic hyperlink formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>URL;turning off URL recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks;turning off automatic recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;turning off automatic recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>predictive text, see also AutoCorrect function/AutoFill function/AutoInput function/word completion/text completion\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346	6			0	lt	\<variable id=\"autocorr_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/autocorr_url.xhp\" name=\"Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\"\>Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	7			0	lt	When you enter text, $[officename] automatically recognizes a word that may be a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\> and replaces the word with a hyperlink. $[officename] formats the hyperlink with direct font attributes (color and underline) the properties of which are obtained from certain Character Styles.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	2			0	lt	If you do not want $[officename] to automatically recognize URLs as you are typing, there are several ways of turning off this feature.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154306	8			0	lt	Undo URL Recognition				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	3			0	lt	When you are typing and notice that a text has just been automatically converted into a hyperlink, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z to undo this formatting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235	4			0	lt	If you do not notice this conversion until later, select the hyperlink and choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152350	9			0	lt	Turn off URL Recognition				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514	10			0	lt	Load a document of the type for which you want to modify the URL recognition.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246	11			0	lt	If you want to modify the URL recognition for text documents, open a text document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413	12			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550	13			0	lt	In the \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360	14			0	lt	If you unmark \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>, words will no longer be automatically replaced with hyperlinks.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423	15			0	lt	In $[officename] Writer there are two check boxes in front of \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>. The box in the first column is for later post-editing and the box in the second column is for AutoCorrect as you type.				20130618 17:22:18
