helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394	27			0	lt	\<variable id=\"copy_drawfunctions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copy_drawfunctions.xhp\" name=\"Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\"\>Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	28			0	lt	In $[officename] it is possible to copy drawing objects between text, spreadsheets and presentation documents. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	29			0	lt	Select the drawing object or objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426	31			0	lt	Copy the drawing object to the clipboard, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996	32			0	lt	Switch to the other document and place the cursor where the drawing object is to be inserted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234	33			0	lt	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573	34			0	lt	Inserting into a text document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276	35			0	lt	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current paragraph. You can change the anchor by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar. This opens a popup menu where you can select the anchor type.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609	36			0	lt	Inserting into a spreadsheet				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	30			0	lt	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current cell. You can change the anchor between cell and page by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149456\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleanchortype.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149456\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Inserting Data From Spreadsheets				20130618 17:22:18
