helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Registering and Deleting a Database 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	bm_id4724570				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>databases;registering (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;deleting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;registered databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	lt	\<variable id=\"data_register\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_register.xhp\"\>Registering and Deleting a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	lt	Data from any \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> can be registered to %PRODUCTNAME. To register means to tell %PRODUCTNAME where the data is located, how it is organized, how to get that data, and more. Once the database is registered, you can use the menu command \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to access the data records from your text documents and spreadsheets.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	lt	To register an existing database file:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	lt	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E1				0	lt	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and select the database file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	lt	To remove a registered database from %PRODUCTNAME				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10707				0	lt	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10719				0	lt	Select the database file and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F3				0	lt	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FB				0	lt	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				20130618 17:22:18
