helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147834				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>database reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources;reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;opening and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;database reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;templates\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149178	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"data_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_report.xhp\" name=\"Create, Use, and Edit Database Reports\"\>Using and Editing Database Reports\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609	13			0	lt	Using a Report				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265	14			0	lt	%PRODUCTNAME stores the information about the created reports in the database file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758	15			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> and select the database file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054	16			0	lt	In the database file window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280	18			0	lt	Double-click one of the report names to open the report.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	lt	These links are added automatically when you create a new report by the Report Wizard or in the Report Builder window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id1695608				0	lt	Editing a Report Created in the Report Builder Window				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id7510910				0	lt	Right-click the name of a report in the database file window, then choose Edit.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id8138065				0	lt	The Report Builder window opens with the report's information loaded. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id5086825				0	lt	Use the toolbars and menu commands and drag-and-drop to edit the report as stated in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\> guide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id4747154				0	lt	Execute the report to see the resulting report document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153104	19			0	lt	Editing a Report Created by the Report Wizard				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863	20			0	lt	On the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100500.xhp\" name=\"last dialog page of the Report AutoPilot\"\>last dialog page of the Report Wizard\</link\>, you can choose to edit the report template before you use the report.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3155431	22			0	lt	You can edit the page styles for the first page and the following pages of the report as well as the paragraph styles, the number formats, the printed field labels, and more.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D7				0	lt	Unless you have a thorough understanding of the database the report accesses, do not edit the SQL statement, database name, the hidden form controls, or the related information on the report.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Creating Reports 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	bm_id3729667				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards;reports\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	lt	\<variable id=\"data_reports\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_reports.xhp\"\>Creating Reports\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	lt	A report is a Writer text document that can show your data in an organized order and formatting. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, you have a choice to create a report either manually using drag-and-drop in the Report Builder window, or semi-automatic by following a series of dialogs in the Report Wizard. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4094363				0	lt	The following list gives you some information to decide which method to use for your data:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8514358				0	lt	Report Builder				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id9764091				0	lt	Report Wizard				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1579638				0	lt	Started by "Create Report in Design View" command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1886959				0	lt	Started by "Use Wizard to Create Report" command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id455030				0	lt	Full flexibility to use report headers and footers, page headers and footers, multi-column reports.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8409985				0	lt	Uses a Writer template to generate a report document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id5931272				0	lt	Use drag-and-drop to position the record fields or other design elements like pictures or lines.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id9869075				0	lt	Select from several given choices to arrange the data records.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8611713				0	lt	Generates a one-time snapshot of the data. To see an updated report, execute the same report again to create a Writer document with the updated data.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id2866908				0	lt	You can choose to generate a one-time snapshot with fixed data, or a "live" report with links to the current data at the time when you open the Base file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4169743				0	lt	Saves the report as a Writer text document. Stores the information how to create the report inside the Base file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id408948				0	lt	Saves the report and the information how to create the report inside the Base file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id2891933				0	lt	Choose Open in the context menu or double-click the report name to create a new report with the current data.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id6142765				0	lt	Choose Open in the context menu or double-click the report name to either see again the static snapshot of the data from first creation time, or to create a new report with the current data. This depends on your choice on the last page of the wizard.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1757560				0	lt	Choose Edit in the context menu of a report name to open the Report Builder window, with the report's information loaded.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4649189				0	lt	Choose Edit in the context menu of a report name to edit the Writer template file that was used to create the report.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	hd_id8414258				0	lt	Creating a New Report Manually In Design View				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id3119602				0	lt	Open the database file where you want to create the new report.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4226508				0	lt	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id5758842				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Create Report in Design View\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4870754				0	lt	Follow the instructions in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\> guide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	lt	Creating a New Report With the Report Wizard				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105DC				0	lt	Open the database file where you want to create the new report.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E0				0	lt	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E8				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Report\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8032166				0	lt	Follow the steps of the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100000.xhp\"\>Report Wizard\</link\> to create the report.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Searching Tables and Form Documents				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	bm_id4066896				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>finding;records in form documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;finding records\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching;tables and forms\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154186	64			0	lt	\<variable id=\"data_search\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_search.xhp\" name=\"Searching Tables and Form Documents\"\>Searching Tables and Form Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3153311\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_recsearch.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153311\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3149178	65			0	lt	In spreadsheets and documents in which form controls are used, you can click the \<emph\>Find Record\</emph\> icon on the form bar to open a dialog to find any text and values. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	66			0	lt	You can search in one or in all data fields. You can select whether the text must be at the beginning, end or any location of the data field. You also can use the ? and * wildcards, as in the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog. You can find additional information about the database search function in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100200.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Searching With a Form Filter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	bm_id8772545				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching; form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering; data in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;filtering in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; filtering data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data, see also values\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156042	5			0	lt	\<variable id=\"data_search2\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_search2.xhp\" name=\"Searching With a Form Filter\"\>Searching With a Form Filter\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182	17			0	lt	Open a form document that contains database fields.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157	18			0	lt	As an example, open an empty text document and press F4. Open the bibliography database table \<emph\>biblio\</emph\> in the data source view. While pressing Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, drag a few column headers into the document so that the form fields are created.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984	19			0	lt	On the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Design Mode On/Off\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3147618\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_switchcontroldesignmode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147618\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to turn off the design mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672	6			0	lt	On the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Form-Based Filters\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149807\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfilter.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149807\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The current document is displayed with its form controls as an empty edit mask. The \<emph\>Form Filter \</emph\>toolbar appears.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666	7			0	lt	Enter the filter conditions into one or several fields. Note that if you enter filter conditions into several fields, all of the entered conditions must match (Boolean AND).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481	8			0	lt	More information about wildcards and operators can be found in \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462	9			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterExecute\"\>If you click the \<emph\>Apply Form-Based Filter\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Form Filter\</emph\> toolbar, the filter will be applied.\</ahelp\> You see the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar and can browse through the found records.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273	10			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterExit\"\>If you click on the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button on the \<emph\>Form Filter\</emph\> toolbar, the form is displayed without a filter.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150114	11			0	lt	Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Apply Filter\"\>\<emph\>Apply Filter\</emph\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3144764\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_datafilterstandardfilter.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3144764\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar to change to the filtered view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3146898	12			0	lt	The filter that has been set can be removed by clicking \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sort\"\>\<emph\>Remove Filter/Sort\</emph\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3151318\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_removefiltersort.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151318\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Table Design				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155448				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases; creating in design view (manually)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>designing; database tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>properties;fields in databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fields;database tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoValue (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>primary keys;design view\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798	104			0	lt	\<variable id=\"data_tabledefine\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\" name=\"Table Design\"\>Table Design\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535	2			0	lt	This section contains information about how to create a new database table in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05010000.xhp\" name=\"design view\"\>design view\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154288	3			0	lt	Open the database file of the database where you want a new table. Click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon. Choose \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\> to create a new table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798	4			0	lt	In the Design view, you can now create the fields for your table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349	5			0	lt	Enter new fields in rows from top to bottom. Click the \<emph\>Field Name\</emph\> cell and enter a field name for each data field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id1595507				0	lt	Include a "primary key" data field. Base needs a primary key to be able to edit the table contents. A primary key has unique contents for each data record. For example, insert a numerical field, right-click the first column, and choose \<emph\>Primary Key\</emph\> from the context menu. Set \<emph\>AutoValue\</emph\> to "Yes", so Base can automatically increment the value for each new record.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	6			0	lt	In the next cell to the right, define the \<emph\>Field Type\</emph\>. When you click in the cell, you can select a field type in the combo box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760	38			0	lt	Each field can only accept data corresponding to the specified field type. For example, it is not possible to enter text in a number field. Memo fields in dBASE III format are references to internally-managed text files which can hold up to 64KB text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456	41			0	lt	You can enter an optional \<emph\>Description\</emph\> for each field. The text of the description will appear as a tip on the column headings in the table view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379	42			0	lt	Field Properties				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798	45			0	lt	Enter properties for each selected data field. Depending on the database type, some input facilities may not be available.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762	46			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> box, enter the default contents for every new record. This contents can be edited later.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869	47			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Entry required\</emph\> box, specify whether or not the field may remain empty.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908	7			0	lt	For the \<emph\>Length\</emph\> box, a combo box may be shown that provides the available choices.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Working with Tables				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id1983703				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table views of databases\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	lt	\<variable id=\"data_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tables.xhp\"\>Working with Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	lt	Data is stored in tables. As an example, your system address book that you use for your e-mail addresses is a table of the address book database. Each address is a data record, presented as a row in that table. The data records consist of data fields, for example the first and the last name fields and the e-mail field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	lt	Creating a New Table With the Table Wizard				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	lt	In %PRODUCTNAME you can create a new table using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/tablewizard00.xhp\"\>Table Wizard\</link\>:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	lt	Open the database file where you want to create the new table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	lt	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Table\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	lt	Creating a New Table With the Design View				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	lt	Open the database file where you want to create the new table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	lt	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	lt	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\"\>Table Design\</link\> window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	lt	Creating a New Table View				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077C				0	lt	Some database types support table views. A table view is a query that is stored with the database. For most database operations, a view can be used as you would use a table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10782				0	lt	Open the database file where you want to create the new table view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	lt	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078E				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Create Table View\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10795				0	lt	You see the View Design window, which is almost the same as the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\"\>Query Design window\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
