helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111	34			0	lt	A fast way of copying from a data source into a text or spreadsheet document, or of creating forms based on a data source, is by drag-and-drop.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3155390\" src=\"res/helpimg/copydata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155390\"\>Mouse pointer copying data\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	35			0	lt	Copying with Drag-and-Drop				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	28			0	lt	If you want to reverse a drag-and-drop, position the cursor in your document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656	46			0	lt	It is also possible to copy by drag-and-drop from a document into a data source:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379	47			0	lt	A text table or the selected range of a spreadsheet can be dragged using drag-and-drop to a table container in the data source explorer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211	48			0	lt	Plain text can be copied using drag-and-drop from one document to a data field in the data source view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145421	36			0	lt	Using data in a text document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	12			0	lt	You can insert a database field in a text document by dragging a field name from the column header of the data source view into the document. This is especially useful when designing form letters. Simply drag the desired fields - home address, form of address, and so on - into your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153105	37			0	lt	To insert a complete record, select the corresponding header and drag it into the document. When you release the mouse button, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Insert database columns\"\>\<emph\>Insert database columns\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears, in which you can decide whether to use all database fields, and whether to copy the data into the document as text, a table or fields. All currently selected records will be inserted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230	39			0	lt	Applying data to a table document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	40			0	lt	You can insert one or more records into the current sheet of a spreadsheet by selecting the rows in the data source view and dragging and dropping them into the spreadsheet. The data is inserted at the place where you release the mouse button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149766	42			0	lt	Inserting controls in a text form				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132	43			0	lt	When you create a text form linked to a database, you can generate controls by drag-and-drop from the data source view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562	45			0	lt	When you drag a database column into the text document, you insert a field. If you hold down Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging, a text field is inserted, grouped with an appropriate label field. The text field already contains all the database information that you need for the form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Copying Graphics From the Gallery				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145345				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>Gallery;dragging pictures to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;dropping Gallery pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;from Gallery to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345	40			0	lt	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_fromgallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics From the Gallery\"\>Copying Graphics From the Gallery\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535	41			0	lt	If you drag a graphic from the Gallery into a text, spreadsheet or presentation document, the graphic will be inserted there.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762	45			0	lt	If you release the graphic \<emph\>directly on a draw object\</emph\>, please note the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825	43			0	lt	If you move the graphic (drag it without pressing any key, in which case no additional symbol appears next to the mouse pointer), only the attributes are copied from the graphic and applied to the draw object on which you release the mouse button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665	42			0	lt	If you copy the graphic (drag it while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, in which case a plus sign appears next to the mouse pointer), the graphic will be inserted as an object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514	44			0	lt	If you create a hyperlink (drag while holding down Shift and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, in which case a linking arrow appears next to the mouse pointer), the drawing object is replaced by the graphic from the Gallery, but the position and size of the replaced draw object are retained.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Adding Graphics to the Gallery				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Gallery; adding pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;adding to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;pictures in Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927	49			0	lt	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_gallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_gallery.xhp\" name=\"Adding Graphics to the Gallery\"\>Adding Graphics to the Gallery\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267	50			0	lt	You can place a graphic from a document such as an HTML page in the Gallery by drag-and-drop.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	56			0	lt	Display the Gallery theme to which you want to add the graphic.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	51			0	lt	Position the mouse pointer above the graphic, without clicking.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	52			0	lt	If the mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol, the graphic refers to a hyperlink. In this case, click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key to select it without executing the respective link.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	53			0	lt	If the mouse pointer does not change to a hand symbol, you can simply click the graphic to select it.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120	54			0	lt	Once the graphic is selected, release the mouse button. Click again on the graphic image, keeping the mouse button pressed for more than two seconds. The graphic image is copied to the internal memory.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150772	55			0	lt	Without releasing the mouse button, drag the graphic into the Gallery.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Copying Graphics Between Documents				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; drag and drop between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;pictures, between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;pictures from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201	15			0	lt	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics Between Documents\"\>Copying Graphics Between Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805	16			0	lt	You can copy a graphic from one document to another by drag-and-drop. If you plan to publish your document, please observe copyright laws and obtain the consent of the authors.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576	17			0	lt	Open the document in which you want to insert the graphic object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338	18			0	lt	Open the document from which you want to copy the graphic.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182	19			0	lt	Click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, to select it without executing any hyperlinks it may refer to.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110	20			0	lt	Keep the mouse button pressed and wait a moment while the object is copied to an internal memory.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	21			0	lt	Drag the graphic into the other document. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible side by side, first move the mouse pointer to the button of the target document while keeping the mouse button pressed. The document in question is then displayed and you can move the mouse pointer into the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628	22			0	lt	Release the mouse button as soon as the gray text cursor indicates the position where you want to insert a copy of the picture.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276	56			0	lt	If the graphic is connected with a hyperlink, the hyperlink and not the graphic is inserted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; copying areas to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; sheet areas, to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;sheet areas in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927	24			0	lt	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_table.xhp\" name=\"Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\"\>Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892	25			0	lt	Open both the text document and the spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	26			0	lt	Select the sheet area you want to copy.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827	27			0	lt	Point to the selected area and press the mouse button. Keep the mouse button pressed for a moment, then drag the area into the text document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	32			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible next to each other, first drag the mouse pointer to the destination document button. Continue to hold down the mouse button. The document is displayed, and you can move the mouse pointer within the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	28			0	lt	Once the cursor is located in the place where you want to insert the sheet area, release the mouse button. The sheet area is inserted as an OLE object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047	29			0	lt	You can select and edit the OLE object at any time.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164	30			0	lt	To edit the OLE object, double-click on it.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155389	33			0	lt	Alternatively, select the object and choose \<emph\>Edit - Object - Edit\</emph\> or choose \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> from the context menu. You edit the object in its own frame within the text document, but you see the icons and menu commands needed for spreadsheets.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860	31			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to open the source document of the OLE object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Adding Buttons to Toolbars 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>customizing; toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>buttons;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>toolbars;adding buttons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>configuring; toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;buttons in toolbars\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201	79			0	lt	\<variable id=\"edit_symbolbar\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/edit_symbolbar.xhp\" name=\"Adding Buttons to Toolbars\"\>Adding Buttons to Toolbars\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561	85			0	lt	To add a button to a toolbar:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157	78			0	lt	Click the arrow icon at the end of a toolbar and choose \<emph\>Visible Buttons\</emph\> and then select the button you want to display.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id2439039				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog where you can add, edit, and remove icons.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384	86			0	lt	To add a button to the list of Visible Buttons:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264	87			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>, and click on the \<emph\>Toolbars\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3154071	88			0	lt	In the\<emph\> Toolbars \</emph\>box, select the toolbar you want to change.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797	89			0	lt	Click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\> , select the new command, then click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3152922	90			0	lt	If you want, you can rearrange the \<emph\>Commands \</emph\>list by selecting a command name and clicking \<emph\>Move Up\</emph\> and \<emph\>Move Down\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171	91			0	lt	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Sending Documents as E-mail				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153345				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>documents; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>e-mail attachments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attachments in e-mails\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"email\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/email.xhp\" name=\"Sending Documents as E-mail\"\>Sending Documents as E-mail\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897	2			0	lt	Working in $[officename], you can send the current document as an e-mail attachment.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335	3			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Document as E-mail\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127	4			0	lt	$[officename] opens your default e-mail program.\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\> If you want to send the current document with another e-mail program, you can select the program to use with \<emph\>Internet - E-mail\</emph\> in the Options dialog box.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986	5			0	lt	In your e-mail program, enter the recipient, subject and any text you want to add, then send the e-mail.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3595385				0	lt	In case you want to send the e-mail to a recipient who only has software that cannot read the OpenDocument format, you can send the current document in an often used proprietary format.\<br/\>For a text document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft Word\</item\>. For a spreadsheet, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft Excel\</item\>. And for a presentation, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft PowerPoint\</item\>. \<br/\>If you want to send the document as a read-only file, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as PDF\</item\>.\<br/\>These commands do not change your current document. Only a temporary copy is created and sent.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Error Report Tool				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150616				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>reports;error reports\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>crash reports\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>activating;Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616	17			0	lt	\<variable id=\"error_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/error_report.xhp\" name=\"Error Report Tool\"\>Error Report Tool\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	1			0	lt	The Error Report Tool starts automatically when a program crash occurs.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	2			0	lt	The Error Report Tool gathers all necessary information that can help the program developers to improve the code, so that in later versions this error can possibly be avoided. Please help us to improve the software and send the generated error report.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538	4			0	lt	Starting the Error Report Tool				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	5			0	lt	With most program crashes the Error Report Tool will start automatically.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154046	7			0	lt	Completing the Report				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335	8			0	lt	On the main Error Report Tool dialog, you can enter some additional information that may help the developers to localize the error. For example, if the error only appears after a change in your hardware or software environment, or if you clicked on a button, please include that information.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399	9			0	lt	Sending the Error Report				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	10			0	lt	The Error Report Tool uses the HTTP PUT / SOAP protocol to send the report data. You may optionally enter some descriptive text that will help us to identify the context of the program crash. Then click the \<emph\>Send\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670	11			0	lt	You will not get an answer to your error report. If you need support, please visit the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\"\>support forum\</link\> on the Internet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526	12			0	lt	You may choose to respond to questions that the developers may have about the reported error. Mark the check box if you allow to be contacted by e-mail, should additional information be required. By default this box is not marked, so you will not get any e-mail.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	13			0	lt	What Data is Sent?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366	14			0	lt	The error report consists of several files. The main file contains information about the error type, operating system name and version, memory usage, and the description that you entered. You can click the \<emph\>Show Report\</emph\> button on the main dialog of the Error Report Tool to view what will get sent in the main file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177	15			0	lt	In addition, relevant memory contents and stack traces are gathered by some system standard tools ("dbhhelp.dll" on Windows systems, "pstack" on UNIX systems). This information will be sent also.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Saving Documents in Other Formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159233				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>documents; saving in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; documents in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; saving in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;saving in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; saving in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; saving in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; saving in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; to Microsoft Office formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Word documents; saving as\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Excel; saving as\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PowerPoint export\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149416	6			0	lt	\<variable id=\"export_ms\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/export_ms.xhp\" name=\"Saving Documents in Other Formats\"\>Saving Documents in Other Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	2			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3153348	3			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Save as type\</emph\> or \<emph\>File type\</emph\> list box, select the desired format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985	4			0	lt	Enter a name in the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252	7			0	lt	If you want the file dialogs to offer another file format as default, select that format in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - General\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Default file format \</emph\>area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\export_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	5			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>Save As\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156426				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>faxes; sending\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faxes;configuring $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as faxes \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>configuring;fax icon\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156426	5			0	lt	\<variable id=\"fax\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/fax.xhp\" name=\"Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\"\>Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	3			0	lt	To send a fax directly from $[officename], you need a fax modem and a fax driver that allows applications to communicate with the fax modem.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166410	6			0	lt	Sending a Fax Through the Print Dialog				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996	7			0	lt	Open the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog by choosing \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\> and select the fax driver in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3155135	8			0	lt	Clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\> opens the dialog for your fax driver, where you can select the fax recipient.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825	9			0	lt	Configuring $[officename] a Fax Icon				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822	10			0	lt	You can configure $[officename] so that a single click on an icon automatically sends the current document as a fax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	11			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040400.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Print\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</link\>\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985	12			0	lt	Select the fax driver from the \<emph\>Fax\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EB				0	lt	Click the arrow icon at the end of the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar. In the drop-down menu, choose \<emph\>Customize\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	lt	The \<emph\>Toolbar\</emph\>s tab page of the \<emph\>Customize\</emph\> dialog appears.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FA				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	lt	Select the "Documents" category, then select the "Send Default Fax" command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and then \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10712				0	lt	On the \<emph\>Toolbars\</emph\> tab page, click the down arrow button to position the new icon where you want it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	lt	Your \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar now has a new icon to send the current document as a fax.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Using the Filter Navigator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150322				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>filters; Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filter conditions;connecting\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	lt	\<variable id=\"filternavigator\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/filternavigator.xhp\"\>Using the Filter Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3150322	13			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterNavigator\"\>To connect several filter conditions with Boolean OR, click the \<emph\>Filter navigation\</emph\> icon on the filter bar.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> window appears.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711	14			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FILTER_NAVIGATOR\"\>The filter conditions that have been set appear in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. As soon as a filter is set, you see a blank filter entry at the bottom of the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> . You can select this entry by clicking the word "Or". Once you have selected the blank filter entry, you can enter additional filter conditions in the form. These conditions are linked by Boolean OR to the previously defined conditions.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3145620	15			0	lt	The context menu can be called for each entry in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. \<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_FILTER_IS_NOT_NULL\"\>You can edit the filter conditions in this area directly as text. If you wish to check if a field has content or no content, you can select the filter conditions "empty" (SQL:"Is Null") or "not empty" (SQL: "Is not Null").\</ahelp\> It is also possible to delete the entry by using the context menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3156374	16			0	lt	You can move filter conditions in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> by dragging and dropping, or use the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Alt+Up Arrow or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Alt+Down Arrow. To copy filter conditions, drag them while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Searching for Attributes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	bm_id5681020				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>fonts;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>font attributes;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attributes; finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding; attributes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;Find & Replace mode\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	lt	\<variable id=\"find_attributes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/find_attributes.xhp\"\>Searching for Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	lt	You can search for text with attributes that are applied either by direct formatting or by styles. For example, if you search for the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> attribute, all instances of text that do not use the default font are found. All text that has a directly coded font attribute, and all text where a style switches the font attribute, are found.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	lt	If you want to find text with any font by name, click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\"\>Find & Replace\</link\> dialog of %PRODUCTNAME Writer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	lt	After you select the attributes that you want to search for, the \<emph\>Search for Styles\</emph\> box in the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>area of the %PRODUCTNAME Writer \<emph\>Find & Replace \</emph\>dialog changes to \<emph\>Including Styles\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	lt	If you want to search for text in which attributes were set by using direct formatting and styles, select the \<emph\>Including Styles\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	lt	The search criteria for attributes are listed below the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BE				0	lt	To search for all font changes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	lt	Clear the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box if necessary.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	lt	In the \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> check box, and click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	lt	In the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog, you now can read "Font" below the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F4				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FB				0	lt	All places where a font change was applied, either directly or by assigning an appropriate style, are found.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FE				0	lt	To reset the Find & Replace mode				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	lt	To stop searching for the current attributes, reset the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog to normal mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070C				0	lt	Click \<emph\>No Format\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071E				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\"\>Find & Replace\</link\> dialog				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id6837672				0	lt	Searching for attributes is available in the Find & Replace dialog for text documents.				20130618 17:22:18
