helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147143	33			0	lt	\<variable id=\"mobiledevicefilters\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/mobiledevicefilters.xhp\" name=\"Mobile Devices Filters for Pocket Device Appliances\"\>Mobile Devices Filters for Pocket Device Appliances\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267	1			0	lt	You can save and open documents to and from several mobile devices file formats.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957	2			0	lt	Currently the following filters are available:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	3			0	lt	AportisDoc for Palm OS compatible devices				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209	4			0	lt	Pocket Excel for Pocket PC compatible devices				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	5			0	lt	Pocket Word for Pocket PC compatible devices				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653	6			0	lt	Installing the Pocket PC filters under Windows will also install a DLL file that supports the synchronization software of your Pocket PC.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252	7			0	lt	The Java Runtime Environment is required to use the mobile device filters.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153665	8			0	lt	Installing the mobile device filters				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685	9			0	lt	Close $[officename] and the Quickstarter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023	10			0	lt	If you are using the Windows operating system with ActiveSync installed, disconnect any Pocket PC device from ActiveSync.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153061	11			0	lt	Start the $[officename] Setup program:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E7				0	lt	Open the Windows \<emph\>Start\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Control Panel\</emph\>, double-click \<emph\>Add or Remove Programs\</emph\>, select the %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION entry, click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794	12			0	lt	In Setup, choose the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> option and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054	13			0	lt	Open the \<emph\>Optional Components\</emph\> entry, then open the \<emph\>Mobile Device Filters\</emph\> entry. Select the filters you want to install.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138	14			0	lt	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>, \<emph\>Next\</emph\>, \<emph\>Install\</emph\>, \<emph\>Finish\</emph\> to install the filters and exit the Setup program.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154123	15			0	lt	Saving $[officename] documents for a mobile device				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192	16			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672	17			0	lt	Open the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box and select the appropriate filter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419	18			0	lt	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768	19			0	lt	Opening mobile device documents in $[officename]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287	20			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428	21			0	lt	Open the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box and select the appropriate filter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618	22			0	lt	Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159196	23			0	lt	Synchronizing file types				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272	24			0	lt	To convert Pocket PC formats to and from $[officename] formats, you must first change some options within ActiveSync. To do this, open the ActiveSync window and open its Options dialog. Perform the following steps:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149064	25			0	lt	Select the \<emph\>Rules\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216	26			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Conversion Settings\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154145	27			0	lt	Click the \<emph\>Device to Desktop\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155	28			0	lt	Select \<emph\>Pocket Word Document - Pocket PC\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638	29			0	lt	In the drop down list of available conversions, select \<emph\>$[officename] Writer \</emph\>and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958	30			0	lt	Repeat steps 4 and 5 for \<emph\>Pocket Excel Workbook\</emph\> selecting \<emph\>$[officename] Calc\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389	31			0	lt	After these steps you can copy documents between $[officename] and your Pocket PC, either by the ActiveSync software or by the Windows Explorer. The filters will be applied to the document files automatically.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Changing the Association of Microsoft Office Document Types				20130618 17:22:18
