helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Copying Attributes With the Format Paintbrush				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	bm_id380260				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>Format Paintbrush\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>formatting;copying\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>copying;formatting\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Paintbrush\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053A				0	lt	\<variable id=\"formatpaintbrush\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/paintbrush.xhp\"\>Copying Formatting With the Format Paintbrush\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10655				0	lt	You can use the Format Paintbrush tool to copy formatting from a text selection or from an object and apply the formatting to another text selection or object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_id101920091122570				0	lt	In Calc, the Format Paintbrush only applies to cell formatting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	lt	Select the text or object whose formatting you want to copy.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	lt	On the \<emph\>Standard Bar\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10660				0	lt	The cursor changes to a paint bucket.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	lt	If you want to apply the formatting to more than one selection, double-click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id209967\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatpaintbrush.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id209967\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. After you apply all the formatting, click the icon again.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	lt	Select or click the text or object that you want to apply the formatting to.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	lt	To exclude paragraph formatting, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> when you click. To exclude character formatting, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift when you click.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	lt	The following table describes the formatting attributes that the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> can copy:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10691				0	lt	Type of Selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10697				0	lt	Comment				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069E				0	lt	Nothing selected, but cursor is inside a text passage				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	lt	Copies the formatting of the current paragraph and the character formatting of the next character in the text flow direction.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	lt	Text is selected				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B1				0	lt	Copies the formatting of the last selected character and of the paragraph that contains the character.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B8				0	lt	Frame is selected				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BE				0	lt	Copies the frame attributes that are defined in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Frame\</item\> dialog. The contents, size, position, linking, hyperlinks, and macros in the frame are not copied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	lt	Object is selected				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	lt	Copies the object formatting that is defined in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Graphics\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Drawing Object\</item\> dialogs. The contents, size, position, hyperlinks, and macros in the object are not copied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	lt	Form control is selected				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D8				0	lt	Not supported				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DF				0	lt	Drawing object is selected				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E5				0	lt	Copies all formatting attributes. In Impress and Draw, the text contents of the object is also copied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	lt	Text within Calc cells is selected				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	lt	Not supported				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F9				0	lt	Writer table or cells are selected				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	lt	Copies the formatting that is specified in Table, Text Flow, Borders, and Background tab pages in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Table\</item\> dialog. The paragraph and character formatting are also copied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	lt	Calc table or cells are selected				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070C				0	lt	Copies the formatting that is specified in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\> dialog as well as the formatting of the cell contents				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Pasting Contents in Special Formats				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	bm_id3620715				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>clipboard;pasting formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;clipboard options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats;pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;pasting in special formats\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10725				0	lt	\<variable id=\"pasting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pasting.xhp\"\>Pasting Contents in Special Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	lt	Contents that are stored on the clipboard can be pasted into your document using different formats. In %PRODUCTNAME you can choose how to paste the contents using a dialog or a drop-down icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	lt	The available options depend on the contents of the clipboard.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144547360				0	lt	In Writer text documents, you can press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+V to paste the contents of the clipboard as unformatted text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	lt	Pasting clipboard contents using an icon menu				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10750				0	lt	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard Bar to open the menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	lt	Select one of the options.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	lt	If you do not like the result, click the \<emph\>Undo\</emph\> icon and then paste again with another option.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10762				0	lt	Pasting clipboard contents using a dialog				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10769				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10771				0	lt	Select one of the options and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	lt	If you are in a spreadsheet and the contents of the clipboard are spreadsheet cells, then a different \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears. Use the \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog to copy cells using basic or advanced options.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	lt	\<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>: swaps the rows and the columns of the cell range to be pasted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	lt	\<emph\>Link\</emph\>: pastes the cell range as a link. If the source file changes, the pasted cells change also.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	lt	The other options are explained in the help, when you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\> dialog from within %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BA				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Printing in Black and White				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150125				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>printing; black and white\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>black and white printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>colors; not printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; printing in black\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150125	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"print_blackwhite\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/print_blackwhite.xhp\" name=\"Printing in Black and White\"\>Printing in Black and White\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499	3			0	lt	Printing text and graphics in black and white				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	4			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. The \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page of the dialog opens.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892	5			0	lt	Click on \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. This opens the Properties dialog for your printer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313	6			0	lt	Select the option to print in black and white. For further information, refer to the user's manual of your printer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	7			0	lt	Confirm the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog and click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113	8			0	lt	The current document will be printed in black and white.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653	9			0	lt	Printing in black and white in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	10			0	lt	Choose Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress or Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Draw, as appropriate.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275	11			0	lt	Then choose \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573	12			0	lt	Under \<emph\>Quality,\</emph\> select either \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> or \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307	13			0	lt	When either of these options is selected, all presentations or drawings will be printed without color. If you only want to print in black for the \<emph\>current\</emph\> print job, select the option in \<emph\>File - Print - %PRODUCTNAME Draw/Impress\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149786	15			0	lt	               \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> converts all colors to a maximum of 256 gradations from black to white. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610	16			0	lt	               \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> converts all colors into the two values black and white. All borders around objects are printed black. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896	17			0	lt	Printing only text in black and white				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559	18			0	lt	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer you can choose to print color-formatted text in black and white. You can specify this either for all subsequent text documents to be printed, or only for the current printing process.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150358	19			0	lt	Printing all text documents with black and white text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541	20			0	lt	Choose Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer or Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer/Web.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084	21			0	lt	Then choose \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910	22			0	lt	Under \<emph\>Contents,\</emph\> mark \<emph\>Print black\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762	23			0	lt	All text documents or HTML documents will be printed with black text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148920	24			0	lt	Printing the current text document with black and white text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933	25			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. Then click the \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667	27			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Print text in black\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	29			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\" name=\"Printing dialogs\"\>Printing dialogs\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154146	30			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01000000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options dialog\"\>Tools - Options dialog\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Printing with Reduced Data				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	bm_id5201574				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>gradients off for faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps;off for faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resolution when printing bitmaps \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transparency;off for faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reduced printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>speed of printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing speed\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;transparencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;faster\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faster printing\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	lt	\<variable id=\"print_faster\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/print_faster.xhp\"\>Printing faster with Reduced Data\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C8				0	lt	You can decide to reduce the data necessary to print your document. The settings can be defined differently for printing directly to the printer or for printing to a file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CE				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Print\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D6				0	lt	Click one of the following settings options: 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D9				0	lt	\<emph\>Printer\</emph\>\<emph\>- \</emph\>to define options for reducing data while printing directly to a printer				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E2				0	lt	\<emph\>Print to file\</emph\>\<emph\>-\</emph\> to define options for reducing data while printing to a file				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	lt	Select any combination of the four options, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EF				0	lt	All documents that you print from now on will use the changed options.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F3				0	lt	Print your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	lt	You can reduce data for transparency, for gradients, or for bitmaps. When you reduce the data, on many printers you will not see a reduction of printing quality. But the printing time is substantially shorter, and when you print to a file, the file size is much smaller.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN10704				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010900.xhp\"\>Print options\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150620				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>protecting; contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protected contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>contents protection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>encryption of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>passwords for protecting contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>security;protecting contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>form controls; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects;protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>graphics;protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames;protecting\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394	3			0	lt	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> from being modified, deleted or viewed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957	4			0	lt	Protecting All Documents When Saving				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150775	5			0	lt	All documents that are saved in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\" name=\"OpenDocument format\"\>OpenDocument format\</link\> can be saved with a password. Documents that are saved with a password cannot be opened without the password. The content is secured so that it cannot be read with an external editor. This applies to content, graphics and OLE objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	6			0	lt	Turning on protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121	7			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box. Save the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286	8			0	lt	Turning off protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492	9			0	lt	Open the document, entering the correct password. Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068	64			0	lt	Information entered in \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\> is not encrypted. This includes the name of the author, creation date, word and character counts.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294	10			0	lt	Protecting Revision Marking				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3161646	11			0	lt	With every change made in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer, the review function records who made the change. This function can be turned on with protection, so that it can only be turned off when the correct password is entered. Until then, all changes will continue to be recorded. Acceptance or rejection of changes is not possible.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684	12			0	lt	Turning on protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104	13			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760	14			0	lt	Turning off protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920	15			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter the correct password.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155113	52			0	lt	Protecting Frames, Graphics, and OLE Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153703	53			0	lt	You can protect the content, position and size of inserted graphics. The same applies to frames (in Writer) and OLE objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147131	54			0	lt	Turning on protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088	55			0	lt	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Picture - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Contents\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\> and/or \<emph\>Size\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147510	56			0	lt	Turning off protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153657	57			0	lt	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Picture - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, unmark as appropriate.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152992	58			0	lt	Protecting Drawing Objects and Form Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429	59			0	lt	The draw objects that you insert into your documents with the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar can be protected from being accidentally moved or changed in size. You can do the same with form objects inserted with the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153226	60			0	lt	Turning on protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148815	61			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Mark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3156289	62			0	lt	Turning off protection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154991	63			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Unmark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	lt	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id4680928				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/protection.xhp\"\>Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id9014252				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp\"\>Protecting Cells in %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Recording and Displaying Changes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150499				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>marking changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>highlighting changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changes; review function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>review function; recording changes example\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Track Changes, see review function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499	7			0	lt	\<variable id=\"redlining\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining.xhp\" name=\"Recording and Displaying Changes\"\>Recording and Displaying Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id4013794				0	lt	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681	2			0	lt	When several authors are working on the same text or spreadsheet, the review function records and displays who made the various changes. On the final edit of the document, it is then possible to look at each individual change and decide whether it should be accepted or rejected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	3			0	lt	For example: You are an editor and are delivering your latest report. But before publication the report must be read by the senior editor and the proofreader, and both will add their changes. The senior editor writes "clarify" after one paragraph and crosses out another entirely. The proofreader corrects the spelling of your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774	4			0	lt	The edited document comes back to you, and you can incorporate or ignore the suggestions of the two reviewers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957	5			0	lt	Let's say you also e-mailed a copy of the report to a good friend and colleague who has done research on a similar topic in the past. You asked for a few suggestions, and the document is now returned by e-mail with your colleague's suggestions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	6			0	lt	As all your colleagues and the managers in your company work with $[officename], you can produce a final version of the document from the results you get back.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Accepting or Rejecting Changes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150247				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>changes; accepting or rejecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function;accepting or rejecting changes\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150247	23			0	lt	\<variable id=\"redlining_accept\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_accept.xhp\" name=\"Accepting or Rejecting Changes\"\>Accepting or Rejecting Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1491134				0	lt	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1110200810120034				0	lt	In Writer text documents you can also accept or reject changes by choosing commands from the context menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571	24			0	lt	When you edit a document in which others have made changes, you can accept or reject the changes individually or all together.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	25			0	lt	If you have put multiple copies of the document in circulation, first merge these into one document (see \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp#redlining_docmerge\"/\>).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	26			0	lt	Open the document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Accept or Reject\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\> dialog appears.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	27			0	lt	Select a change on the \<emph\>List\</emph\> tab. The change is selected and displayed in the document and you can now enter your decision with one of the buttons.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209	28			0	lt	If one author has modified another author's change, you will see the changes hierarchically arranged with a plus sign for opening up the hierarchy.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474	29			0	lt	If the list of changes is too long, you can switch to the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> tab in the dialog and specify that you only want to see the changes of certain authors, or only the changes of the last day, or that you want the list to be restricted in some other way.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271	42			0	lt	Color-coded entries display the result of the filter that is set. Entries in black can be accepted or rejected and match the filter criteria. Entries in blue do not themselves match the filter criteria, but have subentries that are included by the filter. Gray entries cannot be accepted or rejected and do not match the filter criterion. Green entries do match the filter but cannot be accepted or rejected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Comparing Versions of a Document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154788				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>documents; comparing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comparisons;document versions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changes;comparing to original\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154788	32			0	lt	\<variable id=\"redlining_doccompare\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_doccompare.xhp\" name=\"Comparing Versions of a Document\"\>Comparing Versions of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	lt	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3995178				0	lt	Imagine you have some co-authors or reviewers who collaborate with you writing your original document. One day you send out copies of your document to all reviewers. You ask them to edit the copy and send it back.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id9948423				0	lt	Normally, the reviewers enable change tracking by \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> and you can easily see the changes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421	33			0	lt	If one of the authors has made changes to a document without recording them, you can compare the changed document to your original document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087	35			0	lt	Open the reviewer's document and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Compare Document\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4208807				0	lt	You should always start with opening the newer document and compare it with the older document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	36			0	lt	A file selection dialog appears. Select your older original document and confirm the dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762	37			0	lt	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> combines both documents into the reviewer's document. All text passages that occur in the reviewer's document but not in the original are identified as having been inserted, and all text passages that got deleted by the reviewer are identified as deletions.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674	38			0	lt	You can now accept or reject the insertions and deletions. At the end you may save the reviewer's document as a new original with a new name.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Merging Versions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154230				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>documents; merging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions;merging document versions\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154230	17			0	lt	\<variable id=\"redlining_docmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging Versions\"\>Merging Versions\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id2136295				0	lt	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049	19			0	lt	When a document has been edited by more than one person, it is possible to merge the edited copies into the original. The only requirement is that the documents differ only and exclusively in the recorded changes - all other original text must be identical.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425	20			0	lt	Open the original document into which you want to merge all copies.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177	21			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Merge Document\</emph\>. A file selection dialog appears.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576	23			0	lt	Select the copy of the document from the dialog. If there have been no subsequent changes to the original document, the copy is merged into the original.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182	24			0	lt	If changes have been made to the original document, an error dialog appears that informs you that the merge is unsuccessful.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749	22			0	lt	After you merge the documents you will see the recorded changes from the copy in the original document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Recording Changes				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>changes; recording\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>recording; changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>comments; on changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>review function;tracking changes\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364	7			0	lt	\<variable id=\"redlining_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_enter.xhp\" name=\"Recording Changes\"\>Recording Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7271645				0	lt	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145669	8			0	lt	Not all changes are recorded. For example, the changing of a tab stop from align left to align right is not recorded. However, all usual changes made by a proofreader are recorded, such as additions, deletions, text alterations, and usual formatting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	17			0	lt	1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095	9			0	lt	To start recording changes, open the document to be edited and choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Changes\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Changes\</emph\>\</link\> and then choose \<emph\>Record\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749	18			0	lt	2.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802	10			0	lt	Now start making your changes. You will note that all new text passages that you enter are underlined in color, while all text that you delete remains visible but is crossed out and shown in color.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349	19			0	lt	3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	11			0	lt	If you move to a marked change with the mouse pointer, you will see a reference to the type of change, the author, date and time of day for the change in the Help Tip. If the Extended Tips are also enabled, you will also see any available comments on this change.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156119	12			0	lt	Changes in a spreadsheet document are highlighted by a border around the cells; when you point to the cell you can see more detailed information on this change in the Help Tip.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473	13			0	lt	You can enter a comment on each recorded change by placing the cursor in the area of the change and then choosing \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Comment\</emph\>. In addition to Extended Tips, the comment is also displayed in the list in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230400.xhp\" name=\"Accept or Reject Changes\"\>\<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153542	14			0	lt	To stop recording changes, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> again. The check mark is removed and you can now save the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153627	15			0	lt	In a text document, you can highlight all lines that you have changed with an additional colored marking. This can be in the form of a red line in the margin, for example.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530	16			0	lt	To change the settings for tracking changes, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040700.xhp\" name=\"Changes\"\>\<emph\>Changes\</emph\>\</link\> or on the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060600.xhp\" name=\"Changes\"\>\<emph\>Changes\</emph\>\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Protecting Records				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>changes; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protecting; recorded changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>records; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function;protecting records\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"redlining_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Records\"\>Protecting Records\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id1631824				0	lt	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751	2			0	lt	To protect the changes made in a document during editing, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. To turn off the function or to accept or reject changes it is necessary to enter the correct password first.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	3			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Protect Records\</emph\>. This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/password_dlg.xhp\" name=\"Password\"\>\<emph\>Password\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	4			0	lt	Enter a password consisting of at least 5 characters and confirm it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Version Management				20130618 17:22:18
