helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	lt	You can assign custom scripts (macros) to menu items, icons, dialog controls, and events in %PRODUCTNAME.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	lt	%PRODUCTNAME internally supports the following scripting languages:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	lt	%PRODUCTNAME Basic				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10739				0	lt	JavaScript				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073D				0	lt	BeanShell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_id6797082				0	lt	Python				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091F				0	lt	In addition, developers can use high-level languages, for example Java programming language, to control %PRODUCTNAME externally. See the API project at Apache OpenOffice.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	lt	To assign a script to a new menu entry				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Menus\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	lt	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	lt	You see entries for "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), "My Macros" (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	lt	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select a script.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10770				0	lt	A list of the script functions appears in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> list box. Select a function.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	lt	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to create a new menu assignment. The new menu entry appears in the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> list box.				20130618 17:22:18
