helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153838	80			0	lt	Starts with the Impress file \<emph\>{filename.odp}\</emph\> and starts the presentation. Enters edit mode after the presentation.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276	13			0	lt	-minimized				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146080	14			0	lt	Starts minimized. The splash screen is not displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3641773				0	lt	-maximized				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id8224433				0	lt	Starts maximized.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145641	15			0	lt	-invisible				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154756	16			0	lt	Starts in invisible mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148914	17			0	lt	Neither the start-up logo nor the initial program window will be visible. However, the $[officename] software can be controlled and documents and dialogs opened via the \<link href=\"http://api.openoffice.org\" name=\"API\"\>API\</link\>. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147341	18			0	lt	When the $[officename] software has been started with this parameter, it can only be ended using the taskmanager (Windows) or the \<emph\>kill \</emph\>command (UNIX based systems).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150388	48			0	lt	It cannot be used in conjunction with \<emph\>-quickstart\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145147	19			0	lt	More information is found in the \<emph\>$[officename] Developer's Guide\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155334	77			0	lt	-nocrashreport				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149259	78			0	lt	Disables the error report tool.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155903	20			0	lt	-norestore				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156374	21			0	lt	Disables restart and file recovery after a system crash.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id5215918				0	lt	-nofirststartwizard				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id5665761				0	lt	Disables the Welcome Wizard.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148477	25			0	lt	-quickstart				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919	26			0	lt	Activates the Quickstarter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3152479	30			0	lt	-accept={UNO string}				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147130	31			0	lt	Notifies the $[officename] software that upon the creation of "UNO Acceptor Threads", a "UNO Accept String" will be used.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148874	32			0	lt	More information is found in the \<emph\>$[officename] Developer's Guide\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
