helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\version_number.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144436	4			0	lt	\<variable id=\"version_number\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/version_number.xhp\" name=\"Versions and Build Numbers\"\>Versions and Build Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\version_number.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	5			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>Help - About $[officename]\</emph\>. This opens a dialog containing information about the program.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\version_number.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	3			0	lt	To obtain further information, keep holding down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>the Command key \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and press the letters S D T in succession. At the beginning you will find information about the version and build number. This is followed by a list of contributors. To stop the information before the end, press Esc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Viewing File Properties				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152594				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>properties;files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files;properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;file properties\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152594	9			0	lt	\<variable id=\"viewing_file_properties\"\>\<variable id=\"viewing\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/viewing_file_properties.xhp\" name=\"Viewing File Properties\"\>Viewing File Properties\</link\>\</variable\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399	1			0	lt	File properties, such as author name, subject, and keywords, help you manage and identify your documents. $[officename] also tracks file statistics, including the number of words and the number of pages in a document, and automatically adds the statistics as part of the file property.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147834	2			0	lt	You can view file properties for the current document\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\> or for a document in the Windows File Open dialog \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159233	3			0	lt	To view file properties for the current document:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3153311	4			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150443	5			0	lt	To view file properties for a document listed in the Windows File Open dialog				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	6			0	lt	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306	7			0	lt	Select a file in the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121	8			0	lt	Right-click and choose\<emph\> Properties\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
