helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000099.xhp	0	help	par_id3143206	71			0	lt	\<variable id=\"userszenarien\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Tools Menu - Scenarios\"\>Tools Menu - Scenarios\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000099.xhp	0	help	par_id3156069	83			0	lt	On the help page for \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/main.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] general\"\>$[officename] general\</link\> you can find instructions that are applicable to all modules, such as working with windows and menus, customizing $[officename], data sources, Gallery, and drag and drop.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000099.xhp	0	help	par_id3149662	84			0	lt	If you want help with another module, switch to the help for that module with the combo box in the navigation area.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000099.xhp	0	help	par_id3154408	85			0	lt	\<variable id=\"winmanager\"\>The availability of this function depends on your X Window Manager. \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000099.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:HelperDialog\"\>Allows you to activate the automatic Help Agent. You can also activate the Help Agent through \<emph\>$[officename] - General - Help Agent\</emph\> in the Options dialog box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000099.xhp	0	help	par_idN10665				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:HelpTip\"\>Enables the display of icon names at the mouse pointer and other Help contents.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000099.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067C				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ActiveHelp\"\>Enables the display of a brief description of menus and icons at the mouse pointer.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000099.xhp	0	help	par_id6200750				0	lt	Some of the shortcut keys may be assigned to your desktop system. Keys that are assigned to the desktop system are not available to %PRODUCTNAME. Try to assign different keys either for %PRODUCTNAME, in \<emph\>Tools - Customize - Keyboard\</emph\>, or in your desktop system.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Graphics Export Options				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150127				0	lt	Graphics Export Options				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3160463				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Defines graphics export options.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id1				0	lt	When you export graphical elements to a file, you can select the file type. For most supported file types a dialog opens where you can setup export options.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id2				0	lt	The following file types do not show an options dialog: PWP, RAS, SVG, TIFF, XPM.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3				0	lt	The other file types show options dialogs where you can set the width and height of the exported image.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id4				0	lt	Depending on the file type, you can specify some more options. Press Shift+F1 and hover over the control to see an extended help text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id388				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the measurement units.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151330				0	lt	Width				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154561				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Specifies the width.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156027				0	lt	Height				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Specifies the height.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150944				0	lt	Resolution				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150129				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the image resolution. Select the measurement units from the list box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143534				0	lt	More options				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id10				0	lt	For JPEG files you can set the color depth and the quality.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id435923952				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the color depth from 8 bit grayscale or 24 bit true color.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id355152952				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the compression and quality for the export. Choose from a low quality with minimal file size, up to a high quality and big file size. A high compression means a low quality, a low compression means a high quality.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id11				0	lt	For BMP files you can set the compression and the RLE encoding.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id312346798				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Applies RLE (Run Length Encoding) to the BMP graphics.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id12				0	lt	For PBM, PGM, and PPM files you can set the encoding.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id344441				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Exports the file in binary format. The resulting file is smaller than a text file.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3555783				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Exports the file in ASCII text format. The resulting file is larger than a binary file.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id13				0	lt	For PNG files you can set the compression and the interlaced mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id35674840				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether the graphic is to be saved in interlaced mode.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id14				0	lt	For GIF files you can set the transparency and the interlaced mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id31456456938				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to save the background of the picture as transparent. Only objects will be visible in the GIF image. Use the Color Replacer to set the transparent color in the picture.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id15				0	lt	For EPS files you can set the preview, the color format, the compression, and the version.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147779948				0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>You must print an EPS file with a PostScript printer. Other printers will only print the embedded preview.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993155271				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether a preview image is exported in the TIFF format together with the actual PostScript file.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993144740	30			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether a monochrome preview graphic in EPSI format is exported together with the PostScript file. This format only contains printable characters from the 7-bit ASCII code.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993150935	12			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Compression is not available at this level. Select the Level 1 option if your PostScript printer does not offer the capabilities of Level 2.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993159201	14			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the Level 2 option if your output device supports colored bitmaps, palette graphics and compressed graphics.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id319947250	18			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Exports the file in color.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993147088	20			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Exports the file in grayscale tones.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id399153683	24			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>LZW compression is the compression of a file into a smaller file using a table-based lookup algorithm.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id319952780	26			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies that you do not wish to use compression.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147250				0	lt	See \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000020.xhp\" name=\"Import and Export Filter Information\"\>Import and Export Filter Information\</link\> for more information about filters.				20130618 17:22:18
