helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	27			0	lt	Standard				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3155923	28			0	lt	$[officename] determines the type.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472	29			0	lt	Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3148946	30			0	lt	Imported data are treated as text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265	31			0	lt	Date (DMY)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3156434	32			0	lt	Applies a date format (Day, Month, Year) to the imported data in a column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3148740	33			0	lt	Date (MDY)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3149688	34			0	lt	Applies a date format (Month, Day, Year) to the imported data in a column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150230	35			0	lt	Date (YMD)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153207	36			0	lt	Applies a date format (Year, Month, Day) to the imported data in a column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3148981	65			0	lt	US English				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153178	66			0	lt	Numbers formatted in US English are searched for and included regardless of the system language. A number format is not applied. If there are no US English entries, the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> format is applied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3154329	37			0	lt	Hide				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3154946	38			0	lt	The data in the column are not imported.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767	75			0	lt	If you selected one of the date formats (DMY), (MDY), or (YMD) and you enter numbers without date delimiters, the numbers are interpreted as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150650	76			0	lt	Number of characters 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150495	77			0	lt	Date format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3156212	78			0	lt	6				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153056	79			0	lt	Two characters each are taken for day, month, and year in the selected order.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147352	80			0	lt	8				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768	81			0	lt	Four characters are taken for the year, two each for month and day, in the selected order.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295	82			0	lt	5 or 7				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168	83			0	lt	As with 6 or 8 characters, but the first part of the sequence has one character less. This will suppress a leading zero for month and day.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143	44			0	lt	If you want to include the leading zero in the data you import, in telephone numbers for example, apply the "Text" format to the column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149287	39			0	lt	Preview				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147377	40			0	lt	Shows how the imported text will look after it is separated into columns. To apply a format to a column when it is imported, click a column and select a \<emph\>Column type\</emph\>. When you select a \<emph\>Column type\</emph\>, the column heading displays the applied format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105	64			0	lt	If you want to use a fixed width to separate the imported data into columns, click in the ruler to set the width boundaries.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3155746	74			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Navigating Without the Mouse\"\>Navigating Without the Mouse\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120	43			0	lt	For more information, see \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000020.xhp\" name=\"Information about Import and Export Filters\"\>Information about Import and Export Filters\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Warning Print Options				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145759	1			0	lt	Warning Print Options				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	par_id3152352	2			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SD:MODALDIALOG:DLG_PRINT_WARNINGS\"\>The\<emph\> Warning Print Options \</emph\>dialog appears when the page setup does not match the defined print range.\</ahelp\> This is the case, for example, if you draw a rectangle that is larger than the current page format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150620	3			0	lt	Print options				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156324	5			0	lt	Fit page to print range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	par_id3158405	7			0	lt	If you select the \<emph\>Fit page to print range \</emph\>option, the \<emph\>Warning Print Options\</emph\> dialog will not appear in subsequent print runs of this document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156553	8			0	lt	Print on multiple pages				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	9			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SD:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_PRINT_WARNINGS:RBT_POSTER\"\>Specifies whether to distribute the printout on multiple pages.\</ahelp\> The print range will be printed on multiple pages.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147010	10			0	lt	Trim				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000210.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111	11			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SD:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_PRINT_WARNINGS:RBT_CUT\"\>Specifies that anything extending beyond the maximum print range will be cut off and not included in the printing.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	ASCII Filter Options				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146856	1			0	lt	ASCII Filter Options				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000215.xhp	0	help	par_id3153070	2			0	lt	You can specify which options, such as basic font, language, character set, or break, are imported or exported with a text document. The dialog appears when you load an ASCII file with the filter "Text Encoded" or when you save the document the first time, or when you "save as" with another name.				20130618 17:22:18
