helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies how whitespaces are to be handled when a string of the current data type is being processed. Possible values are Preserve, Replace, and Collapse. The sematics follow the definition at http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#rf-whiteSpace.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	hd_id4191717				0	lt	Pattern				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id2318796				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies a regular expression pattern. Strings validated against the data type must conform to this pattern to be valid. The XSD data type syntax for regular expressions is different from the regular expression syntax used elseswhere in %PRODUCTNAME, for example in the Find & Replace dialog.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	hd_id399182				0	lt	Digits (total)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id5298318				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the maximum total number of digits that values of the decimal data type can have.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	hd_id7588732				0	lt	Digits (fraction)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the maximum total number of fractional digits that values of the decimal data type can have.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	hd_id3496200				0	lt	Max. (inclusive)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies an inclusive upper bound for values.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	hd_id888698				0	lt	Max. (exclusive)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies an exclusive upper bound for values.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	hd_id7594225				0	lt	Min. (inclusive)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id8147221				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies an inclusive lower bound for values.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	hd_id5081637				0	lt	Min. (exclusive)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id9759514				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies an exclusive lower bound for values.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	hd_id1614429				0	lt	Length				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id1589098				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the number of characters for a string.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	hd_id1278420				0	lt	Length (at least)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id8746910				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the minimum number of characters for a string.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	hd_id9636524				0	lt	Length (at most)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\xformsdatatab.xhp	0	help	par_id5675527				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the maximum number of characters for a string.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Web Pages				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156014	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/07/09000000.xhp\" name=\"Web Pages\"\>Web Pages\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146946	2			0	lt	To create a new web page for the Internet, open a new \<emph\>HTML Document\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284	3			0	lt	A tool for creating new web pages is the Web Layout mode, which you enable with \<emph\>View - Web Layout\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147285	8			0	lt	Creating a New Web Page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150808	9			0	lt	Switch to the web layout mode by choosing \<emph\>View - Web Layout\</emph\> or by opening a new HTML document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136	15			0	lt	To create an HTML page from your $[officename] document, save the page using one of the "HTML Document" file types.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Print File Directly				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153539				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>printing; directly\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153539	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Print File Directly\"\>Print File Directly\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398	2			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PrintDefault\"\>Click the \<emph\>Print File Directly\</emph\> icon to print the active document with the current default print settings.\</ahelp\> These can be found in the \<emph\>Printer Setup\</emph\> dialog, which you can call with the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Printer Settings\"\>\<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\>\</link\> menu command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275	3			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If you select text or a graphic and click the \<emph\>Print File Direct\</emph\> icon, you are prompted to print the selection or the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id9547105				0	lt	If the current document uses a printer that is not the default printer for your operating system, the \<emph\>Print File Direct \</emph\>icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Print\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10679				0	lt	If the current document uses a printer that is not the default printer that was specified in the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\"\>spadmin\</link\>, printer administration program, the \<emph\>Print File Direct \</emph\>icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Print\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Show Draw Functions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150476				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>Drawing bar\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines; draw functions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>polygon drawing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>freeform lines; draw functions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text boxes; positioning\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>headings; entering as text box\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text objects; draw functions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ticker text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; animating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>vertical callouts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>vertical text boxes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cube drawing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>triangle drawing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ellipse drawing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rectangle drawing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>shapes\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152363	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Show Draw Functions\"\>Show Draw Functions\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150789	72			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertDraw\"\>Click to open or close the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>bar, where you can add shapes, lines, text, and callouts to the current document.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10849				0	lt	You can switch on and off the Drawing toolbar of Writer and Calc documents using an icon on the Standard toolbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154288				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3153683\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertdraw.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153683\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153032	10			0	lt	Show Draw Functions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089D				0	lt	You can show and hide the \<emph\>Visible Buttons\</emph\>. Click the arrow at the end of the toolbar to access the \<emph\>Visible Buttons\</emph\> command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149398	11			0	lt	Selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3153824\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153824\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771	12			0	lt	Lets you select objects in the current document. To select an object, click the object with the arrow. To select more than one object, drag a selection frame around the objects. To add an object to a selection, press Shift, and then click the object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143270	13			0	lt	Line				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3147618\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_line.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147618\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922	64			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Line\"\>Draws a straight line where you drag in the current document. To constrain the line to 45 degrees, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360	71			0	lt	To enter text on a line, double-click the line and type or paste your text. The text direction corresponds to the direction you dragged to draw the line. To hide the line, select \<emph\>Invisible\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Line Style\</emph\> box on the \<emph\>Drawing Object Properties\</emph\> bar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152922	16			0	lt	Rectangle				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154125				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3158407\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_rect.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3158407\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147230	65			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Rect\"\>Draws a rectangle where you drag in the current document. To draw a square, hold down Shift while you drag. Click where you want to place a corner of the rectangle, and drag to the size you want.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153367	20			0	lt	Ellipse				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156443				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3153951\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_ellipse.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153951\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159197	21			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Ellipse\"\>Draws an oval where you drag in the current document. Click where you want to draw the oval, and drag to the size you want. To draw a circle, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155308	23			0	lt	Polygon				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154129				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3152576\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_polygon_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152576\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147214	24			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Polygon_Unfilled\"\>Draws a line composed of a series of straight line segments. Drag to draw a line segment, click to define the endpoint of the line segment, and then drag to draw a new line segment. Double-click to finish drawing the line. To create a closed shape, double-click the starting point of the line.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638	47			0	lt	Hold the Shift key while drawing a polygon to position new points at 45 degree angles.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319	48			0	lt	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05270000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points\"\>Edit Points\</link\> mode enables you to interactively modify the individual points of the polygon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153279	56			0	lt	Curve				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3149379\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezier_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149379\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148878	57			0	lt	\<variable id=\"kurvetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bezier_Unfilled\"\>Draws a smooth Bezier curve. Click where you want the curve to start, drag, release, and then move the pointer to where you want the curve to end and click. Move the pointer and click again to add a straight line segment to the curve. Double-click to finish drawing the curve. To create a closed shape, double click the starting point of the curve.\</ahelp\> The arc of the curve is determined by the distance you drag. \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148587	60			0	lt	Freeform Line				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3154510\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154510\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154163	61			0	lt	\<variable id=\"freihandtext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Freeline_Unfilled\"\>Draws a freeform line where you drag in the current document. To end the line, release the mouse button. To draw a closed shape, release the mouse button near the starting point of the line.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147259	27			0	lt	Arc				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156359				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3153710\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_arc.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153710\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148482	66			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Arc\"\>Draws an arc in the current document. To draw an arc, drag an oval to the size you want, and then click to define the starting point of the arc. Move your pointer to where you want to place the endpoint and click. You do not need to click on the oval. To draw an arc that is based on a circle, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153924	30			0	lt	Ellipse Pie				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154363				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3159186\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_pie.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159186\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156383	67			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Pie\"\>Draws a filled shape that is defined by the arc of an oval and two radius lines in the current document. To draw an ellipse pie, drag an oval to the size you want, and then click to define the first radius line. Move your pointer to where you want to place the second radius line and click. You do not need to click on the oval. To draw a circle pie, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154964	33			0	lt	Circle Segment				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3147315\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlecut.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147315\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149106	68			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CircleCut\"\>Draws a filled shape that is defined by the arc of a circle and a diameter line in the current document. To draw a circle segment, drag a circle to the size you want, and then click to define the starting point of the diameter line. Move your pointer to where you want to place the endpoint of the diameter line and click. You do not need to click on the circle. To draw an ellipse segment, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145150	36			0	lt	Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3155608\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_texttoolbox.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155608\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657	69			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DrawText\"\>Draws a text box with horizontal text direction where you drag in the current document. Drag a text box to the size you want anywhere in the document, and then type or paste your text. Rotate the text box to get rotated text.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158214	62			0	lt	Text Animation				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150380				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3152580\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_text_marquee.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152580\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826	63			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Text_Marquee\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts animated text with horizontal text direction into the current document. Drag a text box, and then type or paste your text. To assign an animation effect, choose \<emph\>Format - Text - Text Animation\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>\<variable id=\"lauftext\"\>Inserts animated text with horizontal text direction into the current document. \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149966	41			0	lt	Callouts				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153781				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3145256\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawcaption.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145256\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151274	70			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DrawCaption\"\>Draws a line that ends in a rectangular callout with horizontal text direction from where you drag in the current document. Drag a handle of the callout to resize the callout. To add text, click the edge of the callout, and then type or paste your text. To change a rectangular callout to a rounded callout, drag the largest corner handle when the pointer changes to a hand.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E50				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05270000.xhp\" name=\"Points\"\>Points\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E60				0	lt	Enables you to edit points on your drawing.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E75				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04140000.xhp\" name=\"From File\"\>From File\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E95				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/3dsettings_toolbar.xhp\"\>Extrusion On/Off\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10EA5				0	lt	Switches the 3D effects on and off for the selected objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149735	75			0	lt	Vertical Callouts				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156068				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3154818\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_verticalcaption.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154818\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150492	76			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:VerticalCaption\"\>Draws a line that ends in a rectangular callout with vertical text direction from where you drag in the current document. Drag a handle of the callout to resize the callout. To add text, click the edge of the callout, and then type or paste your text. To change a rectangular callout to a rounded callout, drag the largest corner handle when the pointer changes to a hand. Only available when Asian language support is enabled.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166437	77			0	lt	Vertical Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146929				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3154372\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_verticaltext.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154372\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152989	78			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:VerticalText\"\>Draws a text box with vertical text direction where you click or drag in the current document. Click anywhere in the document, and then type or paste your text. You can also move the cursor to where you want to add the text, drag a text box, and then type or paste your text. Only available when Asian language support is enabled.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555	74			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_graphic_drawit.xhp\" name=\"Tips\"\>Tips for working with the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>bar.\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Form Controls				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154142				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>form controls;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; form fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>form fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>command button creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>buttons; form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>push buttons;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>radio button creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>check box creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>labels; form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fixed text; form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text boxes;form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>list box creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>picklist creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drop-down lists in form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combo box creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; select mode\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154142	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Form Controls\"\>Form Controls\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151378	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"formulartext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Config\"\>The Form Controls toolbar contains tools that you need to create an interactive form.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can use the toolbar to add controls to a form in a text, spreadsheet, presentation, or HTML document, for example a button that runs a macro.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id1027200809391346				0	lt	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336	68			0	lt	Icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> toolbar (you may need to enable this initially invisible icon):				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155341				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3150943\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_config.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150943\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670	3			0	lt	Form Controls				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B21				0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xforms.xhp\"\>XML Form documents\</link\> (XForms) use the same controls.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152771	45			0	lt	To create a form, open a document and use the Form Controls toolbar to add and define the form controls. If you want, you can also link the form to a database, so that you can use the controls to manipulate a database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150791	46			0	lt	When you create a form in an HTML document, you can use the form to send data over the Internet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171	47			0	lt	%PRODUCTNAME only exports the form properties that are supported by the HTML version that you export to. To specify the HTML version, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C39				0	lt	To add a control to a document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154918	4			0	lt	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the icon of the control that you want to add.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C4D				0	lt	In the document, drag to create the control. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C50				0	lt	To create a square control field, hold down the Shift key while you drag.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154127	78			0	lt	To add a field from the field list of a table or query to a form, drag a cell into the form. In a text document, you can also drag a column header to add a field to a form. To include a label for the field, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift key down when you drag a column head.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C87				0	lt	Modifying a Control				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645	5			0	lt	Right-click the control and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>. A dialog opens where you can define the properties of the control.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363	163			0	lt	To specify a accelerator key for a control, add a tilde (~) in front of the character in the label for the control.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152792	135			0	lt	You can drag and drop controls from one document to another document. You can also copy and paste controls between documents. When you insert a control from another document, $[officename] analyzes the data source, content type, and content properties of the control so that the control fits the logical structure in the target document. For example, a control that displays contents from an address book continues to display the same contents after you copy the control to a different document. You can view these properties on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page of the \<emph\>Form properties\</emph\> dialog. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154411	24			0	lt	Select				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156106				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3153516\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153516\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150470	25			0	lt	This icon switches the mouse pointer to the select mode, or deactivates this mode. The select mode is used to select the controls of the current form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146914	10			0	lt	Check Box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148483				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3156380\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_checkbox.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156380\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153927	11			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CheckBox\"\>Creates a check box.\</ahelp\> Check boxes allow you to activate or deactivate a function in a form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153794	16			0	lt	Text Box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3163665				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3153266\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_edit.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153266\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444	17			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Edit\"\>Creates a text box.\</ahelp\> Text boxes are fields in which the user can enter text. In a form, text boxes display data or allow for new data input.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151218	124			0	lt	Formatted Field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154836				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3143277\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formattedfield.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3143277\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147547	125			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormattedField\"\>Creates a formatted field.\</ahelp\> A formatted field is a text box in which you can define how the inputs and outputs are formatted, and which limiting values apply.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155346	126			0	lt	A formatted field has \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170002.xhp\" name=\"special control properties\"\>special control properties\</link\> (choose \<emph\>Format - Control\</emph\>).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148774	6			0	lt	Push Button				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3151073\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertpushbutton.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151073\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147046	7			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Pushbutton\"\>Creates a push button.\</ahelp\> This function can be used to execute a command for a defined event, such as a mouse click.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731	138			0	lt	You can apply text and graphics to these buttons.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157844	8			0	lt	Option Button				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3152999\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_radiobutton.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152999\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123	9			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RadioButton\"\>Creates an option button.\</ahelp\> Option buttons enable the user to choose one of several options. Option buttons with the same functionality are given the same name (\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"Name\"\>\<emph\>Name\</emph\>\</link\>\<emph\>property\</emph\>). Normally, they are given a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"group box\"\>group box\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156064	18			0	lt	List Box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154326				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3154135\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_listbox.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154135\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428	19			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ListBox\"\>Creates a list box.\</ahelp\> A list box lets users select an entry from a list. If the form is linked to a database and the database connection is active, the\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"List Box Wizard\"\>\<emph\>List Box Wizard\</emph\>\</link\> will automatically appear after the list box is inserted in the document. This wizard helps you create the list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147171	20			0	lt	Combo Box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149981				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3148817\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_combobox.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148817\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149407	21			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ComboBox\"\>Creates a combo box.\</ahelp\> A combo box is a single-line list box with a drop-down list from which users choose an option. You can assign the "read-only" property to the combo box so that users cannot enter other entries than those found in the list. If the form is bound to a database and the database connection is active, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box Wizard\"\>\<emph\>Combo Box Wizard\</emph\>\</link\> will automatically appear after you insert the combo box in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145618	12			0	lt	Label Field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145295				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3151017\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertfixedtext.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151017\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148534	13			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Label\"\>Creates a field for displaying text.\</ahelp\> These labels are only for displaying predefined text. Entries cannot be made in these fields.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC6				0	lt	More Controls				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CDC				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/more_controls.xhp\"\>\<emph\>More Controls\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CF7				0	lt	Form Design				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D0D				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0226.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Form Design\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B57				0	lt	Wizards On/Off				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B65				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id6128727\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_usewizards.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6128727\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B76				0	lt	Turns on and turns off the automatic form controls wizards.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id6403088				0	lt	These wizards help you to enter the properties of list boxes, table controls, and other controls.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149436	134			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170001.xhp\" name=\"Context Menu Commands\"\>Context Menu Commands\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11A56				0	lt	Spin Button				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11A64				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id7816400\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_spinbutton.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7816400\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11A75				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SpinButton\"\>Creates a spin button.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id710776				0	lt	If you add a spin button to a Calc spreadsheet, you can use the Data tab page to create a two-way link between the spin button and a cell. As a result, when you change the contents of a cell, the contents of the spin button are updated. Conversely, if you change the value of the spin button, the contents of the cell are updated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11ABC				0	lt	Scrollbar				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11ACA				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id8203985\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_scrollbar.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8203985\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11ADB				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ScrollBar\"\>Creates a scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CA3				0	lt	You can specify the following properties for a scrollbar:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CDA				0	lt	UI name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CE0				0	lt	Semantics				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CE7				0	lt	Scroll value min				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CED				0	lt	Specifies the minimum height or the minimum width of a scrollbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CF4				0	lt	Scroll value max				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CFA				0	lt	Specifies the maximum height or the maximum width of a scrollbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D01				0	lt	Default scroll value				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D07				0	lt	Specifies the default value of a scrollbar, used when the form is reset.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D0E				0	lt	Orientation				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D14				0	lt	Specifies the orientation of a scrollbar, that is, horizontal or vertical.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D1B				0	lt	Small change				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D21				0	lt	Specifies the minimum amount by which you can scroll a scrollbar, for example, by clicking an arrow.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D28				0	lt	Large change				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D2E				0	lt	Specifies the amount that a large step scrolls a scrollbar, for example, when you click between the scrollbar thumb and a scrollbar arrow.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D35				0	lt	Delay				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D3B				0	lt	Specifies the delay in milliseconds between scrollbar trigger events. For example, the delay that occurs when you click an arrow button on the scrollbar and hold down the mouse button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D42				0	lt	Symbol color				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D48				0	lt	Specifies the color of the arrows on the scrollbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D4F				0	lt	Visible Size				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D55				0	lt	Specifies the size of the scrollbar thumb in "value units". For example, a value of ("Scroll value max." minus "Scroll value min.") / 2 results in a scrollbar thumb that occupies half of the scrollbar.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D58				0	lt	To make the width of the scrollbar equal to the height of the scrollbar, set the Visible Size to zero.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D63				0	lt	In a Calc spreadsheet, you can use the Data tab page to create a two-way link between a scrollbar and a cell.				20130618 17:22:18
