helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Special properties of a formatted field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>formatted fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774	131			0	lt	Special properties of a formatted field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	127			0	lt	\<emph\>Formatting\</emph\>: You can set the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>property by clicking the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button in the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> line of the \<emph\>Properties: Formatted Field\</emph\> dialog. The \<emph\>Number Format\</emph\> dialog appears.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443	128			0	lt	If the formatted field is connected to the text field of a database, the entries in this field will be treated as text. If the formatted field is connected to a field of the database that can be displayed as a number, the input is treated as numbers. The date and time are also handled internally as numbers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150976	129			0	lt	\<emph\>Min. value\</emph\> and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>: You can enter the minimum and maximum numeric value for a formatted field. The min and max values determine the output of existing data (Example: Min. value is 5, the connected database field contains the integer value 3. The output is 5, but the value in the database is not modified) and the input of new data (Example: Max. value is 10 and you enter 20. The input is corrected and 10 is written in the database). If the fields are not filled in for \<emph\>Min. value \</emph\>and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>, no limits will be applied. For formatted fields that are connected to a database text field, these two values and the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> do not apply.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665	130			0	lt	\<emph\>Default value\</emph\>: This value is set for new records as the default value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Special Tips for Date Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150445				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>date fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445	77			0	lt	Special Tips for Date Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230	75			0	lt	When you enter a year using two digits, the corresponding four digit value is determined by a setting in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\>. For example, if 1935 is set as the lower limiting value and you enter 34 as a date value, then the result is 2034 instead of 1934.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205	76			0	lt	The pre-set limit value will be saved for each document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Special Tips for Table Controls				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109850				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>table controls; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; properties of table controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table controls;keyboard-only edit mode\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850	124			0	lt	Special Tips for Table Controls				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539	51			0	lt	You can define a table control to display the records as you like. In other words you can define data fields for displaying or editing data like in a database form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152372	62			0	lt	The following fields are possible in a table control: text, date, time and currency field, numeric field, pattern field, check box and combo box. In the case of combined date/time fields, two columns are created automatically.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194	125			0	lt	The number of selected lines, if any are selected, is in parentheses after the total number of records.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155616	52			0	lt	To insert columns into the table control, click in the column heads and bring up the context menu. The following commands are available:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789	53			0	lt	Insert Column				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750	54			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_INSERTCOL\"\>Calls a submenu to select a data field to adopt it in the table control.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552	59			0	lt	Configure the table control using drag and drop: Open the data source browser and drag the desired fields out of the data source browser and on to the column heads of the table control. A pre-configured column is created.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149827	55			0	lt	Replace with				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	56			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_CHANGECOL\"\>Opens a submenu to select a data field to replace the data field selected in the table control.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267	57			0	lt	Delete Column				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958	58			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETECOL\"\>Deletes the currently selected column.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275	73			0	lt	Column				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996	74			0	lt	Opens the properties dialog of the selected column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148539	79			0	lt	Hide Columns				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157	80			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_HIDECOL\"\>Hides the selected column.\</ahelp\> Its properties are not changed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771	81			0	lt	Show columns				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400	82			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS\"\>Calls a submenu where you can select the columns to show again.\</ahelp\> To show only one column, click the column name. You see only the first 16 hidden columns. If there are more hidden columns, choose the \<emph\>More\</emph\> command to call the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193	83			0	lt	More				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159269	84			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS_MORE\"\>Calls the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	85			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVX_DLG_SHOWGRIDCOLUMNS:1\"\>In the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog you can select the columns to be shown. Hold down the Shift or Ctrl (Mac: Command) key to select multiple entries.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561	86			0	lt	All				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	87			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWALLCOLS\"\>Click \<emph\>All \</emph\>if you want to show all columns.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153349	127			0	lt	Keyboard-only control of Table Controls				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149416	126			0	lt	If you use the keyboard only to travel through controls in your document, you will find one difference to the other types of controls: the Tab key does not move the cursor to the next control, but moves to the next column inside the table control. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the next control, or press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the previous control.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153062	128			0	lt	To enter the special keyboard-only edit mode for Table Controls:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510	129			0	lt	The form document must be in \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"design mode\"\>design mode\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758	130			0	lt	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to select the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3161657	131			0	lt	Press Shift+F4 to select the first control. If the Table Control is not the first control, press Tab until it is selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056	132			0	lt	Press Enter to enter the edit mode. The handles are shown farther out from the control border.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938	133			0	lt	In the edit mode, you can open the edit mode context menu by pressing Shift+F10.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365	134			0	lt	If you want to edit columns, press Shift+Space to enter column edit mode. Now you can rearrange the order of columns with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow keys. The Delete key deletes the current column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419	135			0	lt	Press the Escape key to exit the edit mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Control Properties				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147102				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>controls; properties of form controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>properties; form controls\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147102	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170100.xhp\" name=\"Control Properties\"\>Control Properties\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"kontroll\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ControlProperties\"\>Opens a dialog for editing the properties of a selected control.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3157910	17			0	lt	\<variable id=\"hinweis\"\>You can only call the\<emph\> Properties\</emph\> dialog when in the Design mode with a control selected. \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153760	3			0	lt	If you enter data in the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog, note that multiline input is possible for certain drop-down combo boxes. This concerns all fields in which an SQL statement can be entered, as well as the properties of text boxes or label fields. You can open these fields and enter text in the opened list. The following shortcut keys are valid:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148686	18			0	lt	Keys				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155390	19			0	lt	Effects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	4			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Down Arrow				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150944	5			0	lt	Opens the combo box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153627	6			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Up Arrow				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153063	7			0	lt	Closes the combo box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413	8			0	lt	Shift+Enter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811	9			0	lt	Inserts a new line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379	10			0	lt	Up Arrow				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192	11			0	lt	Places the cursor into the previous line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933	12			0	lt	Down Arrow				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041	13			0	lt	Places the cursor into the next line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153178	14			0	lt	Enter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228	15			0	lt	Completes the input in the field and places the cursor into the next field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422	16			0	lt	As with list boxes or combo boxes, you can open or close the list with a mouse click at the arrow on the right end of the field. However, the input here can be entered either in the opened list or in the top text field. An exception is the properties that expect a list representation, for example, the property \<emph\>List Entries\</emph\>, which can be set for the control fields \<emph\>List Box\</emph\> and \<emph\>Combo Box\</emph\>. Here, you can only edit the entries when the field is opened.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	General				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153681	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>General\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233	2			0	lt	This \<emph\>General \</emph\>tab enables you to define the general properties of a form control. These properties differ, depending on the control type. Not all of the following properties are available for every control.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155342	172			0	lt	If you export the current form document to HTML format, the default control values are exported, not the current control values. Default values are determined - depending on the type of control - by the properties' Default value (for example, in text fields), Default status (for check boxes and option fields), and Default selection (for list boxes).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149734	13			0	lt	Enabled				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	14			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ENABLED\"\>If a control field has the property "Enabled" (Yes), the form user will be able to use the control field.\</ahelp\> If the property is disabled, it will not be enabled (No) and will be displayed in a gray color.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153320	74			0	lt	Line count				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235	75			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LINECOUNT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies how many lines should be displayed in the dropdown list. This setting is only active if you chose "Yes" in the "Dropdown" option.\</ahelp\>For combo boxes with the Dropdown property, you can specify how many lines should be displayed in the dropdown list. With control fields which do not have the Dropdown option, the line's display will be specified by the size of the control field and the font size.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153147	23			0	lt	Action				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415	24			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BUTTONTYPE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The Action property determines the action that occurs when you activate a button.\</ahelp\>You can use navigation actions to design your own database navigation buttons.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152474	25			0	lt	The following table describes the actions that you can assign to a button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303	224			0	lt	Action				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154388	225			0	lt	Description				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154071	26			0	lt	None				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153797	27			0	lt	No action occurs.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216	30			0	lt	Submit form				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228	31			0	lt	Sends the data that is entered in other control fields of the current form to the address that is specified in \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170200.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\> under \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"URL\"\>\<emph\>URL\</emph\>\</link\>. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F7				0	lt	Enter the URL into the form's data property "URL" text box when you export to a PDF file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041	28			0	lt	Reset form				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155101	29			0	lt	Resets the settings in other control fields to the predefined defaults (Default Status, Default Selection, Default Value).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155431	32			0	lt	Open document / web page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010	33			0	lt	Opens the URL that is specified under \<emph\>URL\</emph\>. You can use \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> to specify the target frame.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FE				0	lt	First record				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10803				0	lt	Moves the current form to the first record.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	lt	Previous record				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1080E				0	lt	Moves the current form to the previous record.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10814				0	lt	Next record				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10819				0	lt	Moves the current form to the next record.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081F				0	lt	Last record				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10824				0	lt	Moves the current form to the last record.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082A				0	lt	Save record				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	lt	Saves the current record, if necessary.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10835				0	lt	Undo data entry				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083A				0	lt	Reverses the changes in the current record.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10840				0	lt	New record				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10845				0	lt	Moves the current form to the insert row.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084B				0	lt	Delete record				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10850				0	lt	Deletes the current record.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10856				0	lt	Refresh form				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1085B				0	lt	Reloads the most recently saved version of the current form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154638	19			0	lt	Dropdown				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577	20			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DROPDOWN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether the combo box should dropdown (Yes) or not (No).\</ahelp\>A control field with the dropdown property has an additional arrow button which opens the list of the existing form entries per mouse click. Under \<emph\>Line count\</emph\>, you can specify how many lines (or rows) should be displayed in the dropdown state. Combination fields can have the dropdown property.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159198	182			0	lt	Combo boxes that were inserted as columns in a table control are always dropdown as the default.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153140	11			0	lt	Alignment / Graphics alignment				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151281	12			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALIGN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the alignment option for text or graphics that are used on a control.\</ahelp\>The alignment options are left-aligned, right-aligned, and centered. These options are available for the following elements:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109DD				0	lt	Title of Label fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E1				0	lt	Content of text fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E5				0	lt	Content of table fields in the columns of a table control				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E9				0	lt	Graphics or text that are used in buttons				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EC				0	lt	The \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> option for buttons is called \<emph\>Graphics alignment\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151073	76			0	lt	AutoFill				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152375	77			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_AUTOCOMPLETE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Assigns the AutoFill function to a combo box.\</ahelp\>The AutoFill function displays a list of previous entries after you start to type an entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729	216			0	lt	Label field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801	217			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CONTROLLABEL\"\>Specifies the source for the label of the control.\</ahelp\> The text of the label field will be used instead of the name of a database field. For example, in the \<emph\>Filter Navigator\</emph\>, \<emph\>Search\</emph\> dialog, and as a column name in the table view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153223	231			0	lt	To define one character of the label as a mnemonic, so that the user can access this control by pressing the character on the keyboard, insert a tilde (~) character in front of the character in the label.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154502	218			0	lt	Only the text of a group frame can be used as the label field when using radio buttons. This text applies to all of the radio buttons of the same group.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148587	219			0	lt	If you click on the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button next to the text field, you will see the \<emph\>Label Field Selection\</emph\> dialog. Select a label from the list.				20130618 17:22:18
