helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11391				0	lt	This control is named "Multiline input" for a text column inside a table control.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN114EF				0	lt	Word break				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11505				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays text on more than one line.\</ahelp\> Allows you to use line breaks in a text box, so that you can enter more than one line of text. To manually enter a line break, press the Enter key.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11538				0	lt	Toggle				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1154E				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies if a Push Button behaves as a Toggle Button. If you set Toggle to "Yes", you can switch between the "selected" and "not selected" control states when you click the button or press the spacebar while the the control has the focus. A button in the "selected" state appears "pressed in".\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11558				0	lt	Take Focus on Click				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1156E				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you set this option to "Yes", the Push Button receives the focus when you click the button.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11578				0	lt	Hide selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1158E				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"37965\"\>Specifies whether a text selection on a control remains selected when a the focus is no longer on a control.\</ahelp\> If you set \<emph\>Hide selection\</emph\> to "No", the selected text remains selected when the focus is no longer on the control that contains the text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11598				0	lt	Style				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115AE				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"37966\"\>Specifies whether Check boxes and Option buttons are displayed in a 3D look (default) or a flat look.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115B8				0	lt	Border color				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115CE				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"37967\"\>Specifies the border color for controls that have the Border property set to "flat".\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115B7				0	lt	Symbol color				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN115BB				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the color for symbols on controls, for example the arrows on a scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149314	131			0	lt	Date min				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155755	132			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the earliest date that a user can enter.\</ahelp\>Determines the earliest date that a user can enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152866	133			0	lt	Value min				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147505	134			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can determine here a value for the control field to prevent the user from entering a smaller value.\</ahelp\>For numerical and currency fields you can determine a minimum value to prevent the user from entering a smaller value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153298	135			0	lt	Time min				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148831	136			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TIMEMIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the minimum time that a user can enter.\</ahelp\>Determines the minimum time that a user can enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155746	137			0	lt	Decimal accuracy				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146096	138			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DECIMAL_ACCURACY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the number of digits displayed to the right of the decimal point.\</ahelp\>With numerical and currency fields you can determine the number of digits displayed to the right of the decimal point.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151340	9			0	lt	Name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819	10			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAME\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>On the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> tab page, this option specifies the name for the control field. On the \<emph\>Form Properties \</emph\>tab page, this option specifies the name for the form.\</ahelp\>Each control field and each form has a \<emph\>Name \</emph\>property through which it can be identified. The name will appear in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\> and, using the name, the control field can be referred to from a macro. The default settings already specify a name which is constructed from using the field's label and number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025	191			0	lt	If you work with macros, make sure that the names of the controls are unique.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146325				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>controls; grouping\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>groups;of controls\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>forms; grouping controls\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146325	192			0	lt	The name is also used to group different controls that belong together functionally, such as radio buttons. To do so, give the same name to all members of the group: controls with identical names form a group. Grouped controls can be represented visually by using a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Group Box\"\>Group Box\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149720	197			0	lt	Navigation bar				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149918	198			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAVIGATIONBAR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to display the navigation bar on the lower border of the table control.\</ahelp\>Specifies whether to display the navigation bar on the lower border of table controls.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158426	42			0	lt	Read-only				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153215	43			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_READONLY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines if the control is read-only (Yes) or if it can be edited (No).\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Read-only \</emph\>property can be assigned to all controls in which the user can enter text. If you assign the read-only property to an image field which uses graphics from a database, the user will not be able to insert new graphics into the database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148912	139			0	lt	Border				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637	140			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BORDER\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines if the field's border should be displayed "Without frame", with a "3-D look" or "Flat".\</ahelp\>With control fields that have a frame, you can determine the border display on the form using the \<emph\>Border \</emph\>property. You can select among the "Without frame", "3-D look" or "Flat" options.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149266	44			0	lt	Tab order				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147483	45			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TABINDEX\"\>The \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\> property determines the order in which the controls are focused in the form when you press the Tab key.\</ahelp\> In a form that contains more than one control, the focus moves to the next control when you press the Tab key. You can specify the order in which the focus changes with an index under \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156207	193			0	lt	The \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\> property is not available to \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Hidden Controls\"\>Hidden Controls\</link\>. If you want, you can also set this property for image buttons and image controls, so that you can select these controls with the Tab key.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150378	46			0	lt	When creating a form, an index is automatically assigned to the control fields that are added to this form; every control field added is assigned an index increased by 1. If you change the index of a control, the indices of the other controls are updated automatically. Elements that cannot be focused (Tabstop = No) are also assigned a value. However, these controls are skipped when using the Tab key.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640	47			0	lt	You can also easily define the indices of the different controls in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170300.xhp\" name=\"Tab Order\"\>\<emph\>Tab Order\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0509200912114423				0	lt	Mouse wheel scroll				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200912114566				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets whether the value changes when the user scrolls a mouse wheel. Never: No change of the value. When focused: (default) The value changes when the control has the focus and the wheel is pointing at the control and gets scrolled. Always: The value changes when the wheel is pointing at the control and gets scrolled, no matter which control has the focus.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154049	34			0	lt	Default status				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150837	35			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_CHECKED\"\>Specifies whether an option or a check box is selected by default.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149242	201			0	lt	For a reset type button, you can define the status of the control if the reset button is activated by the user.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156266	202			0	lt	For grouped option fields, the status of the group corresponding to the default setting is defined by the \<emph\>Default Status\</emph\> property.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156150	36			0	lt	Default selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148730	37			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_SELECT_SEQ\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the list box entry to mark as the default entry.\</ahelp\>Specifies the list box entry to mark as the default entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150028	203			0	lt	For a Reset type button, the\<emph\> Default selection\</emph\> entry defines the status of the list box if the reset button is activated by the user.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id919217				0	lt	For a List box that contains a value list, you can click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to open the \<emph\>Default selection\</emph\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id50050				0	lt	In the \<emph\>Default selection\</emph\> dialog, select the entries that you want to mark as selected when you open the form that contains the list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150460	38			0	lt	Default value				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222	39			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEDEFAULT\"\>Sets the default value for the control field.\</ahelp\> For example, the default value will be entered when a form is opened.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740	199			0	lt	For a Reset type button, the\<emph\> Default value entry \</emph\>defines the status of the control if the reset button is activated by the user.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B70				0	lt	Default scroll value				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B74				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_SCROLLVALUE\"\>Sets the default value for the scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155440	252			0	lt	Scroll value max.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148877	251			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SCROLLVALUE_MAX\"\>Specify the maximum value of a scrollbar control.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
