helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN1108D				0	lt	Selection is linked: Position of the selected item is copied into the linked cell. For example, if the third item is selected, the number 3 will be copied.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN11094				0	lt	Select several list items				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN1109A				0	lt	#NV is entered into the linked cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110A1				0	lt	Deselect all list items				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110A7				0	lt	Contents are linked: Linked cell is cleared				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110AA				0	lt	Selection is linked: Value 0 is entered in the linked cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110B1				0	lt	Enter text or a number into the linked cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110B7				0	lt	Contents are linked: Find and select an equal list item				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110BA				0	lt	Selection is linked: The list item at the specified position (starting with 1 for the first item) is selected. If not found, all items are deselected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110C1				0	lt	Enter a formula into the linked cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110C7				0	lt	Find and select a list item that matches the formula result and link mode				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110CE				0	lt	Clear the linked cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110D4				0	lt	Deselect all items in the list box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110DB				0	lt	Change the contents of the list source range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110E1				0	lt	List box items are updated according to the change. The selection is preserved. This may cause an update to the linked cell.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110EC				0	lt	Combo box with linked cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110F9				0	lt	Action				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN110FF				0	lt	Result				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN11106				0	lt	Enter text into the edit field of the combo box, or select an entry from the drop-down list				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN1110C				0	lt	Text is copied into the linked cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN11113				0	lt	Clear the edit field of the combo box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN11119				0	lt	Linked cell is cleared				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN11120				0	lt	Enter text or a number into the linked cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN11126				0	lt	Text or number is copied into the edit field of the combo box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN1112D				0	lt	Enter a formula into the linked cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN11133				0	lt	Formula result is copied into the edit field of the combo box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN1113A				0	lt	Clear the linked cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN11140				0	lt	Edit field of the combo box is cleared				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN11147				0	lt	Change the contents of the list source range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN1114D				0	lt	Drop-down list items are updated according to the change. The edit field of the combo box and the linked cell are not changed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN11163				0	lt	Contents of the linked cell				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN11167				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CELL_EXCHANGE_TYPE\"\>Select the mode of linking a list box with a linked cell on a spreadsheet.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN11179				0	lt	Linked contents: Synchronize the text contents of the selected list box entry with the cell contents. Select "The selected entry"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN1117D				0	lt	Linked selection position: The position of the single selected item in the list box is synchronized with the numerical value in the cell. Select "Position of the selected entry"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN1118B				0	lt	Source cell range				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN111A1				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LIST_CELL_RANGE\"\>Enter a cell range that contains the entries for a list box or combo box on a spreadsheet.\</ahelp\> If you enter a multi-column range, only the contents of the leftmost column are used to fill the control.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Events				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148643				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>controls; events\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>events; controls\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>macros; assigning to events in forms\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148643	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170103.xhp\" name=\"Events\"\>Events\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152350	2			0	lt	On the\<emph\> Events \</emph\>tab page you can link macros to events that occur in a form's control fields.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419	40			0	lt	When the event occurs, the linked macro will be called. To assign a macro to an event, press the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button. An \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05060700.xhp\" name=\"Assign Macro\"\>Assign Macro\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>dialog\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> opens.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149732	3			0	lt	Depending on the control, different events are available. Only the available events for the selected control and context are listed on the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab page. The following events are defined:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149191	12			0	lt	Approve action				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153717	13			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVEACTIONPERFORMED\"\>This event takes place before an action is triggered by clicking the control.\</ahelp\> For example, clicking a "Submit" button initiates a send action; however, the actual "send" process is started only when the \<emph\>When initiating\</emph\> event occurs. The \<emph\>Approve action\</emph\> event allows you to kill the process. If the linked method sends back FALSE, \<emph\>When initiating\</emph\> will not be executed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024	36			0	lt	Execute action				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609	37			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ACTIONPERFORMED\"\>The \<emph\>Execute action\</emph\> event occurs when an action is started.\</ahelp\> For example, if you have a "Submit" button in your form, the send process represents the action to be initiated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156343	41			0	lt	Changed				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148755	42			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_CHANGED\"\>The\<emph\> Changed \</emph\>event takes place when the control loses the focus and the content of the control has changed since it lost the focus.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153524	10			0	lt	Text modified				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150495	11			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_TEXTCHANGED\"\>The\<emph\> Text modified \</emph\>event takes place if you enter or modify a text in an input field.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154123	8			0	lt	Item status changed				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870	9			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ITEMSTATECHANGED\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The\<emph\> Item status changed \</emph\>event takes place if the status of the control field has changed.\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Item status changed\</emph\> event takes place if he status of the control field has changed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151176	16			0	lt	When receiving focus				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154218	17			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_FOCUSGAINED\"\>The\<emph\> When receiving focus \</emph\>event takes place if a control field receives the focus.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150447	18			0	lt	When losing focus				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3159252	19			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_FOCUSLOST\"\>The\<emph\> When losing focus \</emph\>event takes place if a control field looses the focus.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147287	20			0	lt	Key pressed				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152940	21			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_KEYTYPED\"\>The \<emph\>Key pressed \</emph\>event occurs when the user presses any key while the control has the focus.\</ahelp\> This event may be linked to a macro for checking entries.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154127	43			0	lt	Key released				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154150	44			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_KEYUP\"\>The\<emph\> Key released \</emph\>event occurs when the user releases any key while the control has the focus.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154921	26			0	lt	Mouse inside				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618	27			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEENTERED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse inside \</emph\>event takes place if the mouse is inside the control field.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148576	30			0	lt	Mouse moved while key pressed				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	31			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEDRAGGED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse moved while key pressed \</emph\>event takes place when the mouse is dragged while a key is pressed.\</ahelp\> An example is when, during drag-and-drop, an additional key determines the mode (move or copy).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149262	32			0	lt	Mouse moved				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	33			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEMOVED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse moved \</emph\>event occurs if the mouse moves over the control.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159197	22			0	lt	Mouse button pressed				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145271	23			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEPRESSED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse button pressed \</emph\>event occurs if the mouse button is pressed while the mouse pointer is on the control.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BD				0	lt	Note that this event is also used for notifying requests for a popup context menu on the control.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148880	24			0	lt	Mouse button released				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150659	25			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSERELEASED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse button released \</emph\>event occurs if the mouse button is released while the mouse pointer is on the control.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156286	28			0	lt	Mouse outside				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582	29			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_MOUSEEXITED\"\>The\<emph\> Mouse outside \</emph\>event takes place when the mouse is outside the control field.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Form Properties				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147285				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>forms; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>properties; forms\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147285	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170200.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"form\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormProperties\" visibility=\"visible\"\>In this dialog you can specify, among others,  the data source and the events for the whole form.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	General				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152551				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>submitting forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>get method for form transmissions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>post method for form transmissions\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>General\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539	23			0	lt	A form is a text document or spreadsheet with different form controls. If you create a form for a Web page, the user can enter data into it to send over the Internet. The data from the form controls of a form is transmitted to a server by specifying a URL and can be processed on the server.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149283	20			0	lt	Name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150789	24			0	lt	Specifies a name for the form. This name is used to identify the form in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152425	33			0	lt	URL				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226	34			0	lt	Specifies the URL to which the data of the completed form is to be transmitted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154751	31			0	lt	Frame				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	32			0	lt	Defines the target frame in which the loaded URL is to appear.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152551	27			0	lt	Type of submission				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338	28			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SUBMIT_METHOD\"\>Specifies the method to transfer the completed form information.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145065	29			0	lt	Using the "Get" method, the data of every control is transmitted as an environment variable. They are appended to the URL in the form "?Control1=Content1&Control2=Content2&..."; the character string is analyzed by a program on the recipient's server.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443	30			0	lt	Using the "Post" method, a document is created from the content of the form that is sent to the specified URL.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275	26			0	lt	Submission encoding				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147	35			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SUBMIT_ENCODING\"\>Specifies the type for encoding the data transfer.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419	36			0	lt	Data transfer of control information				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153717	37			0	lt	When sending a form, all controls available in $[officename] are taken into consideration. The name of the control and the corresponding value, if available, are transmitted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252	50			0	lt	Which values are transmitted in each case depends on the respective control. For text fields, the visible entries are transmitted; for list boxes, the selected entries are transmitted; for check boxes and option fields, the associated reference values are transmitted if these fields were activated.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984	51			0	lt	How this information is transmitted depends on the selected transfer method (Get or Post) and the coding (URL or Multipart). If the Get method and URL encoding are selected, for example, value pairs in the form <Name>=<Value> are sent.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3157909	52			0	lt	In addition to the controls that are recognized in HTML, $[officename] offers other controls. It should be noted that, for fields with a specific numerical format, the visible values are not transmitted but rather fixed default formats. The following table shows how the data of the $[officename]-specific controls is transmitted:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153698	38			0	lt	Control				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562	39			0	lt	Value Pair				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153823	40			0	lt	Numeric field, currency field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734	41			0	lt	A decimal separator is always displayed as a period.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563	42			0	lt	Date field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794	43			0	lt	The date format is sent in a fixed format (MM-DD-YYYY), regardless of the user's local settings.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670	44			0	lt	Time field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153779	45			0	lt	The time format is sent in a fixed format (HH:MM:SS), regardless of the user's local settings.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361	46			0	lt	Pattern field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419	47			0	lt	The values of pattern fields are sent as text fields, that is, the value visible in the form is sent.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767	48			0	lt	Table control				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933	49			0	lt	From the table control, the individual columns are always transmitted. The name of the control, the name of the column, and the value of the column are sent. Using the Get method with URL encoding, the transmission is done in the form <Name of the table control>.<Name of the column>=<Value>, for example, with the value being dependent on the column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Events				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150499				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>forms; events\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>events;in forms\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170202.xhp\" name=\"Events\"\>Events\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3147043	2			0	lt	The\<emph\> Events \</emph\>tab page, allows you to assign a macro to certain events which occur in a form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233	3			0	lt	To link an event with a macro, first write a macro that contains all the commands to be executed when the event happens. Then assign this macro to the respective event by clicking the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button beside the corresponding event. The\<emph\> Assign Macro \</emph\>dialog opens, where you can select the macro.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182	29			0	lt	The following actions can be configured individually, meaning that you can use your own dialogs to depict an action:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	30			0	lt	Displaying an error message,				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996	31			0	lt	Confirming a delete process (for data records),				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541	32			0	lt	Querying parameters,				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3155261	33			0	lt	Checking input when saving a data record.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127	34			0	lt	For example, you can issue a "confirm deletion" request such as "Really delete customer xyz?" when deleting a data record.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200920562590				0	lt	The events that are shown in the Events dialog cannot be edited directly. You can delete an event from the list by pressing the Del key.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986	4			0	lt	The following lists and describes all events in a form that can be linked to a macro:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559	17			0	lt	Before update				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	56			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Before update event occurs before the control content changed by the user is written into the data source.\</ahelp\> The linked macro can, for example, prevent this action by returning "FALSE".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153779	19			0	lt	After update				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360	57			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_AFTERUPDATE\"\>The After update event occurs after the control content changed by the user has been written into the data source.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157909	36			0	lt	Prior to reset				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3155390	51			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVERESETTED\"\>The\<emph\> Prior to reset \</emph\>event occurs before a form is reset.\</ahelp\> The linked macro can, for example, prevent this action by returning "FALSE".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236	52			0	lt	A form is reset if one of the following conditions is met:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164	53			0	lt	The user presses an (HTML) button that is defined as a reset button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666	54			0	lt	A new and empty record is created in a form that is linked to a data source. For example, in the last record, the \<emph\>Next Record\</emph\> button may be pressed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156119	37			0	lt	After resetting				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563	55			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_RESETTED\"\>The\<emph\> After resetting \</emph\>event occurs after a form has been reset.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150870	27			0	lt	Before submitting				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152	28			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_SUBMITTED\"\>The\<emph\> Before submitting \</emph\>event occurs before the form data is sent.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149167	5			0	lt	When loading				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423	6			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_LOADED\"\>The\<emph\> When loading \</emph\>event occurs directly after the form has been loaded.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148451	38			0	lt	Before reloading				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154218	39			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_RELOADING\"\>The\<emph\> Before reloading \</emph\>event occurs before the form is reloaded.\</ahelp\> The data content has not yet been refreshed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155102	40			0	lt	When reloading				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3157895	41			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_RELOADED\"\>The\<emph\> When reloading \</emph\>event occurs directly after the form has been reloaded.\</ahelp\> The data content has already been refreshed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152792	42			0	lt	Before unloading				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152598	43			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_UNLOADING\"\>The\<emph\> Before unloading \</emph\>event occurs before the form is unloaded; that is, separated from its data source.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154145	44			0	lt	When unloading				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638	45			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_UNLOADED\"\>The\<emph\> When unloading \</emph\>event occurs directly after the form has been unloaded; that is, separated from its data source.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147426	25			0	lt	Confirm deletion				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154988	26			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_CONFIRMDELETE\"\>The\<emph\> Confirm deletion \</emph\>event occurs as soon as data has been deleted from the form.\</ahelp\> For example, the linked macro can request confirmation in a dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149481	46			0	lt	Before record action				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156007	58			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVEROWCHANGE\"\>The\<emph\> Before record action \</emph\>event occurs before the current record is changed.\</ahelp\> For example, the linked macro can request confirmation in a dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145749	47			0	lt	After record action				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	59			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ROWCHANGE\"\>The\<emph\> After record action \</emph\>event occurs directly after the current record has been changed.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154012	48			0	lt	Before record change				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	60			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_POSITIONING\"\>The\<emph\> Before record change \</emph\>event occurs before the current record pointer is changed.\</ahelp\>. For example, the linked macro can prevent this action by returning "FALSE".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157975	49			0	lt	After record change				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098	61			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_POSITIONED\"\>The\<emph\> After record change \</emph\>event occurs directly after the current record pointer has been changed.\</ahelp\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151076	50			0	lt	Fill parameters				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396	62			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVEPARAMETER\"\>The\<emph\> Fill parameters \</emph\>event occurs when the form to be loaded has parameters that must be filled out.\</ahelp\> For example, the data source of the form can be the following SQL command:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148773	63			0	lt	SELECT * FROM address WHERE name=:name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149581	64			0	lt	Here :name is a parameter that must be filled out when loading. The parameter is automatically filled out from the parent form if possible. If the parameter cannot be filled out, this event is called and a linked macro can fill out the parameter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146926	9			0	lt	Error occurred				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485	10			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ERROROCCURED\"\>The\<emph\> Error occurred \</emph\>event is activated if an error occurs when accessing the data source.\</ahelp\> This applies to forms, list boxes and combo boxes.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Data				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150040				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>forms; data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; forms and subforms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; subforms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subforms; description\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>Data\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242	2			0	lt	The\<emph\> Data \</emph\>tab page defines the form properties that refer to the database that is linked to the form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398	107			0	lt	Defines the data source on which the form is based, or specifies whether the data can be edited by the user. Apart from the sort and filter functions, you will also find all the necessary properties to create a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154810	5			0	lt	Data source				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349	16			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATASOURCE\"\>Defines the data source to which the form should refer.\</ahelp\> If you click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button, you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, where you can choose a data source.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146948	6			0	lt	Content				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922	17			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURSORSOURCE\"\>Determines the content to be used for the form. The content can be an existing table or a query (previously created in the database), or it can be defined by an SQL-statement. Before you enter a content you have to define the exact type in \<emph\>Content type\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149657	27			0	lt	If you have selected either "Table" or "Query" in \<emph\>Content type\</emph\>, the box lists all the tables and queries set up in the selected database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148755	7			0	lt	Content type				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541	19			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURSORSOURCETYPE\"\>Defines whether the data source is to be an existing database table or query, or if the form is to be generated based on an SQL statement.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192	29			0	lt	If you choose "Table" or "Query", the form will refer to the table or query that you specify under \<emph\>Content\</emph\>. If you want to create a new query or a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>, then you have to choose the "SQL" option. You can then enter the statement for the SQL query or the subform directly in the \<emph\>List content\</emph\> box on the Control properties Data tab page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158409	105			0	lt	Analyze SQL command				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171	106			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ESCAPE_PROCESSING\"\>Specifies whether the SQL statement is to be analyzed by %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\> If set to Yes, you can click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button next to the \<emph\>Content\</emph\> list box. This will open a window where you can graphically create a database query. When you close that window, the SQL statement for the created query will be inserted in the \<emph\>Content\</emph\> list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684	81			0	lt	Filter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449	82			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FILTER_CRITERIA\"\>Enter the required conditions for filtering the data in the form. The filter specifications follow SQL rules without using the WHERE clause.\</ahelp\> For example, if you want to display all records with the "Mike" forename, type into the data field: Forename = 'Mike'. You can also combine conditions: Forename = 'Mike' OR Forename = 'Peter'. All records matching either of these two conditions will be displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156212	83			0	lt	The filter function is available in user mode through the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12030000.xhp\" name=\"AutoFilter\"\>\<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\>\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12090000.xhp\" name=\"Default Filter\"\>\<emph\>Default Filter\</emph\>\</link\> icons on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigation Bar\"\>\<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> Bar\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156005	84			0	lt	Sort				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3163712	85			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SORT_CRITERIA\"\>Specifies the conditions to sort the data in the form. The specification of the sorting conditions follows SQL rules without the use of the ORDER BY clause.\</ahelp\> For example, if you want all records of a database to be sorted in one field in an ascending order and in another field in a descending order, enter Forename ASC, Name DESC (presuming Forename and Name are the names of the data fields).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444	86			0	lt	The appropriate icons on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigation Bar\"\>\<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> Bar\</link\> can be used in User mode to sort: \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12010000.xhp\" name=\"Sort Ascending\"\>\<emph\>Sort Ascending\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12020000.xhp\" name=\"Sort Descending\"\>\<emph\>Sort Descending\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100100.xhp\" name=\"Sort\"\>\<emph\>Sort\</emph\>\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148616	8			0	lt	Add data only				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153139	20			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATAENTRY\"\>Determines if the form only allows the addition of new data (Yes) or if it allows other properties as well (No).\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575	21			0	lt	If \<emph\>Add data only\</emph\> is set to "Yes", changing or deleting data is not possible.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148455	9			0	lt	Navigation bar				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157976	22			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAVIGATION\"\>Specifies whether the navigation functions in the lower form bar can be used.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485	79			0	lt	The "Parent Form" option is used for subforms. If you choose this option for a subform, you can navigate using the records of the main form if the cursor is placed in the subform. A subform is linked to the parent form by a 1:1 relationship, so navigation is always performed in the parent form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151051	10			0	lt	Cycle				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	23			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CYCLE\"\>Determines how the navigation should be done using the tab key.\</ahelp\> Using the tab key, you can move forward in the form. If you simultaneously press the Shift key, the navigation will follow the opposite direction. If you reach the last (or the first) field and press the tab key again, it can have various effects. Define the key control with the following options:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413	87			0	lt	Option				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150424	88			0	lt	Meaning				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150417	89			0	lt	Default				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157847	90			0	lt	This setting automatically defines a cycle which follows an existing database link: If the form contains a database link, the Tab key will, by default, initiate a change to the next or previous record on exit from the last field (see All Records). If there is no database link the next/previous form is shown (see Current Page).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418	91			0	lt	All records				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3152972	92			0	lt	This option applies to database forms only and is used to navigate through all records. If you use the Tab key to exit from the last field of a form, the current record is changed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020	93			0	lt	Active record				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3145301	94			0	lt	This option applies to database forms only, and is used to navigate within the current record. If you use the Tab key to exit from the last field of a form, the current record is changed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3146913	95			0	lt	Current page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150330	96			0	lt	On exit from the last field of a form, the cursor skips to the first field in the next form. This is standard for HTML forms; therefore, this option is especially relevant for HTML forms.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155064	11			0	lt	Allow additions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360	24			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALLOW_ADDITIONS\"\>Determines if data can be added.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156054	12			0	lt	Allow modifications				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156377	25			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALLOW_EDITS\"\> Determines if the data can be modified.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149019	13			0	lt	Allow deletions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148995	26			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALLOW_DELETIONS\"\>Determines if the data can be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153714	3			0	lt	Link master fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339	14			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_MASTERFIELDS\"\>If you create a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>, enter the data field of the parent form responsible for the synchronization between parent and subform.\</ahelp\> To enter multiple values, press Shift + Enter after each input line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568	71			0	lt	The subform is based on an \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#sql\" name=\"SQL\"\>SQL\</link\> query; more specifically, on a \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Parameter Query\"\>Parameter Query\</link\>. If a field name is entered in the \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\> box, the data contained in that field in the main form is read to a variable that you must enter in \<emph\>Link slave fields\</emph\>. In an appropriate SQL statement, this variable is compared to the table data that the subform refers to. Alternatively, you can enter the column name in the \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156089	72			0	lt	Consider the following example:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017	30			0	lt	The database table on which the form is based is, for example, a customer database ("Customer"), where every customer has been given a unique number in a data field named "Cust_ID". A customer's orders are maintained in another database table. You now want to see each customer's orders after entering them into the form. In order to do this you should create a subform. Under \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\> enter the data field from the customer database which clearly identifies the customer, that is, Cust_ID. Under \<emph\>Link slave fields\</emph\> enter the name of a variable which is to accept the data of the field Cust_ID, for example, x.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248	73			0	lt	The subform should show the appropriate data from the orders table ("Orders") for each customer ID (Customer_ID -> x). This is only possible if each order is uniquely assigned to one customer in the orders table. Alternatively, you can use another field called Customer_ID; however, to make sure that this field is not confused with the same field from the main form, the field is called Customer_Number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153537	74			0	lt	Now compare the Customer_Number in the "Orders" table with the Customer_ID from the "Customers" table, which can be done, for example, using the x variable with the following SQL statement:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	75			0	lt	SELECT * FROM Orders WHERE Customer_Number =: x (if you want the subform to show all data from the orders table)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3163727	76			0	lt	or:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153921	77			0	lt	SELECT Item FROM Orders WHERE Customer_Number =: x (if you want the subform from the orders table to show only the data contained in the "Item" field)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488	78			0	lt	The SQL statement can either be entered in the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> field, or you can create an appropriate parameter query, which can be used to create the subform.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150648	4			0	lt	Link slave fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149923	15			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SLAVEFIELDS\"\>If you create a subform, enter the variable where possible values from the parent form field can be stored.\</ahelp\> If a subform is based on a query, enter the variable that you defined in the query. If you create a form using an SQL statement entered in the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> field, enter the variable you used in the statement. You can choose any variable name. If you want to enter multiple values, press Shift + Enter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	31			0	lt	If, for example, you specified the Customer_ID database field as a parent field under \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\>, then you can define under \<emph\>Link slave fields\</emph\> the name of the variable in which the values of the Customer_ID database field are to be stored. If you now specify an SQL statement in the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> box using this variable, the relevant values are displayed in the subform.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152778	32			0	lt	What is a subform?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155579	33			0	lt	Forms are created based on a database table or database query. They display the data in a visually pleasant fashion and can be used to enter data or edit data.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147094	34			0	lt	\<variable id=\"wozu\"\>If you require a form that can refer to the data in a table or query and can additionally display data from another table, you should create a subform. \</variable\> For example, this subform can be a text box that displays the data of another database table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157972	35			0	lt	A subform is an additional component of the main form. The main form can be called the "parent form" or "master". Subforms are needed as soon as you want to access more than one table from a form. Each additional table requires its own subform.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id4807275				0	lt	After creating a form, it can be changed into a subform. To do this, enter Design Mode, and open the Form Navigator. In the Form Navigator, drag a form (that will become a subform) onto any other form (that will become a master).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444	36			0	lt	The user of your document will not see that a form has subforms. The user only sees a document in which data is entered or where existing data is displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C2A				0	lt	Specify the Link master field from the data fields in the master form. In the subform, the Link slave field can be set as a field which will be matched to the contents of the Link master field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C2D				0	lt	When the user navigates through the data, the form always displays the current data record. If there are subforms defined, the contents of the subforms will be displayed after a short delay of approximate 200 ms. This delay enables you to quickly browse through the data records of the master form. If you navigate to the next master data record within the delay limit, the subform data need not be retrieved and displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Tab Order				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146959	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170300.xhp\" name=\"Tab Order\"\>Tab Order\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150347	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"text\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:TabDialog\"\>In the\<emph\> Tab Order \</emph\>dialog you can modify the order in which control fields get the focus when the user presses the tab key.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3109850	3			0	lt	If form elements are inserted into a document, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> automatically determines in which order to move from one control to the next when using the Tab key. Every new control added is automatically placed at the end of this series. In the \<emph\>Tab Order\</emph\> dialog, you can adapt the order of this series to your individual needs.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934	12			0	lt	You can also define the index of a control through its specific properties by entering the desired value under \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"Order\"\>\<emph\>Order\</emph\>\</link\> in the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog of the control.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760	13			0	lt	A radio button inside a group can only be accessed by the Tab key when one of the radio buttons is set to "selected". If you have designed a group of radio buttons where no button is set to "selected", then the user will not be able to access the group or any of the radio buttons by keyboard.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149140	4			0	lt	Controls				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150789	5			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_TABORDER_CONTROLS\"\>Lists all controls in the form. These controls can be selected with the tab key in the given order from top to bottom.\</ahelp\> Select a control from the \<emph\>Controls \</emph\>list to assign the desired position in the tab order.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153750	6			0	lt	Move Up				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751	7			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_TAB_ORDER_PB_MOVE_UP\"\>Click the\<emph\> Move Up\</emph\> button to shift the selected control one position higher in the tab order.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155339	8			0	lt	Move Down				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	9			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_TAB_ORDER_PB_MOVE_DOWN\"\>Click the\<emph\> Move Down\</emph\> button to shift the selected control one position lower in the tab order.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154288	10			0	lt	Automatic Sort				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	11			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_TAB_ORDER_PB_AUTO_ORDER\"\>Click the\<emph\> Automatic Sort\</emph\> button to automatically sort the controls according to their position in the document.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Add Field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144436	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170400.xhp\" name=\"Add Field\"\>Add Field\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"text\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AddField\"\>Opens a window where you can select a database field to add to the form or report.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114	3			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FIELD_SEL\"\>The field selection window lists all database fields of the table or query that was specified as the data source in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\>.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147620	4			0	lt	You can insert a field into the current document by dragging and dropping. A field is then inserted which contains a link to the database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541	5			0	lt	If you add fields to a form and you switch off the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"Design Mode\"\>Design Mode\</link\>, you can see that $[officename] adds a labeled input field for every inserted database field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Design Mode On/Off				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"Design Mode On/Off\"\>Design Mode On/Off\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040	2			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SwitchControlDesignMode\"\>Toggles the Design mode on or off. This function is used to switch quickly between \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Design\"\>Design\</link\> and User mode. Activate to edit the form controls, deactivate to use the form controls.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153528	5			0	lt	Please note the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171000.xhp\" name=\"Open in Design Mode\"\>\<emph\>Open in Design Mode\</emph\>\</link\> function. If \<emph\>Open in Design Mode\</emph\> is activated, the document is always opened in Design mode, regardless of the state in which it is saved.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	3			0	lt	If your form is linked to a database and you turn off the Design mode, the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Bar\"\>Form Bar\</link\> is displayed at the lower margin of the document window. You can edit the link to the database in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Form Navigator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143284				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>controls;arranging in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Form Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subforms; creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; hidden\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hidden controls in Form Navigator\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143284	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760	2			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowFmExplorer\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> displays all forms and subforms of the current document with their respective controls.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399	21			0	lt	When using several forms, the Form Navigator gives an overview of all forms, and also provides various functions for editing them.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552	3			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FORM_NAVIGATOR\"\>The \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> contains a list of all created (logical) forms with the corresponding control fields.\</ahelp\> You can see whether a form contains control fields by the plus sign displayed before the entry. Click the plus sign to open the list of the form elements.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957	4			0	lt	You can change how the different controls are arranged by dragging and dropping them in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>. Select one or more controls and drag them into another form. Alternatively use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+X or the context menu command \<emph\>Cut\</emph\> to move a control to the clipboard and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V or the command \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> to insert the control into another position.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892	22			0	lt	To edit the name in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>, click on the name and enter a new name, or use the command in the context menu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156347	5			0	lt	If you select a control in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>, the corresponding element is selected in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153662	6			0	lt	If you call the context menu of a selected entry, the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> offers the following functions:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153252	7			0	lt	New				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	8			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_NEW\"\>Adds new elements to the form. The\<emph\> Add \</emph\>function can only be called if a form is selected in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149763	9			0	lt	Form				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156117	10			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_NEW_FORM\"\>Creates a new form in the document. \</ahelp\> To create a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>, add the new form under the desired parent form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155342	11			0	lt	Hidden Control				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430	12			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_NEW_HIDDEN\"\>Creates a hidden control in the selected form that is not displayed on the screen. A hidden control serves to include data that is transmitted together with the form.\</ahelp\> It contains additional information or clarifying text that you can specify when creating the form through the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"Special Properties\"\>Special Properties\</link\> of the control. Select the entry of the hidden control in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> and select the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147	19			0	lt	You can copy controls in the document through the clipboard (shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C for copying and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V for inserting). You can copy hidden controls in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> by using drag-and-drop while keeping the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key pressed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068	20			0	lt	Drag and drop to copy controls within the same document or between documents. Open another form document and drag the hidden control from the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> into the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> of the target document. Click a visible control directly in the document, rest the mouse for a moment so that a copy of the control is added to the drag-and-drop clipboard, then drag the copy into the other document. If you want a copy in the same document, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>while dragging.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152812	13			0	lt	Delete				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938	14			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETE\"\>Deletes the selected entry.\</ahelp\> This allows you to delete individual form components as well as whole forms with one mouse click.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153799	15			0	lt	Tab order				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156282	16			0	lt	When a form is selected, it opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170300.xhp\" name=\"Tab Order\"\>\<emph\>Tab Order\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, where the indices for focusing the control elements on the Tab key are defined.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150869	23			0	lt	Rename				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145607	24			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_RENAME_OBJECT\"\>Renames the selected object.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153194	17			0	lt	Properties				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149766	18			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowPropertyBrowser\"\>Starts the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog for the selected entry.\</ahelp\> If a form is selected, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170200.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\> dialog opens. If a control is selected, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170100.xhp\" name=\"Control Properties\"\>Control Properties\</link\> dialog opens.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	HTML Filters and Forms				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163829				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>forms; HTML filters\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163829	1			0	lt	HTML Filters and Forms				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147285	2			0	lt	You can use all control elements and form events in HTML documents. There have been numerous events to date (for example, focus events), which have not been changed. They will continue to be imported and exported as ONFOCUS, ONBLUR, and so on for JavaScript and as SDONFOCUS, SDONBLUR, and so on for $[officename] Basic.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3150616	3			0	lt	Generic names that consist of the Listener interface and the method name of the event are used for all other events: An event registered as XListener::method is exported as				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571	4			0	lt	SDEvent-XListener-method = "/* event-code */"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425	5			0	lt	Note that the XListener- and method components of this option are case sensitive.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3153683	6			0	lt	Event handling of controls is performed using the $[officename] API. If you assign an event to a control, an object registers itself internally as a "Listener" for a specific control event. To do this, the object must use a specific interface, for example the XFocusListener Interface, so that it can react to focus events. When the event occurs, the control then invokes a special method of the Listener interface when the control receives the focus. The internally registered object then invokes the JavaScript or $[officename] Basic code, which was assigned to the event.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	7			0	lt	The HTML filter now uses precisely these listener interfaces and method names so that it can import and export events as desired. You can register a focus event through				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3150506	8			0	lt	<INPUT TYPE=text ONFOCUS="/* code */"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154289	9			0	lt	rather than through the				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391	10			0	lt	<INPUT TYPE=text SDEvent-XFocusListener-focusGained="/* code */"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996	11			0	lt	register. Events can therefore be registered as desired, including those not offered in the list boxes. To define the script language of events, you can write the following line in the document header:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443	12			0	lt	<META HTTP-EQUIV="content-script-type" CONTENT="...">				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	13			0	lt	As CONTENT you can, for example, use "text/x-StarBasic" for $[officename] Basic or a "text/JavaScript" for JavaScript. If no entry is made, JavaScript is assumed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797	14			0	lt	During exporting, the default script language will be defined based on the first module found in macro management. For events, only one language can be used per document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170800.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Table Element Wizard				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150620	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170800.xhp\" name=\"Table Element Wizard\"\>Table Element Wizard\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170800.xhp	0	help	par_id3155354	2			0	lt	If you insert a table control in a document, the \<emph\>Table Element Wizard\</emph\> starts automatically. In this wizard, you can interactively specify which information is displayed in the table control.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170800.xhp	0	help	par_id3154422	13			0	lt	You can use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171100.xhp\" name=\"Wizards On/Off\"\>\<emph\>Wizards On/Off\</emph\>\</link\> icon to keep the wizard from starting automatically.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170801.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Table Element / List Box / Combo Box Wizard: Data				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170801.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153323	3			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170801.xhp\" name=\"Table Element / List Box / Combo Box Wizard: Data\"\>Table Element / List Box / Combo Box Wizard: Data\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170801.xhp	0	help	par_id3150476	4			0	lt	Select the data source and table to which the form field corresponds. If you insert the form field in a document that is already linked to a data source, this page becomes invisible.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170801.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153894	5			0	lt	Data source				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170801.xhp	0	help	par_id3153114	6			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_LISTBOX_RID_PAGE_TABLESELECTION_LB_DATASOURCE\"\>Specifies the data source that contains the desired table.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170801.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346	7			0	lt	Table				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170801.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774	8			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_LISTBOX_RID_PAGE_TABLESELECTION_LB_TABLE\"\>Specifies the desired table.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170802.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Table Element Wizard: Field Selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170802.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155934	13			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170802.xhp\" name=\"Table Element Wizard: Field Selection\"\>Table Element Wizard: Field Selection\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170802.xhp	0	help	par_id3150476	10			0	lt	Specifies which fields in the table control field should be displayed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170802.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346	11			0	lt	Selected Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170802.xhp	0	help	par_id3155941	12			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_LISTBOX_RID_PAGE_GW_FIELDSELECTION_LB_SELECTED_FIELDS\"\>Displays the data fields that are accepted into the form field.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Combo Box/List Box Wizard				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159233				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>forms; Combo Box/List Box Wizard\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154094	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box/List Box Wizard\"\>Combo Box/List Box Wizard\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363	2			0	lt	If you insert a combo box or a list box in a document, a wizard starts automatically. This wizard allows you to interactively specify which information is shown.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3145211	21			0	lt	You can use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171100.xhp\" name=\"Wizards On/Off\"\>\<emph\>Wizards On/Off\</emph\>\</link\> icon to keep the wizard from starting automatically.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391	22			0	lt	The wizards for combo boxes and list boxes differ from each other in their final step. This is because the nature of control fields:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233	23			0	lt	\<emph\>List Boxes\</emph\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	24			0	lt	In the case of a list box, the user selects one entry from a list of entries. These entries are saved in a database table and cannot be modified through the list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	25			0	lt	As a general rule, the database table that contains the visible list entries in the form is not the table on which the form is based. The list boxes in a form work by using references; that is, references to the visible list entries are located in the form table (values table) and are also entered as such in the values table if the user selects an entry from the list and saves it. Through reference values, list boxes can display data from a table linked to the current form table. Thus the \<emph\>List Box Wizard\</emph\> allows two tables of a database to be linked, so that the control field can display a detailed list of a database field that is located in a different table from the one to which the form refers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673	31			0	lt	In the other tables the required field is searched for by using the field names (ControlSource) and then the fields will be completed accordingly. If the field name is not found, the list will remain empty. When list fields contain linked columns, the first column of the other table will be used without a query being shown first.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860	26			0	lt	If an article table contains, for example, the number of a supplier, the list box can use the "Supplier number" link to display the name of the supplier from the supplier table. On the \<emph\>Field links\</emph\> page the Wizard will ask you about all the settings required for this link.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3150977	27			0	lt	\<emph\>Combo Boxes\</emph\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430	28			0	lt	In the case of combo boxes, users can select one entry from the list entries or enter text themselves. The entries, which are offered as a list from which users can select, may originate from any database table. The entries that users select or enter so that they can be saved can be saved either in the form only, or in a database. If they are saved in a database, they will be written to the database table on which the form is based.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046	29			0	lt	Combo boxes can display the data of any table. A direct link between the current form table and the table whose values are to be displayed in the combo box (list table) is not required. Combo boxes do not work with references. If the user enters or selects a value and saves it, the value actually displayed will be entered in the form table. As there is no link between the form table and the list table, the \<emph\>Field Link\</emph\> table does not appear here.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949	30			0	lt	In the case of a list box, you select entries from the list, and these are saved in the list table. In the case of a combo box, you can add additional text that can be written to the current database table of the form (values table) and stored there as desired. For this function, the \<emph\>Combo Box Wizard\</emph\> has the \<emph\>Data Processing\</emph\> page as the last page, whereas in the case of list boxes this page does not exist. Here you can enter whether and where text that has been entered is to be saved in the values table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Combo Box / List Box Wizard: Table Selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228	4			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170901.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box / List Box Wizard: Table Selection\"\>Combo Box / List Box Wizard: Table Selection\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3149716	5			0	lt	Specifies a table from the available database tables that contains the data field whose content should be displayed as a list entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3153114	8			0	lt	For list boxes, a table that can be linked with the current form table is indicated. The link table must have at least one field in common with the table of the current form. This makes it possible to establish an unambiguous reference.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555	9			0	lt	For combo boxes, there must be a relationship between the form table and the table containing the data to be displayed in the combo box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147226	6			0	lt	Table				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338	7			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_LISTBOX_RID_PAGE_LCW_CONTENTSELECTION_TABLE_LB_SELECTTABLE\"\>In the\<emph\> Table \</emph\>field, select the table containing the data field whose content should be displayed in the control field.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233	10			0	lt	The table given here appears in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control properties\"\>Control properties\</link\> as an element of an SQL statement in the \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Combo/List Box Wizard: Field Selection				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153323	14			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170902.xhp\" name=\"Combo/List Box Wizard: Field Selection\"\>Combo/List Box Wizard: Field Selection\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	par_id3154228	9			0	lt	Select the data field specified in the table on the previous page, whose contents should be displayed in the list or combo box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153894	10			0	lt	Available Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	par_id3093440	11			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_LISTBOX_RID_PAGE_LCW_CONTENTSELECTION_FIELD_LB_SELECTFIELD\"\>Displays all table fields chosen on the previous Wizard page.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145669	12			0	lt	Display Field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136	13			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_EDIT_RID_PAGE_LCW_CONTENTSELECTION_FIELD_ET_DISPLAYEDFIELD\"\>Specifies the field whose data are to be shown in the combo or list boxes.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	19			0	lt	The field name given here appears in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control properties\"\>Control properties\</link\> as an element of an SQL statement in the \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	List Box Wizard: Field Link				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149119	20			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170903.xhp\" name=\"List Box Wizard: Field Link\"\>List Box Wizard: Field Link\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3159224	15			0	lt	Indicates through which fields tables of values and list tables are linked.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3150499	27			0	lt	The value table is the table of the current form where the list field is inserted. The list table is the table whose data is to be shown in the list field. Both tables must be linked over a mutual data field. These links are to be entered on this page of the wizard. The field names must not necessarily be the same (this depends upon how the field names are defined in both tables), but both fields must have the same field type.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180	16			0	lt	Value table field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3150789	17			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_COMBOBOX_RID_PAGE_LCW_FIELDLINK_CMB_VALUELISTFIELD\"\>Specifies the current form data field which should be related to a field in the linked table.\</ahelp\> In addition, click the desired data field in the list field below.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3145669	25			0	lt	In \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control - Properties\"\>Control - Properties\</link\>, the specified field will appear as an entry in the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149827	18			0	lt	List table field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391	19			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_COMBOBOX_RID_PAGE_LCW_FIELDLINK_CMB_TABLEFIELD\"\>Specifies the linked table data field, which is related to the specified value table field.\</ahelp\> In addition, click the data field in the lower list field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	26			0	lt	In \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control - Properties\"\>Control - Properties\</link\>, the specified field will appear in the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page of a SQL statement under \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Combo Box Wizard: Database Field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144740	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170904.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box Wizard: Database Field\"\>Combo Box Wizard: Database Field\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3153323	2			0	lt	With the combination fields, you can either save the value of a field in a database or display this value in a form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3155150	12			0	lt	The user values entered in the combination field or selected in the list can be saved in the database table that is accessed in the form. Note that the saving of values in another table is not possible. If the values are not to be saved in a database, they will be saved only in the form. This is especially helpful in HTML forms, where the user's entered or selected values are to be assigned to a server.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149760	3			0	lt	Do you want to save the value in a database field?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3150178	4			0	lt	Two options are available for this question:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394	5			0	lt	Yes, I want to save it in the following database field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3147043	6			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_RADIOBUTTON_RID_PAGE_OPTION_DBFIELD_RB_STOREINFIELD_YES\"\>Specifies whether the user's entered or selected combination field value should be saved in a database field.\</ahelp\> Several database table fields are offered which can be accessed in the current form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3145212	11			0	lt	In \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control - Properties\"\>Control - Properties\</link\> the selected field appears as an entry in the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149177	7			0	lt	List field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	8			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_LISTBOX_RID_PAGE_OPTION_DBFIELD_LB_STOREINFIELD\"\>Specifies the data field where the combination field value should be saved.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538	9			0	lt	No, I only want to save the value in the form				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170904.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398	10			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_RADIOBUTTON_RID_PAGE_OPTION_DBFIELD_RB_STOREINFIELD_NO\"\>Specifies that the value of this combination field will not be written in the database and will only be saved in the form.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Open in Design Mode				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156211				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>forms; opening in design mode\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; activating in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>design mode after saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; opening in design mode\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>edit mode; after opening\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156211	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171000.xhp\" name=\"Open in Design Mode\"\>Open in Design Mode\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146130	2			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OpenReadOnly\"\>Opens forms in \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Design Mode\"\>Design Mode\</link\> so that the form can be edited.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805	5			0	lt	You cannot activate the controls of the form or edit contents of database records in Design Mode. However, you can change the position and size of the controls, edit other properties, and add or delete controls in Design Mode.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147089	3			0	lt	After you have finished editing your form, right-click "Forms" in the \<emph\>Form Navigator\</emph\> and deselect \<emph\>Open in Design Mode\</emph\>. Save your form when you are finished.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749	4			0	lt	If the form document is write-protected, the \<emph\>Open in Design Mode\</emph\> command is ignored.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Wizards On/Off				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155934	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171100.xhp\" name=\"Wizards On/Off\"\>Wizards On/Off\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147143	2			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:UseWizards\"\>Specifies whether to start the wizard automatically when inserting a new control.\</ahelp\> This setting applies globally to all documents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01171100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201	4			0	lt	There are wizards for inserting a list box or combo box, a table element and group boxes.				20130618 17:22:18
