helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147588	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/09010000.xhp\" name=\"URL Name\"\>URL Name\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150476	2			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFA_HYPERLINK_NAME\"\>Assigns a name to an Internet URL or file.\</ahelp\> You can also enter search criteria for an Internet search site.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539	3			0	lt	Possible search syntax is as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154673	6			0	lt	"Suite+Office"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148548	7			0	lt	Finds all pages that contain the words "Suite" AND "Office" at any position.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805	8			0	lt	"Suite,Office"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	9			0	lt	Finds all pages that contain "Suite" OR "Office".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	10			0	lt	Suite Office				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153346	11			0	lt	Finds all pages that contain the specified text. Search text without quotation marks will be sent directly to the specified search engine in the Internet. In most cases, a search engine combines a string of words with "OR," and finds pages in which at least one of the words appear.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669	12			0	lt	Not all Internet \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#suchmaschine\" name=\"search engines\"\>search engines\</link\> support all logical combinations. It is recommended to use only one of the three options for linking search terms.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Internet URLs				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154094	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/09020000.xhp\" name=\"Internet URLs\"\>Internet URLs\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873	2			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFA_HYPERLINK_URL\"\>Allows you to either type a URL, or insert a URL from a document using drag-and-drop.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153894	5			0	lt	You can edit the URL and insert it at the current cursor position in the active document with the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> icon. The \<emph\>Link\</emph\> icon can only be activated if the \<emph\>URL Name\</emph\> field contains text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Hyperlink				20130618 17:22:18
