helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154926	1			0	lt	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12050000.xhp\" name=\"Refresh\"\>Refresh\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156183	2			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Refresh\"\>Refreshes the displayed data.\</ahelp\> In a multi-user environment, refreshing the data ensures that it remains current.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147261				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3153910\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_reload.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153910\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	3			0	lt	Refresh				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	4			0	lt	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Refresh \</emph\>icon to open a submenu with the following commands:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426	5			0	lt	\<emph\>Refresh\</emph\> - Displays the refreshed contents of the database table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	6			0	lt	\<emph\>Rebuild\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\"HID_BROWSER_REFRESH_REBUILDVIEW\"\>Rebuilds the view of the database table. Use this command when you have changed the structure of the table.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Insert Database Columns				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147000	1			0	lt	Insert Database Columns				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284	2			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SbaBrwInsert\"\>\<variable id=\"datenintext\"\>Inserts all fields of the marked record into the current document at the cursor position.\</variable\>\</ahelp\> The icon is only visible if the current document is a text document or a spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154186				0	lt	\<image id=\"img_id3147291\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbabrwinsert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147291\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	3			0	lt	Data to Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153577	4			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>In the data source browser, select the record that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon. The record is inserted in the document at the cursor position, with the contents of each individual field of the record copied to a table column. You can also select multiple records and transfer them into the document by clicking the \<emph\>Data to Text \</emph\>icon. Each individual record is then written to a new row.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	5			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In the data source browser, select the records that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon, or drag-and-drop data from the data source browser into the document. This opens the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog. Select whether the data should be inserted as a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070100.xhp\" name=\"table\"\>table\</link\>, as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070200.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> or as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070300.xhp\" name=\"text\"\>text\</link\>.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031	6			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The preferences you set in the\<emph\> Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog are saved and will be active the next time the dialog is called. This save process is independent of the database and can record the preferences for a maximum of 5 databases.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326	7			0	lt	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If data is inserted into the document as a table, the table properties are not saved along with the data in the document. If you select the \<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\> function for formatting the table, $[officename] will note the name of the format template. This template will then be used automatically if you insert data as a table again, unless the preferences have been changed.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Table				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151299	1			0	lt	Table				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156183				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>database contents; inserting as tables\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156183	18			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_AS_TABLE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts data selected from the data source browser into the document as a table.\</ahelp\>In the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> option to insert the selected data into the document as a table. In the dialog, you can decide which database fields or columns are transferred, and how the text table is formatted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152594	2			0	lt	Table				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152918	19			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> area, use the arrow keys to select the columns of the database table that you want to apply to the text table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156042	3			0	lt	Database columns				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425	20			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:LB_TBL_DB_COLUMN\"\>Specifies the database columns to be inserted into the text table.\</ahelp\> All database table columns that have not been accepted in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box are listed here. The entries are sorted alphabetically. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147577	4			0	lt	Table column(s)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	21			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:LB_TABLE_COL\"\>Lists all database columns to be inserted into the document.\</ahelp\> A column will be assigned to each corresponding entry in the table. The entry order in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box determines the data order in the text table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146958	5			0	lt	>>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149750	22			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_ALL_TO\"\>Moves all listed database fields into the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box.\</ahelp\> All fields listed in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box are inserted into the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163802	6			0	lt	>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153662	23			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_ONE_TO\"\>Moves the selected database field into the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box. \</ahelp\> You can also double click an entry to move it to the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box. All fields listed in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box are inserted into the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149732	7			0	lt	<				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685	24			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_ONE_FROM\"\>Removes the selected database field from the\<emph\> Table column(s)\</emph\> list box\</ahelp\> The removed field is not inserted into the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771	8			0	lt	<<				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897	25			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_ALL_FROM\"\>Removes all database fields from the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399	13			0	lt	Format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154380	30			0	lt	Specifies the format for inserting the database fields into the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329	14			0	lt	From database				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415	31			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_DBFMT_FROM_DB\"\>Accepts the database formats.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159148	15			0	lt	Select				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349	32			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:LB_DBFMT_FROM_USR\"\>Specifies a format from the list, if the format information of certain data fields is not accepted.\</ahelp\> The formats supplied here are only available for certain database fields, such as numeric or Boolean fields. If you select a database field in text format, you will not be able to select any format from the selection list, since the text format will be automatically maintained.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3144511	33			0	lt	If the format you want is not listed, select "Other Formats..." and define the desired format in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Number Format\"\>\<emph\>Number Format\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154282	34			0	lt	The number format assigned using the selection list always refers to the database field selected in the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138	35			0	lt	To insert the data into the document in the form of a table, the correct \<emph\>Table\</emph\> option must be active. You can then select a database field from the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box to define the formatting of the database field. The changes to the number formats will be applied to the last selection. It does not matter whether the database field was selected from the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box or from the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280	10			0	lt	Insert table heading				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150497	27			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:CB_TABLE_HEADON\"\>Specifies whether to insert a heading line for the columns in the text table.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153178	11			0	lt	Apply column name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152922	28			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_HEADL_COLNMS\"\>Uses the field names of the database table as headings for each of the text table columns.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158407	12			0	lt	Create row only				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194	29			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_HEADL_EMPTY\"\>Inserts an empty heading line into the text table.\</ahelp\> Using the\<emph\> Create row only \</emph\>option, you can define headings in the document, which do not correspond to the database field names.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153369	16			0	lt	Properties				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154299	36			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:PB_TBL_FORMAT\"\>Opens the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05090000.xhp\" name=\"Table Format\"\>\<emph\>Table Format\</emph\>\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Table Format\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> dialog, which enables you to define the table properties such as borders, background, and column width.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153728	17			0	lt	AutoFormat				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154988	37			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:PB_TBL_AUTOFMT\"\>Opens the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05150101.xhp\" name=\"AutoFormat\"\>\<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\>\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> dialog, in which you can select format styles that are immediately applied when inserting the table.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149991	1			0	lt	Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149987				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>database contents; inserting as fields\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149987	8			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_RADIOBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_RB_AS_FIELD\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts data selected from the data source browser into the document as fields.\</ahelp\>In the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialog, select the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\> to insert the selected data into the document as fields. These \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090006.xhp\" name=\"database fields\"\>database fields\</link\> work as wildcards for the individual database columns and can be used for form letters. Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Data to Fields\"\>\<emph\>Data to Fields\</emph\>\</link\> icon to match the contents of the fields to the currently selected record.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153114	9			0	lt	If several records are selected when you choose the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> function, the mail merge fields will be inserted according to the number of records. Also, a field command such as "Next record" will be inserted automatically between individual field command blocks.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	10			0	lt	The \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialog lets you define which database fields to insert into the document and how to format the paragraphs.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136	2			0	lt	Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571	11			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> area, use the arrow button to select the database table columns into which you want to insert field contents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345	3			0	lt	Database columns				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535	12			0	lt	Lists all columns of the database table, which can be accepted in the selection list box to insert them into the document. \<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_LB_TXT_DB_COLUMN\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Select the database columns that you want to insert it in the document.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152551	4			0	lt	>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	13			0	lt	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_TOEDIT\"\>Moves the fields that you selected in the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box into the selection field.\</ahelp\> You can also double-click the entry to select it.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166411	5			0	lt	Select				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802	14			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_MULTILINEEDIT_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_ED_DB_TEXT\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Lists the database columns that you selected to be inserted into the document. You can also enter text here. This text will be also inserted into the document.\</ahelp\> The entries' order in the selection field corresponds to the data order in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153257	7			0	lt	Paragraph Style				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430	15			0	lt	By default, the inserted paragraphs are formatted with the current Paragraph Styles. This format corresponds to the "none" entry in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> list box. \<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_LB_DB_PARA_COLL\" visibility=\"visible\"\>This is where you can select other Paragraph Styles to apply to the paragraph you want to insert into the document.\</ahelp\> The list box displays the available Paragraph Styles defined in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> and managed in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Style Catalog\"\>Style Catalog\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154873	1			0	lt	Text				20130618 17:22:18
