helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3163829	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"sortierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OrderCrit\"\>Specifies the sort criteria for the data display.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149549	12			0	lt	While the functions \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12010000.xhp\" name=\"Sort in Ascending Order\"\>\<emph\>Sort in Ascending Order\</emph\>\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12020000.xhp\" name=\"Sort in Descending Order\"\>\<emph\>Sort in Descending Order\</emph\>\</link\> sort by one criterion only, you can combine several criteria in the\<emph\> Sort Order \</emph\>dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136	13			0	lt	You can remove a sorting that has been performed with the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sorting\"\>\<emph\>Remove Filter/Sorting\</emph\>\</link\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148548	4			0	lt	Sorting				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155941	5			0	lt	Use this area to enter sorting criteria. If you enter additional sorting criteria under \<emph\>and then\</emph\>, the data matching the content of the higher-order criterion is ordered according to the next criterion.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148620	14			0	lt	If you sort the field name "First name" in ascending order and the field name "last name" in descending order, all records will be sorted in ascending order by first name, and then within the first names, in descending order by last name.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345	6			0	lt	Field name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233	7			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OrderCrit\"\>Specifies the data field name whose content will determine the sort order.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774	8			0	lt	Order				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177	9			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:OrderCrit\"\>Specifies the sort order (either ascending or descending).\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275	10			0	lt	and then				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460	11			0	lt	Specifies additional subordinate sort criteria from the other fields.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	lt	Find Record				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146936				0	lt	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases; searching\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>forms; browsing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>records; searching in databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>searching; databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>databases; searching records\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146936	1			0	lt	\<variable id=\"datensatzsuche\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100200.xhp\" name=\"Find Record\"\>Find Record\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147588	2			0	lt	\<variable id=\"suchentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RecSearch\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Searches database tables and forms.\</ahelp\>In forms or database tables, you can search through data fields, list boxes, and check boxes for specific values. \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355	3			0	lt	When searching a table, the data fields of the current table are searched. When searching in a form, the data fields of the table linked with the form are searched.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394	111			0	lt	The search described here is carried out by \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>. If you want to use the SQL server to search in a database, then you should use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12110000.xhp\" name=\"Form-based Filters\"\>Form-based Filters\</link\> icon on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Bar\"\>Form Bar\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095	110			0	lt	The search function is also available for table controls. When calling the search function from a table control, you can search each column of the table control corresponding to the database columns of the linked database table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267	112			0	lt	Search for				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	113			0	lt	Specifies the type of search.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153683	6			0	lt	Text:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	7			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORTEXT\"\>Enter the search term in the box or select it from the list.\</ahelp\> The text under the cursor is already copied into the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> combo box. Note that while running a search in a form, tabs and line breaks cannot be processed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539	8			0	lt	Your search terms will be saved as long as the table or the formula document is open. If you are running more than one search and you would like to repeat the search term, you can select a previously used search term from the combo box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662	114			0	lt	Field content is NULL				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153543	115			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORNULL\"\>Specifies that fields will be found that contain no data.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153717	116			0	lt	Field content is not NULL				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270	117			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORNOTNULL\"\>Specifies that fields will be found that contain data.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156153	9			0	lt	Where to search				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164	10			0	lt	Specifies the fields for the search.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154564	105			0	lt	Form				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176	106			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_LB_FORM\"\>Specifies the logical form in which you want the search to take place.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155434	107			0	lt	The\<emph\> Form \</emph\>combo box is only visible if the current document is a form document with more than one logical form. It does not appear during a search in tables or queries.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384	108			0	lt	Form documents may contain multiple logical forms. These are individual form components, which are each linked to a table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086	109			0	lt	The \<emph\>Form\</emph\> combo box contains the names of all logical forms for which controls exist.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159414	11			0	lt	All Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896	12			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_ALLFIELDS\"\>Searches through all fields.\</ahelp\> If you are running a search in a table, all fields in the table will be searched. If you are running a search in a form, all fields of the logical form (entered under \<emph\>Form\</emph\>) will be searched. If you are running a search in a table control field, all columns that are linked to a valid database table field will be searched.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054	13			0	lt	Note that the fields of the current logical form do not have to be identical to the fields of the form document. If the form document contains fields that point to multiple data sources (that is, multiple logical forms), the \<emph\>All Fields\</emph\> option will only search for the fields linked to data sources in the form document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150865	15			0	lt	Single field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360	16			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SINGLEFIELD\"\>Searches through a specified data field.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154365	17			0	lt	Settings				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158408	18			0	lt	Defines settings to control the search.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149809	19			0	lt	Position				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673	20			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_POSITION\"\>Specifies the relationship of the search term and the field contents.\</ahelp\> The following options are available:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280	21			0	lt	anywhere in the field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145744	22			0	lt	Returns all fields containing the search pattern anywhere in the field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451	23			0	lt	beginning of field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429	24			0	lt	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the beginning of the field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131	74			0	lt	end of field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	75			0	lt	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the end of the field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317	25			0	lt	entire field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154127	26			0	lt	Returns all fields containing the search pattern as an exact match to the contents of the field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886	27			0	lt	If the \<emph\>Wildcard expression\</emph\> check box is marked, this function is not available.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664	28			0	lt	Apply field format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	29			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_FORMATTER\"\>Specifies that all field formats are considered when searching in the current document.\</ahelp\> Field formats are all visible formats that are created using the following possibilities:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103	78			0	lt	in table design mode for field properties,				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488	79			0	lt	in data source view on column formatting,				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152941	80			0	lt	in forms on control properties.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156736	81			0	lt	If the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> box is marked, the data source view of the table or form is searched using the formatting set there. If the box is not marked, the database is searched using the formatting saved in the database.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151280	82			0	lt	Example:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959	83			0	lt	You have a date field, which is saved in "DD.MM.YY" format in the database (for example, 17.02.65). The format of the entry is changed in the data source view to "DD MMM YYYY" (17 Feb 1965). Following this example, a record containing February 17 is only found when the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> option is on:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150593	84			0	lt	Apply field format				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145253	85			0	lt	Search pattern				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3083279	86			0	lt	on				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155850	87			0	lt	"Feb" is returned, but not "2".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148590	88			0	lt	off				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418	89			0	lt	"2" is returned, but not "Feb".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151321	90			0	lt	It is recommended that you always search using field formatting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401	91			0	lt	The following examples show possible issues when searching without field formatting. These issues depend on the database used and only occur for certain internal default formatting:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971	92			0	lt	Search results				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154273	93			0	lt	Cause				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153836	94			0	lt	"5" returns "14:00:00" as a time				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156332	95			0	lt	Time fields are not defined for dBASE databases and must be simulated. To internally display the time "14:00:00", a 5 is necessary.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3157965	96			0	lt	"00:00:00" returns all records of a standard date field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146081	97			0	lt	The database stores a date value internally using a combined date/time field.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	98			0	lt	"45.79" does not return "45.79" although the \<emph\>entire field\</emph\> option is selected under \<emph\>Position\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155518	99			0	lt	The view shown does not match what is stored internally. For example, if value 45.789 is stored in the database as a field of type Number/Double and the shown formatting is set to display only two decimals, "45.79" is only returned in searches with field formatting.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148481	100			0	lt	In this case, standard formatting is formatting that refers to the internally stored data. It is not always visible to the user, especially if it is used for simulating data types (for example, time fields in dBASE databases). This depends on the database used and the individual data type. Searching with field formatting is appropriate if you only want to find what is actually shown. This includes fields of type Date, Time, Date/Time and Number/Double.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507	31			0	lt	However, searching without \<emph\>Apply field format \</emph\>is appropriate for larger databases with no formatting issues, because it is faster.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153355	118			0	lt	If you are searching the values of check boxes, and \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> is on, then you will receive a "1" for marked check boxes, a "0" for unmarked check boxes, and an empty string for undefined (tristate) check boxes. If the search has been carried out with \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> set to off, you will see the language-dependent default values "TRUE" or "FALSE".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150995	119			0	lt	If you use \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> when searching in list boxes, you find the text displayed in list boxes. If you do not use \<emph\>Apply field format,\</emph\> you will find the contents corresponding to the standard field format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150387	32			0	lt	Match case				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267	33			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_CASE\"\>Specifies that upper and lower case are taken into consideration during the search.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145297	34			0	lt	Search backwards				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151249	35			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BACKWARD\"\>Specifies that the search process will run in reverse direction, from the last to the first record.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152484	36			0	lt	From top / From bottom				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316	37			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_STARTOVER\"\>Restarts the search. A forward search restarts with the first record. A backwards search restarts with the last record.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163724	38			0	lt	Wildcard expression				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255	64			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_WILDCARD\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Allows a search with a * or ? wildcard.\</ahelp\> You can use the following wildcards:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146317	39			0	lt	Wildcards				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150298	40			0	lt	Meaning				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919	41			0	lt	Example				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158411	42			0	lt	?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148874	43			0	lt	for exactly one arbitrary character				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365	44			0	lt	"?loppy" returns "Floppy"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426	65			0	lt	"M?ller" returns, for example, Miller and Moller				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148803	45			0	lt	*				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156138	46			0	lt	for 0 or more arbitrary characters				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135	47			0	lt	"*-*" returns "ZIP-Drive" and "CD-ROM"				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582	66			0	lt	"M*er" returns all entries starting with an "M" and ending in "er" (for example, Miller, Moller, Mather)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145762	48			0	lt	If you want to search for the actual characters ? or *, preface them with a backslash: "\\?" or "\\*". However, this is only necessary when \<emph\>Wildcard expression\</emph\> is enabled. When the option is not enabled, the wildcard characters are processed like normal characters.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147130	49			0	lt	Regular expression				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982	50			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_REGULAR\"\>Searches with regular expressions.\</ahelp\> The same regular expressions that are supported here are also supported in the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\" name=\"Find & Replace dialog\"\>Find & Replace dialog\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154718	67			0	lt	Searching with regular expressions offers more options than searching with wildcard expressions. If you search with regular expressions, the following characters correspond to those used in searches with wildcards:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153705	68			0	lt	Search with wildcard expression				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209	69			0	lt	Search with regular expressions				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151045	70			0	lt	?				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150384	71			0	lt	.				20130618 17:22:18
