helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155262	4			0	lt	Default				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155434	5			0	lt	The view of the graphic object is not changed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574	6			0	lt	Grayscale				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153760	7			0	lt	The graphic object is shown in grayscale. A color graphic object can become monochrome in grayscale. You can also use the color sliders to apply a uniform color to the monochrome graphic object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151246	8			0	lt	Black and White				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062	9			0	lt	The graphic object is shown in black and white. All brightness values below 50% will appear black, all over 50% will appear white.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146795	10			0	lt	Watermark				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670	11			0	lt	The graphic object is raised in brightness and reduced in contrast so that it can be used in the background as a watermark. 				20130618 17:22:18
