helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151054	65			0	lt	New Dictionary				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360	66			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Dictionary\</emph\> section you can name a new user-defined dictionary or dictionary of exceptions and specify the language.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398	67			0	lt	Name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192	68			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:ED_DICTNAME\"\>Specifies the name of the new custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> The file extension "*.DIC" is automatically appended.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767	69			0	lt	Language				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3148920	70			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:LB_DICTLANG\"\>By selecting a certain language you can limit the use of the custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> By selecting \<emph\>All\</emph\> the custom dictionary is used independently of the current language.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153106	71			0	lt	Exceptions (-)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149561	72			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:CHECKBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:BTN_EXCEPT\"\>Specifies whether you wish to avoid certain words in your documents.\</ahelp\> In this way, you can create a custom dictionary of all the words to be avoided. If this exception dictionary is activated, during spellchecking you receive a corresponding note about any words which should be avoided.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785	73			0	lt	Edit				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576	74			0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_DICS_EDIT_DIC\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary\</emph\> dialog, in which you can add to your custom dictionary or edit existing entries.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436	75			0	lt	In the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary \</emph\>dialog you have the option to enter new terms or edit existing entries. If you edit an exception dictionary, the dialog has the added facility of defining an exception for a word. During the spellcheck this exception is then listed as a suggestion.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	76			0	lt	When a dictionary is edited, a check is made on the status of the file. If the file is write-protected, it cannot be changed. The buttons \<emph\>New\</emph\> and \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> are then deactivated. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150116	77			0	lt	Book				20130618 17:22:18
