helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10545				0	lt	Java Start Parameters				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10549				0	lt	You can use this dialog to enter optional start parameters for the Java runtime environment (JRE). The settings that you specify in this dialog are valid for any JRE that you start.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10568				0	lt	Java Start parameter				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056C				0	lt	\<ahelp hid=\"svx:Edit:RID_SVXDLG_JAVA_PARAMETER:ED_PARAMETER\"\>Enter a start parameter for a JRE as you would on a command line. Click Assign to add the parameter to the list of available start parameters.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_id5404522				0	lt	Do not use escape characters or quotes in path names.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D8				0	lt	For example, to point the system property "myprop" to a folder, enter the following parameter:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN105DD				0	lt	-Dmyprop=c:\\program files\\java				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057B				0	lt	To enable debugging in a JRE, enter the following parameters:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057E				0	lt	-Xdebug				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\javaparameters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10581				0	lt	-Xrunjdwp:transport=dt_socket,server=y,address=8000				20130618 17:22:18
